<usx version="3.1">
  <book code="PSA" style="id">EN_ULT en_English_ltr Mon Oct 09 2023 16:39:14 GMT-0500 (Central Daylight Time) tc</book>
  <para style="ide">UTF-8
</para>
  <para style="h">Psalms
</para>
  <para style="toc1">The Book of Psalms
</para>
  <para style="toc2">Psalms
</para>
  <para style="toc3">Psa
</para>
  <para style="mt1">Psalms
</para>
  <para style="cl">Psalm

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PSA 1"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book One
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 1:1"/>The happinesses of the man who walks not in the advice of the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and stands not in the pathway of sinners,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and sits not in the seat of scoffers,
<verse eid="PSA 1:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 1:2"/>but in the instruction of Yahweh {is} his delight,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in his instruction he meditates day and night.
<verse eid="PSA 1:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 1:3"/>And he is like a tree set to grow by streams of water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">which gives its fruit in its season,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and its leaf does not wither,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he makes successful all that he does.

<verse eid="PSA 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 1:4"/>Not so the wicked!
</para>
  <para style="q2">But {they are} like the chaff that wind chases away.
<verse eid="PSA 1:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 1:5"/>Thus the wicked will not stand in the judgment,
</para>
  <para style="q2">nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous.

<verse eid="PSA 1:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 1:6"/>For Yahweh knows the way of the righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the way of the wicked will perish.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 1:6"/><verse eid="PSA 1:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="PSA 2"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 2:1"/>Why do nations conspire
</para>
  <para style="q2">and peoples plot futilely?
<verse eid="PSA 2:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 2:2"/>The kings of the earth take their stand,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the rulers conspire together
</para>
  <para style="q2">against Yahweh and against his anointed.
<verse eid="PSA 2:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 2:3"/>“Let us tear apart their bonds
</para>
  <para style="q2">and cast their cords away from us.”

<verse eid="PSA 2:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 2:4"/>He who is sitting in the heavens laughs;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Lord mocks them.
<verse eid="PSA 2:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 2:5"/>Then he will speak to them in his anger
</para>
  <para style="q2">and terrify them in his fury,
<verse eid="PSA 2:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 2:6"/>“I, I have poured out my king
</para>
  <para style="q2">on Zion, the mountain of my holiness.”

<verse eid="PSA 2:6"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 2:7"/>I will describe a decree of Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He said to me, “You are my son!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Today I have begotten you.
<verse eid="PSA 2:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 2:8"/>Ask from me, and I will give nations {as} your inheritance
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the extremities of the earth {as} your possession.
<verse eid="PSA 2:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 2:9"/>You will break them with an iron rod;
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a jar of a potter, you will smash them to pieces.”

<verse eid="PSA 2:9"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 2:10"/>And now kings, act prudently;
</para>
  <para style="q2">be admonished, rulers of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 2:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 2:11"/>Serve Yahweh with fear
</para>
  <para style="q2">and rejoice with trembling.
<verse eid="PSA 2:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 2:12"/>Kiss the son, lest he be angry
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you perish in the way,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his anger burns for just a moment.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The happinesses of all the seekers of refuge in him.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 2:12"/><verse eid="PSA 2:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="PSA 3"/>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David, when he fled from the face of Absalom his son

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 3:1"/>Yahweh, how many my oppressors have become!
</para>
  <para style="q2">The risers against me are many.
<verse eid="PSA 3:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 3:2"/>{There are} many sayers about me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“There is no salvation for him in God.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 3:2"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 3:3"/>But you, Yahweh, are a shield round about me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my glory, and the lifter up of my head.
<verse eid="PSA 3:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 3:4"/>{With} my voice I call to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he answered me from the hill of his holiness.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 3:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 3:5"/>I laid myself down and slept. I awoke,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for Yahweh protects me.
<verse eid="PSA 3:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 3:6"/>I will not fear the multitudes of people
</para>
  <para style="q2">who stand against me round about.

<verse eid="PSA 3:6"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 3:7"/>Rise up, Yahweh! Save me, my God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">For you hit all my enemies on the cheek;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the teeth of the wicked you break.
<verse eid="PSA 3:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 3:8"/>Salvation {is} of Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Your blessing {is} on your people.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 3:8"/><verse eid="PSA 3:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="PSA 4"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; with stringed instruments; a psalm of David.

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 4:1"/>Answer me when I call, God of my righteousness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in distress you relieve me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Be gracious {to} me and hear my prayer.

<verse eid="PSA 4:1"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 4:2"/>Son of man, until when {will} my glory become shame?
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Until when} will you love futility, {until when} will you seek falsehood?
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 4:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 4:3"/>But know that Yahweh has set apart the faithful for himself.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh hears when I call to him.
<verse eid="PSA 4:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 4:4"/>Tremble and do not sin!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Meditate in your heart on your bed and be silent.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 4:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 4:5"/>Sacrifice sacrifices of righteousness
</para>
  <para style="q2">and trust in Yahweh.

<verse eid="PSA 4:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 4:6"/>Many say, “Who will show us good?”
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lift up the light of your face on us, Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 4:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 4:7"/>You have put joy in my heart
</para>
  <para style="q2">more than the time {when} their grain and their new wine abound.
<verse eid="PSA 4:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 4:8"/>In peace I will both lie down and sleep,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you alone, Yahweh, cause me to dwell securely.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 4:8"/><verse eid="PSA 4:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="PSA 5"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on the flutes; a psalm of David

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 5:1"/>{To} my words give ear, Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Understand my murmuring!
<verse eid="PSA 5:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 5:2"/>Listen attentively to the sound of my cry for help,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my king and my God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for to you I pray!

<verse eid="PSA 5:2"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 5:3"/>Yahweh, in the morning you hear my voice.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the morning I prepare for you and watch.
<verse eid="PSA 5:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 5:4"/>For you are not a god pleased with wickedness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">evil ones will not sojourn with you.
<verse eid="PSA 5:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 5:5"/>The arrogant will not stand in front of your eyes;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you hate all doers of iniquity.
<verse eid="PSA 5:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 5:6"/>You will destroy speakers of falsehood;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the man of blood and deceit Yahweh abhors.
<verse eid="PSA 5:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 5:7"/>But I, in the greatness of your covenant faithfulness, I will come into your house;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will bow down toward your temple of holiness in fear.

<verse eid="PSA 5:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 5:8"/>Yahweh, guide me in your righteousness because of my watchers;
</para>
  <para style="q2">straighten before my face your path.
<verse eid="PSA 5:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 5:9"/>For there is no firmness in his mouth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their inward being is destruction.
</para>
  <para style="q2">An open tomb is their throat;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their tongue they make smooth.
<verse eid="PSA 5:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 5:10"/>Make them guilty, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they fall due to their schemes!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Because of their many transgressions, drive them out,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for they rebel against you!
<verse eid="PSA 5:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 5:11"/>But may all refuge seekers in you rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they shout joyfully to eternity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may you cover over them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may lovers of your name exult in you.

<verse eid="PSA 5:11"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 5:12"/>For you, Yahweh, you bless the righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you surround him {with} favor as a shield.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 5:12"/><verse eid="PSA 5:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="PSA 6"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; with stringed instruments; on Sheminith; a psalm of David.

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 6:1"/>Yahweh, rebuke me not in your nose,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in your rage discipline me not.
<verse eid="PSA 6:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 6:2"/>Be gracious {to} me, Yahweh, for I am frail!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Heal me, Yahweh, for my bones are shaking!
<verse eid="PSA 6:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 6:3"/>And my soul is very disturbed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">And you, Yahweh, until when?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 6:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 6:4"/>Turn back, Yahweh! Rescue my soul!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Save me for the sake of your covenant faithfulness!
<verse eid="PSA 6:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 6:5"/>For in death, there is no remembrance of you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In Sheol, who will thank you?

<verse eid="PSA 6:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 6:6"/>I am weary with my groaning.
</para>
  <para style="q2">During every night, I cause my bed to swim,
</para>
  <para style="q2">With my tears, my couch I melt.
<verse eid="PSA 6:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 6:7"/>My eye has wasted away from grief,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it advances because of all my adversaries.

<verse eid="PSA 6:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 6:8"/>Turn away from me, all you doers of iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for Yahweh has heard the sound of my sobbing!
<verse eid="PSA 6:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 6:9"/>Yahweh has heard my appeal for mercy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh accepts my prayer.
<verse eid="PSA 6:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 6:10"/>Let all my enemies be shamed and greatly disturbed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let them turn back. Let them be shamed {in} an instant.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 6:10"/><verse eid="PSA 6:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="PSA 7"/>
  <para style="d">A musical composition of David, which he sang to Yahweh concerning the words of Cush the Benjamite.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 7:1"/>Yahweh my God, in you I have taken refuge;
</para>
  <para style="q2">save me from all my pursuers, and rescue me!
<verse eid="PSA 7:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 7:2"/>Lest he rip my life apart like a lion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">tearing apart, and there is no one to rescue.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 7:3"/>Yahweh my God, if I have done this,
</para>
  <para style="q2">if there is wrong on my hands,
<verse eid="PSA 7:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 7:4"/>if I have repaid evil {to} one {who was at} peace with me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or senselessly rescued my adversary,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 7:5"/>let my enemy pursue my soul and overtake {it},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let him trample my life to the ground
</para>
  <para style="q2">and cause my honor to live in the dust.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 7:6"/>Arise, Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">In your nose, be lifted with the rage of my adversaries!
</para>
  <para style="q2">And wake up for me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have ordered judgment.
<verse eid="PSA 7:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 7:7"/>And an assembly of peoples surround you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and over it return on high!
<verse eid="PSA 7:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 7:8"/>Yahweh, adjudicate the peoples!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Judge me, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">according to my righteousness and according to my integrity, Most High!
<verse eid="PSA 7:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 7:9"/>May the evil of the wicked end, and {would} you establish the righteous.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The righteous God examines hearts and kidneys.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 7:10"/>My shield is with God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the savior of the upright of heart.
<verse eid="PSA 7:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 7:11"/>God is a righteous judge,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a God {who is} indignant on every day.
<verse eid="PSA 7:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 7:12"/>If he does not repent, his sword he will sharpen,
</para>
  <para style="q2">his bow he has bent and prepared.
<verse eid="PSA 7:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 7:13"/>And for him he has prepared implements of death;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has made his arrows into burning {arrows}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 7:14"/>Behold he is pregnant with wickedness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he conceives trouble,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he births lies.
<verse eid="PSA 7:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 7:15"/>He digs a pit and hollows it out
</para>
  <para style="q2">and falls into the hole he has made.
<verse eid="PSA 7:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 7:16"/>His trouble returns on his head,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his violence comes down on the top of his head.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 7:17"/>I will thank Yahweh according to his righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and sing praise to the name of Yahweh, the Most High.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 7:17"/><verse eid="PSA 7:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="PSA 8"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on Gittith. A psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 8:1"/>Yahweh, our Lord, how magnificent is your name in all the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{you} whose splendor is bestowed on the heavens.
<verse eid="PSA 8:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 8:2"/>Out of the mouth of children and nursing ones you have established strength
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of your adversaries,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to cause the enemy and avenger to end.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 8:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 8:3"/>When I look at your heavens, the work of your fingers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the moon and the stars, which you have set in place,
<verse eid="PSA 8:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 8:4"/>what is mankind that you remember him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or the son of man that you pay attention to him?
<verse eid="PSA 8:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 8:5"/>Yet you have made him to lack little from the heavenly beings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {with} glory and majesty you have crowned him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 8:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 8:6"/>You made him rule over the works of your hands,
</para>
  <para style="q2">everything you have put under his feet:
<verse eid="PSA 8:6"/></para>
  <para style="q3"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 8:7"/>sheep and oxen—all of them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and also the animals of the field,
<verse eid="PSA 8:7"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 8:8"/>birds of the sky, and the fish of the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q3">the passers {on} the paths of the seas.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 8:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 8:9"/>Yahweh, our Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">how magnificent is your name in all the earth!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 8:9"/><verse eid="PSA 8:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="PSA 9"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on “The Death of the Son.” A psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 9:1"/>I will thank Yahweh with all my heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will recount all your wonders.
<verse eid="PSA 9:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 9:2"/>I will rejoice and exult in you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing praise to your name, Most High!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 9:3"/>When my enemies turn back,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they stumble and perish from your face.
<verse eid="PSA 9:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 9:4"/>For you have done my justice and my claim;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have sat on your throne, a judge of righteousness!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 9:5"/>You rebuked nations; you destroyed the wicked;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you blotted out their name forever and ever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 9:6"/>The enemy are finished—desolation forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you pulled up cities.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{As for} them, their remembrance perished,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 9:7"/>but Yahweh will sit forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He has established his throne for justice,
<verse eid="PSA 9:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 9:8"/>as for him, he will judge the world with righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will adjudicate for the peoples with fairness.
<verse eid="PSA 9:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 9:9"/>And may Yahweh be a secure height for the oppressed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a secure height for times with distress.
<verse eid="PSA 9:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 9:10"/>And may the knowers of your name trust in you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you have not abandoned the seekers of you, Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 9:11"/>Sing praises to Yahweh, the sitter {in} Zion!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Declare his deeds among the peoples
<verse eid="PSA 9:11"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 9:12"/>for the seeker of {vengeance for} bloodshed remembered them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does not forget the cry of the poor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 9:13"/>Have mercy on me, Yahweh! See my affliction from my haters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">O lifter of me from the gates of death,
<verse eid="PSA 9:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 9:14"/>in order that I might recount all your praise
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the gates of the daughter of Zion.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will rejoice in your salvation!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 9:15"/>The nations have sunk down into the pit they made;
</para>
  <para style="q3">their foot is caught in the net that they hid.
<verse eid="PSA 9:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 9:16"/>Yahweh has revealed himself, he has done justice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the wicked is ensnared by the work of his hands.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Higgaion Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 9:17"/>The wicked will turn back to Sheol;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all nations are forgetful of God.
<verse eid="PSA 9:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 9:18"/>But the needy will not be forgotten eternally,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{nor} will the hope of the afflicted perish forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 9:19"/>Arise, Yahweh! Let not humanity prevail!
</para>
  <para style="q2">On your face let nations be judged.
<verse eid="PSA 9:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 9:20"/>Put terror to them, Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">May nations know they are human.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 9:20"/><verse eid="PSA 9:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="PSA 10"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 10:1"/>Why, Yahweh, do you stand far-off?
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Why} do you hide in times of trouble?
<verse eid="PSA 10:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 10:2"/>In arrogance, the wicked hotly pursue the afflicted;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they be caught by the schemes that they have planned.
<verse eid="PSA 10:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 10:3"/>Indeed, the wicked boasts about the desires of his soul
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he blesses the robber; he despises Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 10:4"/>According to the haughtiness of his nose the wicked seeks not;
</para>
  <para style="q2">All his thoughts {are}, “{There is} no God.”
<verse eid="PSA 10:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 10:5"/>His ways endure at every time;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your judgments are high from in front of him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{as for} all his enemies, he snorts at them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 10:6"/>He says in his heart, “I will not be shaken;
</para>
  <para style="q2">to generation and generation {it is I} who {will} not {be} in distress.”
<verse eid="PSA 10:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 10:7"/>His mouth is full of curses and lies and oppression;
</para>
  <para style="q2">under his tongue are mischief and evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 10:8"/>He sits in ambush near the villages; in the secret places he murders the innocent;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his eyes stealthily watch for a helpless person.
<verse eid="PSA 10:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 10:9"/>He ambushes in a secret place like a lion in cover;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he ambushes to seize the afflicted.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He seizes the afflicted by pulling in his net.
<verse eid="PSA 10:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 10:10"/>He stoops, crouches,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and unfortunate people fall by his power.
<verse eid="PSA 10:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 10:11"/>He says in his heart, “God has forgotten;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has hidden his face; to perpetuity he sees not.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 10:12"/>Arise, Yahweh! God, lift up your hand!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not forget the afflicted ones.
<verse eid="PSA 10:12"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 10:13"/>Why does the wicked despise God?
</para>
  <para style="q2">He says in his heart, “You will not seek.”
<verse eid="PSA 10:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 10:14"/>You have seen! Indeed, you notice mischief and vexation to take {it} in your hand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The helpless person entrusts {himself} to you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">as for the orphan you, {even} you, are {his} helper.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 10:15"/>Break the arm of the wicked and the evil.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May it seek his wickedness, {but} not find {it}.
<verse eid="PSA 10:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 10:16"/>Yahweh is king forever and ever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the nations have perished from his land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 10:17"/>The desire of afflicted ones, you have heard, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you strengthen their heart, you cause your ear to attend:
<verse eid="PSA 10:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 10:18"/>to judge the orphan and oppressed;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{that} mankind {who is} from the earth will never again terrify.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 10:18"/><verse eid="PSA 10:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="PSA 11"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 11:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">To the chief musician; of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">In Yahweh I take refuge.
</para>
  <para style="q1">How can you say to my soul,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Flutter {like} a bird to your mountain.
<verse eid="PSA 11:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 11:2"/>For behold, the wicked, they bend a bow;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they have set their arrow on the string
</para>
  <para style="q1">to shoot in the darkness at the upright of heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 11:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 11:3"/>If the foundations are destroyed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">what can the righteous do”?
<verse eid="PSA 11:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 11:4"/>Yahweh {is} in his holy temple;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh {is} in the heavens, his throne.
</para>
  <para style="q1">His eyes see, his eyelids test the sons of man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 11:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 11:5"/>Yahweh tests the righteous and the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the one loving violence his soul hates.
<verse eid="PSA 11:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 11:6"/>May he rain snares upon the wicked;
</para>
  <para style="q1">fire and brimstone and a scorching wind the portion of their cup!
<verse eid="PSA 11:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 11:7"/>For Yahweh is righteous, he loves righteousness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the upright will see his face.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 11:7"/><verse eid="PSA 11:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="PSA 12"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on Sheminith; a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 12:1"/>Help, Yahweh, for the faithful have come to an end;
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the faithful have vanished from {among} the sons of man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 12:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 12:2"/>Man, they speak falsehood with his neighbor;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they speak {with} lip of smoothness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">with a heart and a heart.
<verse eid="PSA 12:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 12:3"/>May Yahweh cut off all lips of smoothness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the tongue speaking great things,
<verse eid="PSA 12:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 12:4"/>which say, “With our tongue we will make strong.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Our lips {are} with us, who {is} master over us?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 12:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 12:5"/>“Because of oppression of the poor, because of {the} groaning of the needy,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Now I will arise,” says Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q1">“I will place in {the} safety he pants for it.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 12:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 12:6"/>{The} words of Yahweh {are} pure words,
</para>
  <para style="q1">silver refined in a furnace on the ground,
</para>
  <para style="q1">purified seven.
<verse eid="PSA 12:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 12:7"/>You Yahweh, you will keep them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You will protect him from this generation for eternity.
<verse eid="PSA 12:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 12:8"/>The wicked walk about on every side
</para>
  <para style="q1">when vileness is high among the sons of man.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 12:8"/><verse eid="PSA 12:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="PSA 13"/>
  <para style="d">To the chief musician; a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 13:1"/>How long, Yahweh? Will you forget me forever?
</para>
  <para style="q1">How long will you hide your face from me?
<verse eid="PSA 13:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 13:2"/>How long must I take counsel in my soul,
</para>
  <para style="q1">sorrow in my heart by day?
</para>
  <para style="q1">How long will the one being hostile to me be high over me?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 13:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 13:3"/>Consider {and} answer me, Yahweh my God;
</para>
  <para style="q1">give light to my eyes, lest I sleep the {sleep of} death,
<verse eid="PSA 13:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 13:4"/>Lest the one being hostile to me say, “I have prevailed over him,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">{and} my adversaries rejoice when I am shaken.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 13:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 13:5"/>But I have trusted in your covenant faithfulness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let my heart rejoice in your salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 13:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 13:6"/>I will sing to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because he has dealt bountifully with me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 13:6"/><verse eid="PSA 13:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 13"/>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="PSA 14"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 14:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">The fool says in his heart, “No God.”
</para>
  <para style="q2">They are corrupt, they do a deed abominably.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{There is} none doing good.
<verse eid="PSA 14:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 14:2"/>Yahweh looks down from the heavens on the sons of man
</para>
  <para style="q2">to see whether there is one understanding, one seeking God.
<verse eid="PSA 14:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 14:3"/>The whole has turned aside. Together they have corrupted themselves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{There is} none doing good, not even one.
<verse eid="PSA 14:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 14:4"/>Do they not know, all of the doers of iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones eating my people {as} they eat bread?
</para>
  <para style="q2">They do not call {upon} Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 14:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 14:5"/>There they feared a fear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for God {is} with the generation of the righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 14:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 14:6"/>You shame the counsel of the afflicted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh {is} his refuge.
<verse eid="PSA 14:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 14:7"/>Who will give the salvation of Israel from Zion?
</para>
  <para style="q2">When Yahweh restores the prosperity of his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Jacob will be glad, Israel will rejoice.


<verse eid="PSA 14:7"/><verse eid="PSA 14:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 14"/>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="PSA 15"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 15:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, who may sojourn in your tent?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Who may dwell on your holy mountain?
<verse eid="PSA 15:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 15:2"/>The one walking blamelessly,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and doing righteousness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and speaking truth in his heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 15:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 15:3"/>He does not slander with his tongue,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he does not do evil to his neighbor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and an insult he does not raise up against one close to him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 15:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 15:4"/>In whose eyes one being rejected is despised,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but those who fear Yahweh he honors.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He swears to his own hurt, and does not change.
<verse eid="PSA 15:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 15:5"/>He does not put out his money at interest,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a bribe against the innocent he does not take.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The one doing these {things} will not be shaken for eternity.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 15:5"/><verse eid="PSA 15:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 15"/>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="PSA 16"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 16:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A miktam of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Protect me, God, for I take refuge in you.
<verse eid="PSA 16:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 16:2"/>You said to Yahweh, “You are my Lord; my good is not beyond you.”
<verse eid="PSA 16:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 16:3"/>As for the holy {ones} who are on the earth, they are the majestic {ones}; all my delight is in them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 16:4"/>Their sorrows will be multiplied, they {who} hasten {after} another {god}. I will not pour out their drink offerings from blood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will not take up their names on my lips.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 16:5"/>Yahweh, the portion of my inheritance and my cup. You are holding my lot.
<verse eid="PSA 16:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 16:6"/>{The} measuring cords have fallen for me in pleasant {places}; indeed, {the} inheritance is beautiful for me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 16:7"/>I will bless Yahweh, who has given me counsel; even {in the} night my kidneys instruct me.
<verse eid="PSA 16:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 16:8"/>I have set Yahweh continually before me, because he is at my right hand, I will not be shaken.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 16:9"/>Therefore my heart is glad, and my glory rejoices. Also, my flesh will dwell in security.
<verse eid="PSA 16:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 16:10"/>For you will not abandon my soul to Sheol. You will not hand over your faithful one to see the pit.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 16:11"/>You make known to me the path of life; abundance of joys are before your face; in your right hand are delights forever!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 16:11"/><verse eid="PSA 16:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 16"/>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="PSA 17"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 17:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A prayer of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Listen, Yahweh {to} righteousness. Pay attention to my cry!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Give ear to my prayer from lips without deceit.
<verse eid="PSA 17:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 17:2"/>Let my vindication come from your face; let your eyes see rightly!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 17:3"/>You have examined my heart, you have visited {me in the} night,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have tested me {and} have detected nothing. I have purposed that my mouth will not transgress.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 17:4"/>With regard to the actions of man, by the word of your lips I have kept myself away from the paths of the violent.
<verse eid="PSA 17:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 17:5"/>My steps hold firmly to your tracks; my footsteps have not slipped.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 17:6"/>I have called upon you, for you will answer me, God; Incline your ear to me; listen to my speech.
<verse eid="PSA 17:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 17:7"/>Set apart your covenant faithfulness, you, the one saving by your right hand the ones seeking refuge {in you} from those rising up!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 17:8"/>Keep me as the pupil of your eye; hide me under the shadow of your wings,
<verse eid="PSA 17:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 17:9"/>from the faces of the wicked who deal violently with me, the ones being hostile against my soul, they surround me.
<verse eid="PSA 17:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 17:10"/>Their fat they have closed up; with their mouths they speak with pride.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 17:11"/>They have surrounded me now {in} our steps. Their eyes they have set, crouching down to the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 17:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 17:12"/>His likeness is as a lion, he longs to tear; and as a young lion he is dwelling in hiding places.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 17:13"/>Arise, Yahweh, confront his face, make him bow down! Rescue my soul from the wicked {with} your sword!
<verse eid="PSA 17:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 17:14"/>From men {with} your hand Yahweh, from men from {the} world, their portion in life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with your treasure you fill their belly. They are satisfied with sons, and they leave their abundance to their children.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 17:15"/>I, in righteousness, will see your face; when I awake, I will be satisfied {with} your manifestation.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 17:15"/><verse eid="PSA 17:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 17"/>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="PSA 18"/>
  <para style="d">To the chief musician. Of David, {the} servant of Yahweh, who spoke to Yahweh the words of this song on the day that Yahweh delivered him from the palm of all his enemies and from the hand of Saul.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 18:1"/>And he said, “I love you, Yahweh, my strength.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 18:2"/>Yahweh is my rock and my stronghold and my deliverer; my God, my rock; I take refuge in him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my shield and the horn of my salvation, my high tower.
<verse eid="PSA 18:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 18:3"/>{To} the one being praised I call, {to} Yahweh, and I am saved from my enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 18:4"/>The cords of death encompassed me, and the torrents of wickedness terrified me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 18:5"/>The cords of Sheol surrounded me; the snares of death confronted me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 18:6"/>In my distress, I called {to} Yahweh, and to my God I cried out for help. He heard my voice from his temple,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my cry to his face went in his ears.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 18:7"/>Then the earth shook and trembled, and the foundations of the mountains quaked
</para>
  <para style="q1">and shook themselves because it burned to him.
<verse eid="PSA 18:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 18:8"/>Smoke went up from his nose, and fire from his mouth devoured. Coals from him burned.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 18:9"/>And he lowered the heavens, and he came down, and a dark cloud was under his feet.
<verse eid="PSA 18:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 18:10"/>And he rode on a cherub, and he flew, and he flew swiftly on the wings of the wind.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 18:11"/>He set darkness his covering, the booth around him {was} a darkness of waters, clouds of the skies.
<verse eid="PSA 18:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 18:12"/>From the brightness before him, hailstones and coals of fire broke through his thick clouds.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 18:13"/>And Yahweh thundered in the heavens and the Most High uttered his voice, hailstones and coals of fire.
<note style="f" caller="+"> <char style="ft" closed="false">Some modern versions add after shouted, </char><char style="fqa" closed="true">hailstones and coals of fire</char> this expression may be an accidental repetition from the previous verse.</note>
<verse eid="PSA 18:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 18:14"/>And he sent out his arrows and he scattered them and lightnings in abundance and he panicked them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 18:15"/>And the channels of the sea were seen,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the foundations of the world were uncovered,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from your rebuke, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the blast of the breath of your nose.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 18:16"/>He stretched out from the height, he took hold of me. He drew me out of many waters.
<verse eid="PSA 18:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 18:17"/>He delivered me from my strong enemy, from the ones hating me, for they were stronger than me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 18:18"/>They confronted me on the day of my calamity, but Yahweh was my support!
<verse eid="PSA 18:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 18:19"/>And he brought me out to an open space; he delivered me because he delighted in me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 18:20"/>Yahweh has rewarded me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands he has given back to me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 18:21"/>For I have kept the ways of Yahweh, and I have not been wicked from my God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 18:22"/>For all of his judgments {are} before me, and his statutes, I have not turned away from them.
<verse eid="PSA 18:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 18:23"/>And I have been blameless with him, and I have kept myself from my iniquity.
<verse eid="PSA 18:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 18:24"/>And Yahweh has given back to me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands before his eyes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 18:25"/>With the faithful you show yourself faithful;
</para>
  <para style="q1">with a blameless man, you show yourself blameless.
<verse eid="PSA 18:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 18:26"/>With the purified, you show yourself pure, but with the crooked, you show yourself cunning.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 18:27"/>For you save a lowly people, but the eyes {of} the ones being high, you bring them down.
<verse eid="PSA 18:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 18:28"/>For you light my lamp; Yahweh my God lightens my darkness.
<verse eid="PSA 18:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 18:29"/>For by you I run {after} a troop, and by my God I leap {over} a wall.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 18:30"/>This God, his way {is} perfect. The word of Yahweh is refined.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He {is} a shield to all of the ones taking refuge in him.
<verse eid="PSA 18:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 18:31"/>For who is God except Yahweh? And who is a rock except our God?
<verse eid="PSA 18:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 18:32"/>This God is the one girding me {with} valor, and he makes my way perfect,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 18:33"/>making my feet like a deer, and he makes me stand on my high places,
<verse eid="PSA 18:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 18:34"/>training my hands for war, and my arms bend a bow of bronze.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 18:35"/>And you give to me the shield of your salvation, and your right hand supports me, and your humility makes me great.
<verse eid="PSA 18:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 18:36"/>You enlarge my step under me, and my feet do not slip.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 18:37"/>I pursue my enemies, and I destroy them, and I do not return until I have ended them.
<verse eid="PSA 18:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 18:38"/>I severely wounded them so that they were not able to rise; they fell under my feet.
<verse eid="PSA 18:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 18:39"/>And you gird me {with} valor for war; you make the ones rising up under me bow down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 18:40"/>And my enemies, you give to me the back of {their} neck; the ones hating me, I destroyed them.
<verse eid="PSA 18:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 18:41"/>They called out for help, but there was none saving; to Yahweh, but he did not answer them.
<verse eid="PSA 18:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 18:42"/>And I beat them fine as dust upon the face of the wind; like the mud of the streets I cast them out.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 18:43"/>You rescue me from the disputes of people. You made me as the head of nations. People I did not know serve me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 18:44"/>At the hearing of an ear, they hear me; sons of the foreigner cringe to me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 18:45"/>Sons of the foreigner fade away, and they come trembling from their fortresses.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 18:46"/>Yahweh is alive! And blessed be my rock, and may the God of my salvation be exalted,
<verse eid="PSA 18:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 18:47"/>the God giving vengeance to me, and he subdues peoples under me,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 18:48"/>the one delivering me from my enemies. Also, from the ones arising {against} me you lift me up, from a man of violence, you deliver me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:48"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 18:49"/>Therefore, I thank you among the nations, Yahweh; and I will sing praise to your name,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:49"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 18:50"/>the one magnifying the salvation of his king and doing covenant faithfulness to his anointed, to David, and to his seed until forever.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 18:50"/><verse eid="PSA 18:50"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 18"/>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="PSA 19"/>
  <para style="d">To the chief musician; a psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 19:1"/>The heavens are declaring the glory of God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the sky is proclaiming the work of his hands.
<verse eid="PSA 19:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 19:2"/>Day to day makes flow forth a word,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and night to night declares knowledge.
<verse eid="PSA 19:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 19:3"/>{There} is no speech and {there} are no words, their voice is not being heard.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 19:4"/>Their line has gone out through all of the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their words to the end of the world.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He has set in them a tent for the sun,
<verse eid="PSA 19:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 19:5"/>and that is like a bridegroom coming out from his chamber,
</para>
  <para style="q1">it rejoices like a strong man to run its path.
<verse eid="PSA 19:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 19:6"/>From the end of the heavens is its going forth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and its circuit to the ends of them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and there is nothing hidden from its heat.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 19:7"/>The law of Yahweh is perfect, restoring the soul;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the testimony of Yahweh is sure, making wise the simple.
<verse eid="PSA 19:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 19:8"/>The precepts of Yahweh are right, making the heart rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the commandment of Yahweh is pure, enlightening the eyes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 19:9"/>The fear of Yahweh is clean, enduring forever;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the judgments of Yahweh are true, they are altogether righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 19:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 19:10"/>They are to be desired more than gold, and more than much fine gold,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they are more sweet than honey and nectar of honeycombs.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 19:11"/>Also, by them your servant is warned;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in keeping them there is great reward.
<verse eid="PSA 19:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 19:12"/>Who can discern {his} errors?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Acquit me from hidden {faults}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 19:13"/>Also, keep back your servant from presumptuous ones;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let them not rule over me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then I will be blameless,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will be innocent from great transgression.
<verse eid="PSA 19:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 19:14"/>Let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart
</para>
  <para style="q1">be acceptable to your face,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, my strength and the one redeeming me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 19:14"/><verse eid="PSA 19:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 19"/>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="PSA 20"/>
  <para style="d">To the chief musician; a psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 20:1"/>May Yahweh answer you in the day of trouble;
</para>
  <para style="q1">may the name of the God of Jacob set you on high.
<verse eid="PSA 20:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 20:2"/>May he send you help from the sanctuary
</para>
  <para style="q1">and support you from Zion.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 20:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 20:3"/>May he remember all of your grain offerings
</para>
  <para style="q1">and regard as fat your burnt offering.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 20:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 20:4"/>May he grant you according to your heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and may he fulfill all of your plans.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 20:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 20:5"/>We will shout for joy over your salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in the name of our God we will set up {our} banners.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May Yahweh fulfill all of your petitions.
<verse eid="PSA 20:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 20:6"/>Now I know that Yahweh saves his anointed;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will answer him from his holy heaven
</para>
  <para style="q1">with mighty deeds of salvation of his right hand.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 20:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 20:7"/>These in chariots and these in horses,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but we will remember the name of Yahweh our God.
<verse eid="PSA 20:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 20:8"/>They bow down and fall,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but we rise and stand upright!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 20:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 20:9"/>Save, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">may the king answer us on the day we call.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 20:9"/><verse eid="PSA 20:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 20"/>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="PSA 21"/>
  <para style="d">To the chief musician; a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 21:1"/>Yahweh, in your strength the king rejoices,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in your salvation how greatly he exults!
<verse eid="PSA 21:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 21:2"/>You have given to him the desire of his heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the request of his lips you have not withheld.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 21:3"/>For you meet him with blessings of good;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you place on his head a crown of refined gold.
<verse eid="PSA 21:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 21:4"/>He asked life from you; you gave {it} to him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">length of days, forever and ever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 21:5"/>His glory is great through your salvation;
</para>
  <para style="q1">splendor and majesty you place on him.
<verse eid="PSA 21:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 21:6"/>For you place on him eternal blessings;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you make him glad with joy with your face.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 21:7"/>For the king is trusting in Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and through the covenant faithfulness of the Most High, he will not be shaken.
<verse eid="PSA 21:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 21:8"/>Your hand will find all of your enemies;
</para>
  <para style="q1">your right hand will find the ones hating you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 21:9"/>You will make them as an oven of fire at the time of your face.
</para>
  <para style="q1">In his nose Yahweh will swallow them
</para>
  <para style="q1">and will consume them {with} fire.
<verse eid="PSA 21:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 21:10"/>You will destroy their fruit from the earth
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their seed from {among} the sons of man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 21:11"/>Though they stretch out evil against you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">they plan a plot they will not be able.
<verse eid="PSA 21:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 21:12"/>For you will make them shoulder;
</para>
  <para style="q1">on your strings you will set {your arrows} toward their faces.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 21:13"/>Be exalted, Yahweh, in your strength;
</para>
  <para style="q1">we will sing and we will praise your power.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 21:13"/><verse eid="PSA 21:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 21"/>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="PSA 22"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on “The Doe of the Dawn.” A psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 22:1"/>My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?
</para>
  <para style="q1">{Why are you} far from the salvation of me, {far from} the words of my groaning?
<verse eid="PSA 22:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 22:2"/>My God, I call by day, but you do not answer,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and {in} the night, and there is no silence for me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 22:3"/>Yet you are holy,
</para>
  <para style="q1">sitting {in} the praises of Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 22:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 22:4"/>In you our fathers trusted;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they trusted, and you delivered them.
<verse eid="PSA 22:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 22:5"/>To you they cried and they were rescued.
</para>
  <para style="q1">In you they trusted and they were not ashamed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 22:6"/>But I am a worm and not a man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">a reproach of mankind and despised by the people.
<verse eid="PSA 22:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 22:7"/>All of the ones seeing me mock me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they open wide with the lip. They shake the head,
<verse eid="PSA 22:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 22:8"/>“Roll to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let him deliver him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let him rescue him, since he delights in him.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 22:9"/>Yet you are the one pulling me out from the womb,
</para>
  <para style="q1">making me trust upon the breasts of my mother.
<verse eid="PSA 22:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 22:10"/>Upon you I was cast from the womb;
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the womb of my mother, you {have been} my God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 22:11"/>You {do} not be far away from me, for trouble is near,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for {there is} no one helping {me}.
<verse eid="PSA 22:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 22:12"/>Many bulls surround me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">strong ones of Bashan encircle me.
<verse eid="PSA 22:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 22:13"/>They open their mouths against me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">a tearing and roaring lion.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 22:14"/>I am poured out like water,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all of my bones are dislocated.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My heart is like wax;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it has melted within my inner parts.
<verse eid="PSA 22:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 22:15"/>My strength is dried up like a shard,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my tongue is being made to cling to my gums,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to the dust of death you lay me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 22:16"/>For dogs have surrounded me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a company of ones doing evil have encircled me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">like the lion, my hands and my feet.
<verse eid="PSA 22:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 22:17"/>I can count all of my bones.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They look {and} they stare at me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 22:18"/>They divide my garments among them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they cast lots for my clothing.
<verse eid="PSA 22:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 22:19"/>But you, Yahweh, {do} not be far away.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My strength, hurry to help me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 22:20"/>Deliver my life from the sword,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my only one from the hand of the dog.
<verse eid="PSA 22:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 22:21"/>Save me from the mouth of the lion,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and from the horns of wild oxen, answer me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 22:22"/>I will declare your name to my brothers;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the midst of the assembly I will praise you.
<verse eid="PSA 22:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 22:23"/>You who fear Yahweh, praise him!
</para>
  <para style="q1">All of the seed of Jacob, honor him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and be terrified from him, all of the seed of Israel!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 22:24"/>For he has not despised nor abhorred the affliction of the afflicted,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he has not hidden his face from him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but when he cried to him, he heard.
<verse eid="PSA 22:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 22:25"/>From with you my praise in the great assembly;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will fulfill my vows before those who fear him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 22:26"/>The poor will eat and be satisfied.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The ones seeking Yahweh will praise.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May your heart live forever.
<verse eid="PSA 22:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 22:27"/>All of the ends of the earth will remember and turn to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all of the families of the nations will bow down to your face.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 22:28"/>For to Yahweh the kingdom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he is ruling over the nations.
<verse eid="PSA 22:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 22:29"/>All of the fat of the earth will eat and will bow down;
</para>
  <para style="q1">to his face will kneel all of the ones going down to the dust,
</para>
  <para style="q1">even his self he kept not alive.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 22:30"/>Seed will serve him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it will be told of the Lord to the generation.
<verse eid="PSA 22:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 22:31"/>They will come and will declare his righteousness to a people who will be born,
</para>
  <para style="q1">that he has done {it}!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 22:31"/><verse eid="PSA 22:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 22"/>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="PSA 23"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 23:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh is my shepherd; I will lack nothing.
<verse eid="PSA 23:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 23:2"/>He makes me lie down in green pastures;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he leads me to waters of rest.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 23:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 23:3"/>He restores my soul.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He leads me in right paths for the sake of his name.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 23:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 23:4"/>Even though I walk through {the} valley of deep darkness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will fear no evil, for you are with me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">your rod and your staff, they comfort me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 23:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 23:5"/>You arrange a table before my face in front of my enemies;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have anointed my head with oil;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my cup overflows.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 23:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 23:6"/>Surely goodness and covenant faithfulness will pursue me all the days of my life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will dwell in the house of Yahweh for length of days!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 23:6"/><verse eid="PSA 23:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 23"/>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="PSA 24"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 24:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">To Yahweh {is} the earth and its fullness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the world and the ones dwelling in it.
<verse eid="PSA 24:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 24:2"/>For he has founded it upon the seas
</para>
  <para style="q1">and established it upon the rivers.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 24:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 24:3"/>Who may ascend on the mountain of Yahweh?
</para>
  <para style="q1">And who may stand in his holy place?
<verse eid="PSA 24:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 24:4"/>{The} one clean of hands and pure of heart,
</para>
  <para style="q1">who has not lifted up his soul to what is false,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and has not sworn deceitfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 24:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 24:5"/>He will take up a blessing from Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">and righteousness from the God of his salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 24:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 24:6"/>This {is} the generation of the ones seeking him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones seeking your face, Jacob.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 24:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 24:7"/>Lift up your heads, {you} gates,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and be lifted up, {you} ancient doors,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that the King of Glory may come in.
<verse eid="PSA 24:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 24:8"/>Who {is} this King of Glory?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, strong and mighty; Yahweh, mighty in battle.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 24:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 24:9"/>Lift up your heads, {you} gates,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and lift up, {you} ancient doors,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that the King of Glory may come in.
<verse eid="PSA 24:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 24:10"/>Who {is} he, this King of Glory?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh of Armies,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he {is} the King of Glory.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 24:10"/><verse eid="PSA 24:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 24"/>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" sid="PSA 25"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 25:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">To you, Yahweh, I lift up my soul.
<verse eid="PSA 25:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 25:2"/>My God, in you I trust;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not let me have shame;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not let my enemies exult over me.
<verse eid="PSA 25:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 25:3"/>Indeed, all the ones waiting on you will not have shame;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones acting treacherously without cause will have shame.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 25:4"/>Make me know your ways, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">teach me your paths.
<verse eid="PSA 25:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 25:5"/>Lead me in your truth and teach me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you are the God of my salvation;
</para>
  <para style="q1">on you I wait all the day.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 25:6"/>Remember your compassion, Yahweh, and your covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for they are from ancient times.
<verse eid="PSA 25:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 25:7"/>Do not remember the sins of my youth or my transgressions;
</para>
  <para style="q1">according to your covenant faithfulness remember me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the sake of your goodness, Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 25:8"/>Good and upright is Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">therefore he teaches the sinful in the way.
<verse eid="PSA 25:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 25:9"/>He leads the humble in justice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he teaches the humble his way.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 25:10"/>All the paths of Yahweh are covenant love and faithfulness
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the ones keeping his covenant and his testimonies.
<verse eid="PSA 25:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 25:11"/>For the sake of your name, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">forgive my iniquity, for it is great.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 25:12"/>Who is the man fearing Yahweh?
</para>
  <para style="q1">He will teach him in the way he is to choose.
<verse eid="PSA 25:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 25:13"/>His soul will remain in good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his seed will inherit the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 25:14"/>The secret of Yahweh is for the ones fearing him
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his covenant, to cause them to know it.
<verse eid="PSA 25:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 25:15"/>My eyes are continually toward Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for he will make my feet go out of the net.
<verse eid="PSA 25:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 25:16"/>Turn toward me and be gracious to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I am alone and afflicted.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 25:17"/>The troubles of my heart are enlarged;
</para>
  <para style="q1">bring me out of my distresses.
<verse eid="PSA 25:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 25:18"/>See my affliction and my trouble,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and forgive all of my sins.
<verse eid="PSA 25:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 25:19"/>See my enemies, for they are many,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with hatred of violence they hate me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 25:20"/>Guard my life and deliver me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not let me have shame, for I take refuge in you!
<verse eid="PSA 25:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 25:21"/>May integrity and uprightness preserve me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I wait for you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 25:22"/>God, redeem Israel
</para>
  <para style="q1">from all of his troubles!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 25:22"/><verse eid="PSA 25:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 25"/>
  <chapter number="26" style="c" sid="PSA 26"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 26:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Vindicate me, Yahweh, for I have walked in my integrity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in Yahweh I have trusted without wavering.
<verse eid="PSA 26:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 26:2"/>Examine me, Yahweh, and test me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">try my kidneys and my heart.
<verse eid="PSA 26:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 26:3"/>For your covenant faithfulness is before my eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I walk about in your truth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 26:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 26:4"/>I do not sit with men of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will not go with the ones concealing themselves.
<verse eid="PSA 26:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 26:5"/>I hate the assembly of the ones doing evil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will not sit with the wicked.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 26:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 26:6"/>I wash my hands in innocence,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so I will go around your altar, Yahweh,
<verse eid="PSA 26:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 26:7"/>to cause to be heard the sound of thanksgiving
</para>
  <para style="q1">and recount all of your wonderful acts.
<verse eid="PSA 26:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 26:8"/>Yahweh, I love the habitation of your house,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the place of the dwelling place of your glory.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 26:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 26:9"/>Do not gather my soul with the sinful,
</para>
  <para style="q1">nor my life with men of blood,
<verse eid="PSA 26:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 26:10"/>who {have} in their hands an evil scheme
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their right hand is full of bribes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 26:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 26:11"/>But I will walk in my integrity;
</para>
  <para style="q1">redeem me and be gracious to me.
<verse eid="PSA 26:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 26:12"/>My foot stands on level ground;
</para>
  <para style="q1">among the assemblies will I bless Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 26:12"/><verse eid="PSA 26:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 26"/>
  <chapter number="27" style="c" sid="PSA 27"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 27:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh is my light and my salvation;
</para>
  <para style="q2">whom will I fear?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh is the refuge of my life;
</para>
  <para style="q2">whom will I dread?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 27:2"/>When the ones doing evil advance against me to devour my flesh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my enemies and the ones being hostile to me, they stumbled and fell.
<verse eid="PSA 27:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 27:3"/>Though an army encamps against me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my heart will not fear;
</para>
  <para style="q1">though war arises against me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in this I will be confident.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 27:4"/>One {thing} I have asked from Yahweh, that I will seek:
</para>
  <para style="q1">that I may dwell in the house of Yahweh all the days of my life,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to look upon the beauty of Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to inquire in his temple.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 27:5"/>For in the day of trouble he will hide me in his hut;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will hide me in the hiding-place of his tent.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He will lift me high upon a rock.
<verse eid="PSA 27:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 27:6"/>And now my head will be lifted up above the ones being hostile to me {who are} all around me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will sacrifice in his tent sacrifices of a shout of joy.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will sing and make music to Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 27:7"/>Hear, Yahweh, my voice {when} I cry out,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and be gracious to me, and answer me.
<verse eid="PSA 27:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 27:8"/>“Seek my face.” My heart said to you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Your face, Yahweh, I will seek.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 27:9"/>Do not hide your face from me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not turn your servant away in anger.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have been my help.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not abandon me nor leave me, God of my salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 27:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 27:10"/>For my father and my mother have left me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but Yahweh will care for me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 27:11"/>Teach me your way, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and lead me on a level path
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of my enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 27:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 27:12"/>Do not give me up to the desire of my adversaries,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for false witnesses have risen against me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a witness of violence.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 27:13"/>Unless I had believed that I would look on the goodness of Yahweh in the land of the living.
<verse eid="PSA 27:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 27:14"/>Wait on Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Be strong, and let your heart be courageous,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and wait on Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 27:14"/><verse eid="PSA 27:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 27"/>
  <chapter number="28" style="c" sid="PSA 28"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 28:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">To you, Yahweh, I cry; my rock, do not be deaf to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest you be deaf to me, and I be equal with those going down to the pit.
<verse eid="PSA 28:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 28:2"/>Hear the voice of my pleas when I cry to you for help,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when I lift up my hands toward your inner sanctuary of holiness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 28:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 28:3"/>Do not drag me away with the wicked and with the workers of iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones speaking of peace with their neighbors while evil is in their hearts.
<verse eid="PSA 28:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 28:4"/>Give to them according to their work and according to the evil of their deeds;
</para>
  <para style="q1">give to them according to the work of their hands; return to them their recompense.
<verse eid="PSA 28:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 28:5"/>Because they do not give heed to the works of Yahweh or the action of his hands,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will tear them down and not build them up.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 28:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 28:6"/>Blessed be Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because he has heard the voice of my pleas.
<verse eid="PSA 28:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 28:7"/>Yahweh is my strength and my shield;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in him my heart trusts, and I am helped;
</para>
  <para style="q1">therefore my heart exults,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with my song I will praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 28:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 28:8"/>Yahweh is strength for his people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he is a refuge of help {for} his anointed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 28:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 28:9"/>Save your people and bless your inheritance,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and shepherd them and carry them unto the eternity.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 28:9"/><verse eid="PSA 28:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 28"/>
  <chapter number="29" style="c" sid="PSA 29"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 29:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Ascribe to Yahweh, sons of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">ascribe to Yahweh glory and strength.
<verse eid="PSA 29:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 29:2"/>Ascribe to Yahweh the glory of his name;
</para>
  <para style="q1">bow down to Yahweh in the adornment of holiness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 29:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 29:3"/>The voice of Yahweh over the waters,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the God of glory thunders,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh over many waters.
<verse eid="PSA 29:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 29:4"/>The voice of Yahweh is with power;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the voice of Yahweh is with majesty.
<verse eid="PSA 29:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 29:5"/>The voice of Yahweh is breaking cedars,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Yahweh breaks the cedars of Lebanon.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 29:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 29:6"/>And he makes Lebanon skip like a calf
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Sirion like a son of wild oxen.
<verse eid="PSA 29:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 29:7"/>The voice of Yahweh is hewing out with flames of fire.
<verse eid="PSA 29:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 29:8"/>The voice of Yahweh shakes the wilderness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh shakes the wilderness of Kadesh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 29:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 29:9"/>The voice of Yahweh causes the deer to give birth
</para>
  <para style="q1">and strips the forests bare,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in his temple everyone is saying, “Glory!”
<verse eid="PSA 29:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 29:10"/>Yahweh sits over the flood;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh sits as king forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 29:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 29:11"/>Yahweh will give strength to his people;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh will bless his people with peace.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 29:11"/><verse eid="PSA 29:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 29"/>
  <chapter number="30" style="c" sid="PSA 30"/>
  <para style="d">A psalm a song at the dedication of the house; of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 30:1"/>I will extol you, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you have drawn me up
</para>
  <para style="q1">and have not let the ones being hostile
</para>
  <para style="q1">to me rejoice over me.

<verse eid="PSA 30:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 30:2"/>Yahweh my God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I cried out to you for help,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you healed me.
<verse eid="PSA 30:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 30:3"/>Yahweh, you have brought up my soul from Sheol;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have kept me alive from the ones
</para>
  <para style="q1">going down to the pit.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 30:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 30:4"/>Sing praise to Yahweh, {you} his faithful ones,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness.
<verse eid="PSA 30:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 30:5"/>For his anger is {for} a moment,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{but} his favor is {for} a lifetime.
</para>
  <para style="q1">In the evening weeping may come to lodge
</para>
  <para style="q1">but rejoicing {comes} in the morning.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 30:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 30:6"/>And I, in my ease, said,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“I will never be shaken.”
<verse eid="PSA 30:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 30:7"/>Yahweh, by your favor
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have made my mountain stand strong;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you hid your face, {and} I was dismayed.
<verse eid="PSA 30:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 30:8"/>To you, Yahweh, I cried out,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to the Lord I pled for favor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 30:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 30:9"/>“What profit {is there} in my blood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in my descent to the pit?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Will the dust praise you?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Will it declare your faithfulness?

<verse eid="PSA 30:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 30:10"/>Hear, Yahweh, and be gracious to me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, be my helper.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 30:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 30:11"/>You have turned for me my mourning to dancing;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have loosed my sackcloth
</para>
  <para style="q1">and have clothed me with gladness
<verse eid="PSA 30:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 30:12"/>in order that {my} glory may sing praise to you and not be silent.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh my God, I will give thanks to you forever.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 30:12"/><verse eid="PSA 30:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 30"/>
  <chapter number="31" style="c" sid="PSA 31"/>
  <para style="d">To the chief musician; a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 31:1"/>In you, Yahweh, I take refuge;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not ever let me have shame;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in your righteousness deliver me.
<verse eid="PSA 31:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 31:2"/>Incline your ear to me; rescue me quickly;
</para>
  <para style="q1">be for me a rocky summit of refuge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">a dwelling place of strongholds to save me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 31:3"/>Indeed, you are my rock and my stronghold;
</para>
  <para style="q1">therefore for the sake of your name you lead me and guide me.
<verse eid="PSA 31:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 31:4"/>You will pull me out of the net which they have secretly laid for me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you are my refuge.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 31:5"/>Into your hand I commit my spirit;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have redeemed me, Yahweh, God of faithfulness.
<verse eid="PSA 31:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 31:6"/>I hate the ones keeping idols of worthlessness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but I trust in Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 31:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 31:7"/>I will be glad and rejoice in your covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you have seen my affliction;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have known the troubles of my soul,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 31:8"/>and you have not delivered me into the hand of the ones being hostile to me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have set my feet in an open space.
<verse eid="PSA 31:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 31:9"/>Be gracious to me, Yahweh, for I am in distress;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my eye has wasted away from grief, my soul and my body.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 31:10"/>For my life has come to an end with sorrow,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my years with groaning;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my strength fails from my iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my bones waste away.
<verse eid="PSA 31:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 31:11"/>Among all of the ones being hostile to me I have become a reproach,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and especially to my neighbors,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and dread to the ones knowing me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones seeing me outside flee from me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 31:12"/>I have been forgotten like a dead man out of mind;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I am like a broken vessel.
<verse eid="PSA 31:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 31:13"/>For I hear the whispering of many—
</para>
  <para style="q1">terror on every side!—
</para>
  <para style="q1">while they conspire together against me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they plan to take my life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 31:14"/>But I trust in you, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I say, “You are my God.”
<verse eid="PSA 31:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 31:15"/>My times are in your hand;
</para>
  <para style="q1">rescue me from the hand of the ones being hostile to me and from the ones pursuing me.

<verse eid="PSA 31:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 31:16"/>Make your face shine upon your servant;
</para>
  <para style="q1">save me in your covenant faithfulness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 31:17"/>Yahweh, do not let me have shame, for I have called upon you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let the wicked have shame; let them be silent in Sheol.
<verse eid="PSA 31:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 31:18"/>Let lying lips be silenced,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones speaking insolent things against the righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in pride and contempt.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 31:19"/>How great is your goodness
</para>
  <para style="q1">which you have stored up for the ones fearing you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{which} you have done for the ones taking refuge in you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">before the sons of man!
<verse eid="PSA 31:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 31:20"/>You hide them in the hiding-place of your presence from the plots of man;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you hide them in a shelter from the strife of tongues.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 31:21"/>Blessed be Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for he has shown marvelously his covenant faithfulness to me in a besieged city.
<verse eid="PSA 31:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 31:22"/>For I said in my alarm,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“I am cut off from your eyes.”
</para>
  <para style="q1">But indeed you heard the voice of my pleas when I cried out to you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 31:23"/>Love Yahweh, all {you} faithful ones!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh preserves the faithful,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but he pays back fully the proud person.
<verse eid="PSA 31:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 31:24"/>Be firm and let your heart be courageous,
</para>
  <para style="q1">all the ones waiting for Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 31:24"/><verse eid="PSA 31:24"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 31"/>
  <chapter number="32" style="c" sid="PSA 32"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 32:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A maskil of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">The happinesses of the one whose transgression is lifted up,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one covered from sin!
<verse eid="PSA 32:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 32:2"/>The happinesses of the man to whom Yahweh reckons no guilt,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in whose spirit {there is} no deceit!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 32:3"/>When I kept silent, my bones wasted away
</para>
  <para style="q1">through my screaming all of the day.
<verse eid="PSA 32:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 32:4"/>For by day and night your hand was heavy upon me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My vitality was changed {as} by the heat of summer.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 32:5"/>My sin I acknowledged to you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my guilt I did not cover.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I said, “I will confess my transgressions to Yahweh,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you lifted up the guilt of my sin.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 32:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 32:6"/>For this {reason} let everyone who is faithful pray to you at a time of finding;
</para>
  <para style="q1">surely in a flood of great waters, they will not reach to him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 32:7"/>You are a hiding place for me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you preserve me from distress;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you will surround me {with} shouts of deliverance.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 32:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 32:8"/>I will instruct you and teach you in the way which you are to go.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will counsel you {with} my eye upon you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 32:9"/>Do not be like a horse {or} like a mule {which are} without understanding;
</para>
  <para style="q1">ornament of him to curb with bit and bridle,
</para>
  <para style="q1">or else they will not come near to you.
<verse eid="PSA 32:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 32:10"/>Many {are the} pains of the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the one trusting in Yahweh, covenant faithfulness surrounds him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 32:11"/>Be glad in Yahweh and rejoice, righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and shout for joy, all {you} upright of heart.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 32:11"/><verse eid="PSA 32:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 32"/>
  <chapter number="33" style="c" sid="PSA 33"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 33:1"/>Shout for joy in Yahweh, righteous {ones};
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise {is} fitting for the upright.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 33:2"/>Give thanks to Yahweh with the harp;
</para>
  <para style="q2">with a lyre of ten
{strings,} make music to him.

<verse eid="PSA 33:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 33:3"/>Sing to him a new song;
</para>
  <para style="q2">be skillful to play with a shout!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 33:4"/>For the word of Yahweh {is} upright,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of his work {is} in faithfulness.

<verse eid="PSA 33:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 33:5"/>Loving righteousness and justice,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the covenant faithfulness of Yahweh fills the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 33:6"/>By the word of Yahweh, the heavens were made,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and by the breath of his mouth, all of their host.

<verse eid="PSA 33:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 33:7"/>Gathering the waters of the sea like a heap;
</para>
  <para style="q2">putting the deeps into storehouses,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 33:8"/>let all of the earth fear Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let all of the dwellers of the world be in dread of him.

<verse eid="PSA 33:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 33:9"/>For he, he spoke, and it came to be;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he, he commanded, and it stood.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 33:10"/>Yahweh frustrates the counsel of nations;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he thwarts the plans of peoples.

<verse eid="PSA 33:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 33:11"/>The counsel of Yahweh stands forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the plans of his heart, to generation and generation.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 33:12"/>The happiness of the nation which Yahweh {is} its God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the people he chose for an inheritance for himself.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 33:13"/>From the heavens, Yahweh looks down;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he sees all of the sons of man.

<verse eid="PSA 33:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 33:14"/>From the place of his dwelling he gazes
</para>
  <para style="q2">at all of the dwellers of the earth,

<verse eid="PSA 33:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 33:15"/>the one forming their hearts together,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one understanding all of their works.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 33:16"/>The king is not saved by a great army;
</para>
  <para style="q2">a warrior is not delivered by great strength.

<verse eid="PSA 33:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 33:17"/>The horse {is} a falsehood for salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and by its great strength, it does not deliver.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 33:18"/>Behold, the eye of Yahweh {is} toward the fearers of him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">toward those hoping for his covenant faithfulness,

<verse eid="PSA 33:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 33:19"/>to deliver their soul from death
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to keep them alive in the famine.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 33:20"/>Our soul waits for Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he {is} our help and our shield.

<verse eid="PSA 33:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 33:21"/>For in him our heart rejoices;
</para>
  <para style="q2">for in the name of his holiness we trust.

<verse eid="PSA 33:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 33:22"/>Let your covenant faithfulness, Yahweh, be upon us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as we have hoped in you.


<verse eid="PSA 33:22"/><verse eid="PSA 33:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 33"/>
  <chapter number="34" style="c" sid="PSA 34"/>
  <para style="d">Of David; when he changed his behavior to the face of Abimelech and he sent him away and he left.

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 34:1"/>I shall bless Yahweh at all times;
</para>
  <para style="q2">continually his praise {is} in my mouth.
<verse eid="PSA 34:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 34:2"/>In Yahweh my soul will boast;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the humble will hear and rejoice.
<verse eid="PSA 34:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 34:3"/>Magnify Yahweh with me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let us exalt his name together.
<verse eid="PSA 34:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 34:4"/>I sought Yahweh, and he answered me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from all of my fears he delivered me.
<verse eid="PSA 34:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 34:5"/>They look to him and are radiant;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let their faces not have shame.
<verse eid="PSA 34:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 34:6"/>This afflicted {one} called, and Yahweh heard,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from all of his troubles he saved him.
<verse eid="PSA 34:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 34:7"/>The angel of Yahweh is encamping around the fearers of him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he rescues them.
<verse eid="PSA 34:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 34:8"/>Taste and see that Yahweh {is} good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the happinesses of the man—he takes refuge in him!
<verse eid="PSA 34:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 34:9"/>Fear Yahweh, his holy {ones},
</para>
  <para style="q2">for there is no lack for the fearers of him.
<verse eid="PSA 34:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 34:10"/>Young lions are poor and hungry,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the seekers of Yahweh will not lack any good {thing}.
<verse eid="PSA 34:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 34:11"/>Come, sons, listen to me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the fear of Yahweh I will teach you.
<verse eid="PSA 34:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 34:12"/>Who {is} the man, the {one} desiring life,
</para>
  <para style="q2">loving days to see good?
<verse eid="PSA 34:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 34:13"/>Guard your tongue from evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your lips from speaking deceit.
<verse eid="PSA 34:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 34:14"/>Turn away from evil and do good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">seek peace and pursue it.
<verse eid="PSA 34:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 34:15"/>The eyes of Yahweh {are} toward the righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his ears {are} toward their cry.
<verse eid="PSA 34:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 34:16"/>The face of Yahweh {is} against the doers of evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to cut off their remembrance from the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 34:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 34:17"/>They cry out, and Yahweh hears,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from all of their troubles he delivers them.
<verse eid="PSA 34:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 34:18"/>Yahweh {is} near to the broken of heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the crushed of spirit he saves.
<verse eid="PSA 34:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 34:19"/>Many {are} the evils of the righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh delivers him from all of them.
<verse eid="PSA 34:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 34:20"/>He is guarding all of his bones;
</para>
  <para style="q2">not one of them is broken.
<verse eid="PSA 34:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 34:21"/>Evil will put to death the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the haters of the righteous will be guilty.
<verse eid="PSA 34:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 34:22"/>Yahweh is redeeming the soul of his servants,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and everyone taking refuge in him will not be guilty.


<verse eid="PSA 34:22"/><verse eid="PSA 34:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 34"/>
  <chapter number="35" style="c" sid="PSA 35"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 35:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, oppose my opponents;
</para>
  <para style="q1">fight those fighting me.
<verse eid="PSA 35:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 35:2"/>Grab the small shield and large shield;
</para>
  <para style="q1">rise up as my helper!
<verse eid="PSA 35:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 35:3"/>Draw out spear and javelin to meet those chasing me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">say to my soul, “I {am} your salvation.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 35:4"/>May those who seek my life have shame and be dishonored.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May those who plan my harm be turned back and confounded.
<verse eid="PSA 35:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 35:5"/>May they be as chaff before the wind,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the angel of Yahweh driving {them} away.
<verse eid="PSA 35:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 35:6"/>May their way be dark and slippery places,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the angel of Yahweh chasing them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 35:7"/>For without cause they hid for me a pit, their net;
</para>
  <para style="q1">without cause they dug for my life.
<verse eid="PSA 35:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 35:8"/>Let destruction overtake him; he does not know.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let the net that he hid catch him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">In destruction, let him fall into it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 35:9"/>But my soul will be joyful in Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it will rejoice in his salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 35:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 35:10"/>All my bones will say, “Yahweh, who is like you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">rescuing the oppressed from those stronger than them
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the oppressed and needy from those robbing them?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 35:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="q1">Witnesses of violence rise up;
</para>
  <para style="q2">what I do not know they ask me.
<verse eid="PSA 35:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 35:12"/>They repay me evil in place of good—
</para>
  <para style="q2">bereavement to my soul.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 35:13"/>But I, when they were sick, my clothing {was} sackcloth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I afflicted my soul with fasting,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my prayer returned upon my bosom.
<verse eid="PSA 35:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 35:14"/>As {for} a friend, as {for} a brother to me, I walked about;
</para>
  <para style="q2">as {one} lamenting {for} a mother, mourning, I bowed down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 35:15"/>But at my stumbling they rejoiced and gathered together;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they gathered together against me, the stricken {ones}, and I did not know.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They tore and did not cease.
<verse eid="PSA 35:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 35:16"/>Among godless mockers of food,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they gnashed their teeth at me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 35:17"/>Lord, how long will you look on?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Restore my soul from their destructions,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my only {one} from the young lions!
<verse eid="PSA 35:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 35:18"/>I will thank you in the great assembly;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will praise you among many people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 35:19"/>Do not let my deceitful enemies rejoice over me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let {not} the haters of me without cause wink the eye.
<verse eid="PSA 35:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 35:20"/>For they do not speak peace,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and against the quiet {ones} of the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">they devise words of deceits.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 35:21"/>They open their mouth wide against me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they say, “Aha, Aha, our eyes have seen.”
<verse eid="PSA 35:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 35:22"/>You have seen, Yahweh; do not be silent;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Lord, do not be far from me.
<verse eid="PSA 35:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 35:23"/>Awake and arouse yourself for my justice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my God and my Lord, for my cause.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 35:24"/>Judge me according to your righteousness, Yahweh my God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not let them rejoice over me.
<verse eid="PSA 35:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 35:25"/>Do not let them say in their heart, “Aha, our soul!”
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not let them say, “We have swallowed him up.”
<verse eid="PSA 35:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 35:26"/>Let them be ashamed and confounded together,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those rejoicing at my evil.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let them be clothed with shame and humiliation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones magnifying {themselves} against me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 35:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 35:27"/>Let them shout for joy and be glad,
</para>
  <para style="q1">those delighting in my righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and let them say continually, “Let Yahweh be great,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the {one} delighting in the peace of his servant.”
<verse eid="PSA 35:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 35:28"/>And my tongue will meditate on your righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">all the day, your praise.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 35:28"/><verse eid="PSA 35:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 35"/>
  <chapter number="36" style="c" sid="PSA 36"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; of the servant of Yahweh; of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 36:1"/>The declaration of transgression to the wicked {is} in the midst of my heart:
</para>
  <para style="q2">there is no dread of God before his eyes.
<verse eid="PSA 36:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 36:2"/>For it is slippery to him in his eyes
</para>
  <para style="q2">to find his iniquity to hate {it}.
<verse eid="PSA 36:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 36:3"/>The words of his mouth {are} iniquity and deceit;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has ceased to act wisely, to do good.
<verse eid="PSA 36:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 36:4"/>He devises iniquity on his bed;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he stations himself on the not-good road;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does not reject evil.
<verse eid="PSA 36:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 36:5"/>Yahweh, your covenant faithfulness {is} in the heavens;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your trustworthiness, to the clouds.
<verse eid="PSA 36:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 36:6"/>Your righteousness {is} like the mountains of God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your judgments {are} the great deep.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You save man and beast, Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 36:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 36:7"/>How precious {is} your covenant faithfulness, God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">And the sons of man take refuge in the shadow of your wings.
<verse eid="PSA 36:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 36:8"/>They are refreshed from the fatness of your house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {from} the river of your delights you give them drink.
<verse eid="PSA 36:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 36:9"/>For with you {is} the fountain of life;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in your light we see light.
<verse eid="PSA 36:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 36:10"/>Extend your covenant faithfulness to the knowers of you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your righteousness to the upright of heart.
<verse eid="PSA 36:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 36:11"/>Let not the foot of pride come to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let not the hand of the wicked remove me.
<verse eid="PSA 36:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 36:12"/>There the doers of iniquity have fallen;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are thrust down and are not able to rise.


<verse eid="PSA 36:12"/><verse eid="PSA 36:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 36"/>
  <chapter number="37" style="c" sid="PSA 37"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 37:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not be upset about evildoers;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not be envious of the doers of unrighteousness.
<verse eid="PSA 37:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 37:2"/>For like the grass they will quickly wither,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and like a green plant they will fade.

<verse eid="PSA 37:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 37:3"/>Trust in Yahweh and do good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">inhabit the land and feed faithfulness.
<verse eid="PSA 37:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 37:4"/>And delight yourself in Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will give to you the desires of your heart.

<verse eid="PSA 37:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 37:5"/>Roll your way upon Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and trust in him, and he, he will act
<verse eid="PSA 37:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 37:6"/>and he will bring out your righteousness like the light,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your justice like the noonday.

<verse eid="PSA 37:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 37:7"/>Be silent to Yahweh and tremble for him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not be angry because of the {one} making his way prosper,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of a man doing schemes.

<verse eid="PSA 37:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 37:8"/>Let go of nose and abandon wrath;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not be angry; only to cause evil.
<verse eid="PSA 37:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 37:9"/>For evildoers will be cut off,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the ones waiting for Yahweh, they, they will inherit the land.

<verse eid="PSA 37:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 37:10"/>And yet a little and there are no wicked;
</para>
  <para style="q2">then you will look carefully at his place, but he is not.
<verse eid="PSA 37:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 37:11"/>But the meek will inherit the land
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will delight themselves over an abundance of peace.

<verse eid="PSA 37:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 37:12"/>The wicked is plotting against the righteous
</para>
  <para style="q2">and is gnashing his teeth against him.
<verse eid="PSA 37:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 37:13"/>The Lord laughs at him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for he sees that his day is coming.

<verse eid="PSA 37:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 37:14"/>The wicked have opened a sword and have trodden their bow
</para>
  <para style="q2">to bring down the poor and the needy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to slaughter the upright of way.
<verse eid="PSA 37:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 37:15"/>Their sword will come into their heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their bows will be broken.

<verse eid="PSA 37:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 37:16"/>Better
{is} the little of the righteous
</para>
  <para style="q2">than the abundance of many wicked.

<verse eid="PSA 37:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 37:17"/>For the arms of the wicked will be broken,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh is supporting the righteous.

<verse eid="PSA 37:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 37:18"/>Yahweh is knowing the days of the blameless,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their inheritance will be forever.

<verse eid="PSA 37:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 37:19"/>They will not have shame in a time of evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in the days of famine they will have enough.

<verse eid="PSA 37:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 37:20"/>For the wicked will perish,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the enemies of Yahweh {will be} like the precious of pastures;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they vanish, in smoke they vanish.

<verse eid="PSA 37:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 37:21"/>The wicked is borrowing and does not repay,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the righteous is showing grace and giving.

<verse eid="PSA 37:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 37:22"/>For those blessed by him will inherit the land,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but those cursed by him will be cut off.

<verse eid="PSA 37:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 37:23"/>From Yahweh the steps of a man are established,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he delights in his way.

<verse eid="PSA 37:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 37:24"/>Though he falls, he will not be hurled down,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for Yahweh is supporting his hand.

<verse eid="PSA 37:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 37:25"/>I was a youth, and I am old,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I have not seen the righteous abandoned
</para>
  <para style="q2">or his seed seeking bread.

<verse eid="PSA 37:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 37:26"/>All the day he is showing grace and lending,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his seed {are} for a blessing.

<verse eid="PSA 37:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 37:27"/>Turn away from evil and do good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and dwell forever.

<verse eid="PSA 37:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 37:28"/>For Yahweh is loving justice,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will not abandon his faithful.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Forever they are preserved,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the offspring of the wicked will be cut off.

<verse eid="PSA 37:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 37:29"/>The righteous will inherit the land
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will dwell forever upon it.
<verse eid="PSA 37:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 37:30"/>The mouth of the righteous murmurs wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his tongue speaks justice.
<verse eid="PSA 37:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 37:31"/>The law of his God {is} in his heart;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his steps will not slip.
<verse eid="PSA 37:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 37:32"/>The wicked is watching the righteous
</para>
  <para style="q2">and is seeking to kill him.
<verse eid="PSA 37:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 37:33"/>Yahweh will not abandon him into his hand,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will not condemn him when he is judged.
<verse eid="PSA 37:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 37:34"/>Wait for Yahweh and keep his way,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will raise you up to inherit the land.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When the wicked are cut off, you will see
{it.}
<verse eid="PSA 37:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 37:35"/>I have seen a wicked, violent {one},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and spreading himself out like a green native
{tree.}
<verse eid="PSA 37:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 37:36"/>And he passed away, and behold, he was not,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I sought him, and he was not found.
<verse eid="PSA 37:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 37:37"/>Watch the blameless and see the upright,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for {there is} a future for the man of peace.
<verse eid="PSA 37:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 37:38"/>But the transgressors are destroyed together;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the future of the wicked is cut off.
<verse eid="PSA 37:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 37:39"/>And the salvation of the righteous {is} from Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">their fortress in the time of distress.
<verse eid="PSA 37:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 37:40"/>And Yahweh helps them and delivers them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he delivers them from the wicked and saves them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they have taken refuge in him.


<verse eid="PSA 37:40"/><verse eid="PSA 37:40"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 37"/>
  <chapter number="38" style="c" sid="PSA 38"/>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David; to bring to remembrance.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 38:1"/>Yahweh, do not rebuke me in your anger,
</para>
  <para style="q2">nor discipline me in your wrath.
<verse eid="PSA 38:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 38:2"/>For your arrows have sunk into me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your hand has come down on me.
<verse eid="PSA 38:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 38:3"/>There is no soundness in my flesh from the face of your indignation;
</para>
  <para style="q2">there is no peace in my bones from the face of my sin.
<verse eid="PSA 38:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 38:4"/>For my iniquities have passed over my head;
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a heavy burden, they are too heavy for me.
<verse eid="PSA 38:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 38:5"/>My wounds stink, they fester
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the face of my foolishness.
<verse eid="PSA 38:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 38:6"/>I am twisted; I am bowed down exceedingly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all the day I go about mourning.
<verse eid="PSA 38:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 38:7"/>For my loins are full of burning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is no soundness in my flesh.
<verse eid="PSA 38:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 38:8"/>I am numb and crushed exceedingly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I roar from the groaning of my heart.
<verse eid="PSA 38:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 38:9"/>Lord, all of my desire {is} before you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my sighing is not hidden from you.
<verse eid="PSA 38:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 38:10"/>My heart pounds; my strength has left me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the light of my eyes—even they {are} not with me.
<verse eid="PSA 38:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 38:11"/>My loved ones and my friends stand from before my plague,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my relatives stand from afar.
<verse eid="PSA 38:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 38:12"/>And the seekers of my life lay snares,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the pursuers of my harm speak destructions
</para>
  <para style="q2">and mutter treacheries all the day.
<verse eid="PSA 38:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 38:13"/>But I {am} like a deaf man; I do not hear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and like a mute man—he does not open his mouth.
<verse eid="PSA 38:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 38:14"/>And I am like a man who is not hearing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there are no rebukes in his mouth.
<verse eid="PSA 38:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 38:15"/>Because for you, Yahweh, I have waited;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you, you will answer, Lord my God.
<verse eid="PSA 38:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 38:16"/>For I said, “Lest they rejoice over me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">at the slipping of my foot, they magnify
{themselves} against me.”
<verse eid="PSA 38:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 38:17"/>For I am set up for a stumbling,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my pain {is} before me continually.
<verse eid="PSA 38:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 38:18"/>For I declare my iniquity;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am anxious because of my sin.
<verse eid="PSA 38:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 38:19"/>But my living enemies are strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my haters of falsehood are many.
<verse eid="PSA 38:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 38:20"/>And the repayers of evil in exchange for good
</para>
  <para style="q2">accuse me in exchange for my pursuing of good.
<verse eid="PSA 38:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 38:21"/>Do not forsake me, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my God, do not be far from me.
<verse eid="PSA 38:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 38:22"/>Hurry to my help,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lord, my salvation.


<verse eid="PSA 38:22"/><verse eid="PSA 38:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 38"/>
  <chapter number="39" style="c" sid="PSA 39"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on Jeduthun. A psalm of David.

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 39:1"/>I said, “Let me guard my ways
</para>
  <para style="q2">from sinning with my tongue.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let me guard a muzzle for my mouth
</para>
  <para style="q2">while the wicked {is} before me.”
<verse eid="PSA 39:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 39:2"/>I was mute {with} silence;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I was silent from good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my pain was stirred up.

<verse eid="PSA 39:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 39:3"/>My heart became hot within me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in my sighing, fire burned.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I spoke with my tongue:

<verse eid="PSA 39:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 39:4"/>“Make me know my end, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the measure of my days, what it
{is}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May I know how transient I
{am.}

<verse eid="PSA 39:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 39:5"/>Behold, you have given my days {as} handbreadths,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my lifetime {is} as nothing before you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Surely every man stands {as} all vapor.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 39:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 39:6"/>Surely a man walks about as an image;
</para>
  <para style="q2">surely they make an uproar for vapor.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He heaps up and does not know
</para>
  <para style="q2">who will be gathering them.

<verse eid="PSA 39:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 39:7"/>And now, what do I wait for, Lord?
</para>
  <para style="q2">My hope, it {is} for you.

<verse eid="PSA 39:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 39:8"/>Deliver me from all my transgressions;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not make me the reproach of a fool.

<verse eid="PSA 39:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 39:9"/>I am mute; I do not open my mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you, you have done
{it}.

<verse eid="PSA 39:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 39:10"/>Remove your plague from upon me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the blow of your hand, I, I am finished.

<verse eid="PSA 39:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 39:11"/>With rebukes on account of iniquity you discipline a man,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you dissolve like a moth his desired thing.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Surely all mankind {is} vapor.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 39:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 39:12"/>Hear my prayer, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and give ear to my cry for help.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not be deaf to my weeping,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I {am} a sojourner with you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a foreigner like all my fathers.

<verse eid="PSA 39:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 39:13"/>Look away from me that I may be cheerful
</para>
  <para style="q2">before I go and I am no more.”


<verse eid="PSA 39:13"/><verse eid="PSA 39:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 39"/>
  <chapter number="40" style="c" sid="PSA 40"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; of David; a psalm

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 40:1"/>Waiting, I waited for Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he inclined to me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and heard my cry.
<verse eid="PSA 40:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 40:2"/>And he brought me up from the pit of tumult,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the mud of the mire,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he set my feet on a rock;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he established my steps.
<verse eid="PSA 40:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 40:3"/>And he put a new song in my mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise to our God.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Many will see and will fear
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will trust in Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 40:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 40:4"/>The happinesses of the man who has made
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh his trust,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and has not turned to the proud
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the goers aside to falsehood!
<verse eid="PSA 40:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 40:5"/>Many {things} you have done, you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh my God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">your wonderful deeds and your thoughts toward us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">there is none to line up against you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Should I declare and speak {them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are more than to recount.
<verse eid="PSA 40:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 40:6"/>Sacrifice and grain offering you have not desired;
</para>
  <para style="q2">ears you have dug for me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Burnt offering and sin offering
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have not asked for.
<verse eid="PSA 40:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 40:7"/>Then I said, “Behold, I have come;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the scroll of the book it is written about me.
<verse eid="PSA 40:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 40:8"/>To do your will, my God, I have delighted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your law {is} in the midst of my inward parts.”
<verse eid="PSA 40:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 40:9"/>I have proclaimed righteousness in the great assembly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">behold, I will not restrain my lips.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, you, you know.
<verse eid="PSA 40:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 40:10"/>I have not concealed your righteousness in the midst of my heart;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have declared your faithfulness and your salvation.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have not hidden your covenant faithfulness and your trustworthiness
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the great assembly.
<verse eid="PSA 40:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 40:11"/>You, Yahweh, will not withhold your compassion from me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your covenant faithfulness and your trustworthiness
</para>
  <para style="q2">will continually preserve me.
<verse eid="PSA 40:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 40:12"/>For evils have surrounded me
</para>
  <para style="q2">until there is no number;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my iniquities have overtaken me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am not able to see.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They are more numerous than the hairs of my head,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my heart has abandoned me.
<verse eid="PSA 40:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 40:13"/>Be pleased, Yahweh, to rescue me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, hurry to my help.
<verse eid="PSA 40:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 40:14"/>Let them have shame and have disgrace together,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the seekers of my life to sweep it away.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let them be turned back and be confounded,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those pleased with my harm.
<verse eid="PSA 40:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 40:15"/>Let them be appalled on account of their shame,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones saying to me, “Aha! Aha!”
<verse eid="PSA 40:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 40:16"/>Let all the seekers of you
</para>
  <para style="q2">rejoice and be glad in you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let the lovers of your salvation say continually,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“May Yahweh be great!”
<verse eid="PSA 40:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 40:17"/>And I {am} poor and needy;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Lord thinks of me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You {are} my help and my deliverer;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my God, do not delay.


<verse eid="PSA 40:17"/><verse eid="PSA 40:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 40"/>
  <chapter number="41" style="c" sid="PSA 41"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; a psalm of David

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 41:1"/>The happinesses of the one considering the lowly!
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the day of evil, Yahweh will rescue him.
<verse eid="PSA 41:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 41:2"/>Yahweh will guard him and will keep him alive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will be called happy in the land;
</para>
  <para style="q2">so do not give him into the soul of his enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 41:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 41:3"/>Yahweh will support him on the bed of suffering;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you transformed each bed of his in his sickness.
<verse eid="PSA 41:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 41:4"/>I, I said, “Yahweh, be gracious to me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Heal my soul, for I have sinned against you.”
<verse eid="PSA 41:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 41:5"/>My enemies say evil concerning me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“When will he die and his name perish?”
<verse eid="PSA 41:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 41:6"/>And if he comes to see
{me,} he speaks worthlessness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his heart gathers iniquity to itself.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He goes out to the outside; he speaks.
<verse eid="PSA 41:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 41:7"/>Together against me all my haters whisper;
</para>
  <para style="q2">against me they plan evil to me.
<verse eid="PSA 41:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 41:8"/>“A matter of wickedness is poured on him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he who has lain down will not repeat to rise.”
<verse eid="PSA 41:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 41:9"/>Even the man of my peace, whom I trusted in him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the eater of my bread,
</para>
  <para style="q2">has made great the heel against me.
<verse eid="PSA 41:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 41:10"/>But you, Yahweh, be gracious to me and raise me up,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may repay them.
<verse eid="PSA 41:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 41:11"/>By this I know that you delight in me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that my enemy does not shout over me.
<verse eid="PSA 41:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 41:12"/>And I, in my integrity you upheld me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you set me to your face forever.
<verse eid="PSA 41:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 41:13"/>Blessed {be} Yahweh, the God of Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the everlasting and unto the everlasting.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Amen and amen.


<verse eid="PSA 41:13"/><verse eid="PSA 41:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 41"/>
  <chapter number="42" style="c" sid="PSA 42"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book Two
</para>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A maskil of the sons of Korah.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 42:1"/>As a deer pants for streams of water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so my soul pants for you, God.
<verse eid="PSA 42:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 42:2"/>My soul thirsts for God, for the living God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When will I come and appear to the face of God?
<verse eid="PSA 42:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 42:3"/>My weeping is bread to me day and night,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in {their} saying to me all of the day, “Where {is} your God?”
<verse eid="PSA 42:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 42:4"/>Let me remember these,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let me pour out my soul within me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I went over with the crowd.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I led them in procession to the house of God
</para>
  <para style="q2">with a voice of rejoicing and praise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a multitude celebrating a festival.
<verse eid="PSA 42:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 42:5"/>Why have you bowed yourself down, my soul,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and are clamoring within me?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Wait for God, for I will again thank him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the salvation of his face.
<verse eid="PSA 42:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 42:6"/>My God, my soul has bowed itself down within me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Therefore I will remember you
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the land of the Jordan and the Hermons,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from Mount Mizar.
<verse eid="PSA 42:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 42:7"/>Deep is calling to deep at the sound of your waterfalls.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of your breakers and your waves pass over me.
<verse eid="PSA 42:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 42:8"/>{By} day, Yahweh commands his covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and at night, his song {is} with me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a prayer to the God of my life.
<verse eid="PSA 42:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 42:9"/>Let me say to God, my rock,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Why have you forgotten me?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Why do I walk about mourning
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of the oppression of the enemy?”
<verse eid="PSA 42:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 42:10"/>With crushing in my bones,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones afflicting me reproach me
</para>
  <para style="q1">in their saying to me all of the day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Where is your God?”
<verse eid="PSA 42:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 42:11"/>Why have you bowed yourself down, my soul,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and why are you clamoring within me?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Wait for God, for I will again thank him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the salvation of my face and my God.


<verse eid="PSA 42:11"/><verse eid="PSA 42:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 42"/>
  <chapter number="43" style="c" sid="PSA 43"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 43:1"/>Vindicate me, God, and plead my plea against a nation not faithful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rescue me from a deceitful and unjust man.
<verse eid="PSA 43:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 43:2"/>For you {are} the God of my refuge.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Why have you rejected me?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Why do I walk about mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?
<verse eid="PSA 43:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 43:3"/>Send out your light and your faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">them, let them lead me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let them bring me to the mountain of your holiness
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to your dwellings.
<verse eid="PSA 43:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 43:4"/>Let me come to the altar of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the God of the joy of my gladness.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will thank you with the lyre,
</para>
  <para style="q2">God, my God.
<verse eid="PSA 43:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 43:5"/>Why have you bowed yourself down, my soul,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and why are you clamoring within me?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Wait for God, for I will again thank him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the salvation of my face and my God.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 43:5"/><verse eid="PSA 43:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 43"/>
  <chapter number="44" style="c" sid="PSA 44"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A maskil of the sons of Korah.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 44:1"/>God, we have heard with our ears,
</para>
  <para style="q2">our fathers have recounted to us,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the work you worked in their days,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the days of antiquity.
<verse eid="PSA 44:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 44:2"/>You, you drove out the nations {by} your hand,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you planted them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You caused harm to the peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you sent them.
<verse eid="PSA 44:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 44:3"/>For they did not possess the land with their sword,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their arm did not save them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but your right hand and your arm and the light of your face,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you favored them.
<verse eid="PSA 44:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 44:4"/>You {are} he, my king, God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Command the salvation of Jacob.
<verse eid="PSA 44:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 44:5"/>By you we gore our enemies;
</para>
  <para style="q2">by your name we trample the ones arising {against} us.
<verse eid="PSA 44:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 44:6"/>For I do not trust in my bow,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my sword does not save me,
<verse eid="PSA 44:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 44:7"/>but you save us from our enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you shame the ones hating us.
<verse eid="PSA 44:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 44:8"/>In God we boast all of the day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we will praise your name forever.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 44:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 44:9"/>But you have rejected and humiliated us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you do not go out with our armies.
<verse eid="PSA 44:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 44:10"/>You make us turn back from the enemy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the ones hating us plunder for themselves.
<verse eid="PSA 44:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 44:11"/>You have made us like sheep of food,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have scattered us among the nations.
<verse eid="PSA 44:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 44:12"/>You have sold your people for not-wealth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have not increased by their price.
<verse eid="PSA 44:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 44:13"/>You have made us a reproach to our neighbors,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a scorn and a derision to {those} around us.
<verse eid="PSA 44:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 44:14"/>You have made us a proverb among the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a shaking of the head among the peoples.
<verse eid="PSA 44:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 44:15"/>All of the day my disgrace {is} before me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the shame of my face covers me,
<verse eid="PSA 44:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 44:16"/>from the voice of one reproaching and one reviling,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the face of an enemy and one avenging.
<verse eid="PSA 44:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 44:17"/>All of this has come {to} us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but we have not forgotten you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we have not dealt falsely with your covenant.
<verse eid="PSA 44:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 44:18"/>Our heart has not turned itself back,
</para>
  <para style="q2">nor have our steps turned aside from your way.
<verse eid="PSA 44:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 44:19"/>But you have crushed us into a place of jackals,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have covered over us with a dark shadow.
<verse eid="PSA 44:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 44:20"/>If we had forgotten the name of our God
</para>
  <para style="q2">and spread out our palms to a foreign god,
<verse eid="PSA 44:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 44:21"/>would God not have discovered this?
</para>
  <para style="q2">For he is knowing the secrets of the heart.
<verse eid="PSA 44:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 44:22"/>But because of you we are killed all of the day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">we are considered like sheep of slaughter.
<verse eid="PSA 44:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 44:23"/>Awake! Why are you sleeping, Lord?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Wake up! Do not reject {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 44:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 44:24"/>Why do you hide your face,
</para>
  <para style="q2">forget our affliction and our oppression?
<verse eid="PSA 44:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 44:25"/>For our soul has sunk down into the dust,
</para>
  <para style="q2">our belly clings to the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 44:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 44:26"/>Arise {as} a helper to us
</para>
  <para style="q1">and redeem us because of your covenant faithfulness.


<verse eid="PSA 44:26"/><verse eid="PSA 44:26"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 44"/>
  <chapter number="45" style="c" sid="PSA 45"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on “Lilies.” A maskil of the sons of Korah; a song of loves.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 45:1"/>My heart boils over {with} a good matter.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am reciting my works to the king.
</para>
  <para style="q2">My tongue is the stylus of a quick scribe.
<verse eid="PSA 45:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 45:2"/>You are fairer than the sons of man.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Grace is poured onto your lips.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Therefore God has blessed you forever.
<verse eid="PSA 45:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 45:3"/>Gird your sword on your thigh, warrior,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{in} your glory and your majesty.
<verse eid="PSA 45:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 45:4"/>And {in} your majesty prosper, ride out
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the sake of truth and humility {and} righteousness.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May your right hand teach you fearful things.
<verse eid="PSA 45:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 45:5"/>Your arrows are sharp;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the peoples fall under you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the heart of the enemies of the king.
<verse eid="PSA 45:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 45:6"/>Your throne, God, {is} forever and ever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">A scepter of justice {is} the scepter of your kingdom.
<verse eid="PSA 45:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 45:7"/>You love righteousness, and you hate wickedness.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Therefore God, your God, has anointed you
</para>
  <para style="q2">{with} the oil of joy more than your companions.
<verse eid="PSA 45:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 45:8"/>Myrrh and aloes, cassia, {are} all of your garments.
</para>
  <para style="q2">From palaces of ivory, stringed instruments make you rejoice.

<verse eid="PSA 45:8"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 45:9"/>Daughters of kings {are} among your precious {ones}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The queen is stationed at your right hand in gold of Ophir.
<verse eid="PSA 45:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 45:10"/>Listen, daughter, and consider, and incline your ear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and forget your people and the house of your father.
<verse eid="PSA 45:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 45:11"/>Then the king will desire your beauty.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because he is your lord, prostrate yourself to him.
<verse eid="PSA 45:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 45:12"/>The daughter of Tyre with a gift;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the rich of the people will entreat your face.
<verse eid="PSA 45:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 45:13"/>All glorious {is} the daughter of the king within;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from interweavings of gold {is} her clothing.
<verse eid="PSA 45:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 45:14"/>She will be led to the king in embroidery.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The virgins after her, her companions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">will be brought to you.
<verse eid="PSA 45:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 45:15"/>They will be led by joy and rejoicing;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will enter into the palace of the king.
<verse eid="PSA 45:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 45:16"/>In place of your fathers will be your sons;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will make him princes in all of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 45:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 45:17"/>Let me make {people} remember your name in every generation to generation;
</para>
  <para style="q2">therefore the peoples will thank you forever and ever.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 45:17"/><verse eid="PSA 45:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 45"/>
  <chapter number="46" style="c" sid="PSA 46"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. Of the sons of Korah. On “Maidens.” A song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 46:1"/>God {is} to us a refuge and strength,
</para>
  <para style="q2">being found greatly a help in trouble.
<verse eid="PSA 46:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 46:2"/>Therefore we will not fear in the changing of the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the shaking of the mountains into the heart of the seas,
<verse eid="PSA 46:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 46:3"/>should its waters roar and foam,
</para>
  <para style="q2">should the mountains quake at its swelling.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 46:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 46:4"/>A stream, its channels make the city of God rejoice,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the holy {place} of the dwellings of the Most High.
<verse eid="PSA 46:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 46:5"/>God {is} in the midst of her, she will not be shaken.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God will help her at the turning of the morning.
<verse eid="PSA 46:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 46:6"/>Nations may roar; kingdoms may shake.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He utters with his voice; the earth melts.
<verse eid="PSA 46:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 46:7"/>Yahweh of Armies {is} with us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the God of Jacob {is} a stronghold to us.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 46:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 46:8"/>Come, see the works of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who makes desolations on the earth,
<verse eid="PSA 46:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 46:9"/>making wars cease to the end of the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He shatters the bow and cuts the spear in pieces;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he burns the wagons with fire.
<verse eid="PSA 46:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 46:10"/>“Be still and know that I {am} God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will be high among the nations, I will be high on the earth.”
<verse eid="PSA 46:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 46:11"/>Yahweh of Armies {is} with us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the God of Jacob {is} a stronghold to us.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 46:11"/><verse eid="PSA 46:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 46"/>
  <chapter number="47" style="c" sid="PSA 47"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A psalm of the sons of Korah.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 47:1"/>Clap a palm, all peoples!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Shout to God with a voice of rejoicing.
<verse eid="PSA 47:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 47:2"/>For Yahweh, the Most High, is to be feared,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the great king over all of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 47:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 47:3"/>He subdues peoples under us
</para>
  <para style="q2">and nations under our feet.
<verse eid="PSA 47:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 47:4"/>He chose our inheritance for us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the pride of Jacob, whom he loved.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 47:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 47:5"/>God has gone up with a shout,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh with the sound of a shofar.
<verse eid="PSA 47:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 47:6"/>Sing praise {to} God, sing praise!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Sing praise {to} our king, sing praise!
<verse eid="PSA 47:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 47:7"/>For God {is} the king of all of the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Sing praise {with} a maskil.
<verse eid="PSA 47:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 47:8"/>God reigns over the nations;
</para>
  <para style="q2">God sits on the throne of his holiness.
<verse eid="PSA 47:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 47:9"/>The nobles of the peoples will gather themselves
</para>
  <para style="q2">{as} the people of the God of Abraham,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for {to} God are the shields of the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is greatly exalted!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 47:9"/><verse eid="PSA 47:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 47"/>
  <chapter number="48" style="c" sid="PSA 48"/>
  <para style="d">A song. A psalm of the sons of Korah.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 48:1"/>Yahweh is great, and he is being praised greatly
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the city of our God, {on} the mountain of his holiness.
<verse eid="PSA 48:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 48:2"/>Beautiful of elevation, the joy of all of the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{is} Mount Zion {in} the recesses of the north,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the city of the great king.
<verse eid="PSA 48:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 48:3"/>God {is} in her citadels.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is known as a stronghold.
<verse eid="PSA 48:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 48:4"/>For behold, kings assembled themselves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they advanced together.
<verse eid="PSA 48:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 48:5"/>They, they saw, then they marveled.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They were terrified, they hastened themselves away.
<verse eid="PSA 48:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 48:6"/>Trembling seized them there,
</para>
  <para style="q2">pain like childbearing.
<verse eid="PSA 48:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 48:7"/>With the wind of the east,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you shatter ships of Tarshish.
<verse eid="PSA 48:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 48:8"/>As we have heard, so we have seen
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the city of Yahweh of Armies, in the city of our God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God will establish it to forever.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 48:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 48:9"/>We have compared your covenant faithfulness, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the midst of your temple.
<verse eid="PSA 48:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 48:10"/>As {is} your name, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so {is} your praise to the ends of the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Your right hand is full {of} righteousness.
<verse eid="PSA 48:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 48:11"/>Let Mount Zion rejoice,
</para>
  <para style="q2">let the daughters of Judah be glad,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of your judgments.
<verse eid="PSA 48:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 48:12"/>Circle Zion and go around her.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Count her towers,
<verse eid="PSA 48:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 48:13"/>put your heart to her rampart, consider her citadels,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that you may recount to a later generation.
<verse eid="PSA 48:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 48:14"/>For this God {is} our God forever and ever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He, he will guide us until death.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 48:14"/><verse eid="PSA 48:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 48"/>
  <chapter number="49" style="c" sid="PSA 49"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A psalm of the sons of Korah.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 49:1"/>Hear this, all peoples!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Listen, all dwellers of the world,
<verse eid="PSA 49:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 49:2"/>both sons of a human and sons of a man,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the rich and the poor together.
<verse eid="PSA 49:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 49:3"/>My mouth will speak wisdom,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the meditation of my heart, understanding.
<verse eid="PSA 49:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 49:4"/>I will incline my ear to a proverb;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will open my enigma with a harp.
<verse eid="PSA 49:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 49:5"/>Why should I fear in the days of evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{when} the iniquity of my heels surrounds me,
<verse eid="PSA 49:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 49:6"/>the ones trusting in their wealth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in the abundance of their treasure they boast?
<verse eid="PSA 49:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 49:7"/>Redeeming, a man does not redeem a brother,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does not give his ransom to God.
<verse eid="PSA 49:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 49:8"/>For the redemption of their life is costly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it ceases forever,
<verse eid="PSA 49:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 49:9"/>that one should live on forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{that} one should not see the pit.
<verse eid="PSA 49:9"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 49:10"/>For one will see.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The wise die, likewise the fool and the brute perish,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they leave their wealth to others.
<verse eid="PSA 49:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 49:11"/>Inside of them, their houses {are} forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">their dwellings {are} to generation and generation.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They call over lands by their names.
<verse eid="PSA 49:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 49:12"/>But a human does not abide in honor.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is likened to the beasts, they are destroyed.
<verse eid="PSA 49:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 49:13"/>This, their way, {is} folly to them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but after them, they delight in their mouths.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 49:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 49:14"/>Like sheep, they appoint {them} to Sheol;
</para>
  <para style="q2">death will shepherd them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And the upright will rule over them in the morning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Sheol will consume their form from the dwelling to it.
<verse eid="PSA 49:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 49:15"/>But God will redeem my soul from the hand of Sheol,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for he will take me.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 49:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 49:16"/>Do not fear when a man becomes rich,
</para>
  <para style="q2">when the glory of his house increases.
<verse eid="PSA 49:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 49:17"/>For in his death, he will not take anything;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his glory will not go down after him.
<verse eid="PSA 49:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 49:18"/>Although in his life he blesses his soul
</para>
  <para style="q2">(and they do praise you when you do well for yourself),
<verse eid="PSA 49:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 49:19"/>he will come to the generation of his fathers;
</para>
  <para style="q2">forever they will not see light.
<verse eid="PSA 49:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 49:20"/>A human in honor, but he does not understand,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is likened to the beasts, they are destroyed.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 49:20"/><verse eid="PSA 49:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 49"/>
  <chapter number="50" style="c" sid="PSA 50"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 50:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A Psalm of Asaph
</para>
  <para style="q1">The God of gods, Yahweh, has spoken,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he has summoned the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the rising of the sun to its setting.
<verse eid="PSA 50:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 50:2"/>From Zion, the perfection of beauty,
</para>
  <para style="q2">God has shined forth.
<verse eid="PSA 50:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 50:3"/>Our God comes, and he is not silent.
</para>
  <para style="q2">A fire devours to his face,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and around him it is stormed greatly.
<verse eid="PSA 50:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 50:4"/>He calls to the heavens above and to the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that he may judge his people.
<verse eid="PSA 50:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 50:5"/>“Gather my faithful {ones} to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the cutters of my covenant by sacrifice.”
<verse eid="PSA 50:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 50:6"/>The heavens declare his righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that God, he is judge.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 50:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 50:7"/>“Hear, my people, and I will speak;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Israel, and I will testify against you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I {am} God, your God.
<verse eid="PSA 50:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 50:8"/>I do not accuse you regarding your sacrifices,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for your burnt offerings are always before me.
<verse eid="PSA 50:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 50:9"/>I will not take a bull from your house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">goats from your folds.
<verse eid="PSA 50:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 50:10"/>For every beast of the forest {is} to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the cattle on a thousand hills.
<verse eid="PSA 50:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 50:11"/>I know all the birds of the mountains,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the creature of the field {is} with me.
<verse eid="PSA 50:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 50:12"/>If I were hungry, I would not say {that} to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the world and its fulness {are} to me.
<verse eid="PSA 50:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 50:13"/>Do I eat the flesh of bulls,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or do I drink the blood of goats?
<verse eid="PSA 50:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 50:14"/>Sacrifice a thank offering to God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and pay your vows to the Most High.
<verse eid="PSA 50:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 50:15"/>Call on me in the day of trouble;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will deliver you, and you will glorify me.”
<verse eid="PSA 50:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 50:16"/>But to the wicked {one} God says,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“What to you to recount my statutes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or that you should lift up my covenant onto your mouth?
<verse eid="PSA 50:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 50:17"/>For you, you hate instruction,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you cast my words behind you.
<verse eid="PSA 50:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 50:18"/>When you see a thief, you approve of him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you partake with adulterers.
<verse eid="PSA 50:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 50:19"/>You send your mouth in evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your tongue frames deceit.
<verse eid="PSA 50:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 50:20"/>You sit, you speak against your brother;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you impute slander against the son of your mother.
<verse eid="PSA 50:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 50:21"/>You have done these {things},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I have been silent.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You thought the being of I AM {was} like you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will accuse you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let me array to your eyes.
<verse eid="PSA 50:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 50:22"/>Consider this now, forgetters of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">lest I tear and none be delivering!
<verse eid="PSA 50:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 50:23"/>The one sacrificing a thank offering glorifies me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the one placing a way,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will make him look upon the salvation of God.”


<verse eid="PSA 50:23"/><verse eid="PSA 50:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 50"/>
  <chapter number="51" style="c" sid="PSA 51"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A psalm of David, when Nathan the prophet came to him after he had gone in to Bathsheba.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 51:1"/>Be merciful to me, God, according to your covenant faithfulness.
</para>
  <para style="q2">According to the multitude of your compassions, wipe away my transgressions.
<verse eid="PSA 51:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 51:2"/>Make great, wash me from my iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and cleanse me from my sin.
<verse eid="PSA 51:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 51:3"/>For I, I know my transgressions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my sin {is} always before me.
<verse eid="PSA 51:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 51:4"/>Against you, you only, I have sinned
</para>
  <para style="q2">and done evil in your eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so you are right in your speaking,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are blameless in your judging.
<verse eid="PSA 51:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 51:5"/>Behold, I was born in iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in sin my mother conceived me.
<verse eid="PSA 51:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 51:6"/>Behold, you desire truth in the kidneys,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you teach me wisdom in the closed {place}.
<verse eid="PSA 51:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 51:7"/>May you purify me with hyssop, that I may be clean.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May you wash me, that I may be whiter than snow.
<verse eid="PSA 51:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 51:8"/>Make me hear joy and gladness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may the bones you have crushed rejoice.
<verse eid="PSA 51:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 51:9"/>Hide your face from my sins,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and wipe away all of my iniquities.
<verse eid="PSA 51:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 51:10"/>Create for me a clean heart, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and renew an established spirit within me.
<verse eid="PSA 51:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 51:11"/>May you not cast me away from your face,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may you not take the Spirit of your holiness from me.
<verse eid="PSA 51:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 51:12"/>Restore to me the joy of your salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and support me {with} a willing spirit.
<verse eid="PSA 51:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 51:13"/>Let me teach transgressors your ways,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that sinners may return to you.
<verse eid="PSA 51:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 51:14"/>Deliver me from blood, God, the God of my salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">may my tongue sing {about} your righteousness.
<verse eid="PSA 51:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 51:15"/>Lord, may you open my lips,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that my mouth may declare your praise.
<verse eid="PSA 51:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 51:16"/>For you do not delight in sacrifice, or I would give {it};
</para>
  <para style="q2">you do not accept a burnt offering.
<verse eid="PSA 51:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 51:17"/>The sacrifices of God {are} a broken spirit.
</para>
  <para style="q2">A broken and crushed heart, God, you will not despise.
<verse eid="PSA 51:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 51:18"/>Do good to Zion in your acceptance;
</para>
  <para style="q2">build the walls of Jerusalem.
<verse eid="PSA 51:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 51:19"/>Then you will delight in sacrifices of righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a burnt offering and a whole {one}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then they will offer bulls on your altar.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 51:19"/><verse eid="PSA 51:19"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 51"/>
  <chapter number="52" style="c" sid="PSA 52"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A maskil of David. When Doeg the Edomite came and declared to Saul and said to him, “David came to the house of Ahimelech.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 52:1"/>Why do you boast about harm, O warrior?
</para>
  <para style="q2">The covenant faithfulness of God all of the day.
<verse eid="PSA 52:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 52:2"/>Like a sharpened razor, your tongue devises calamities,
</para>
  <para style="q2">worker of betrayal!
<verse eid="PSA 52:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 52:3"/>You love evil more than good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">lying more than speaking righteousness.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 52:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 52:4"/>You love all words of destruction,
</para>
  <para style="q2">tongue of betrayal!
<verse eid="PSA 52:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 52:5"/>God will also tear you down forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will take you away and tear you from the tent
</para>
  <para style="q2">and uproot you from the land of the living.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 52:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 52:6"/>And the righteous will see and fear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will laugh at him.
<verse eid="PSA 52:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 52:7"/>“Behold, the man did not make God his refuge,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he trusted in the abundance of his wealth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he was strong in his calamity.”
<verse eid="PSA 52:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 52:8"/>But I {am} like a green olive tree in the house of God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will trust in the covenant faithfulness of God forever and ever.
<verse eid="PSA 52:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 52:9"/>I will thank you forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you have done {this}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will await your name,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for {it is} good before your faithful {ones}.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 52:9"/><verse eid="PSA 52:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 52"/>
  <chapter number="53" style="c" sid="PSA 53"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on “Weakness.” A maskil of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 53:1"/>The fool says in his heart, “No God.”
</para>
  <para style="q2">They are corrupt, and they do iniquity abominably.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{There is} none doing good.
<verse eid="PSA 53:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 53:2"/>God looks down from the heavens on the sons of man
</para>
  <para style="q2">to see whether there is one understanding,
</para>
  <para style="q2">one seeking God.
<verse eid="PSA 53:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 53:3"/>All of him has turned away.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Together they have corrupted themselves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{There is} none doing good, not even one.
<verse eid="PSA 53:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 53:4"/>Do they not know, the doers of iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones eating my people {as} they eat bread?
</para>
  <para style="q2">They do not call {upon} God.
<verse eid="PSA 53:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 53:5"/>There they feared a fear {when} no fear was,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because God scattered the bones of the one encamping against you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have shamed {them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">for God despises them.
<verse eid="PSA 53:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 53:6"/>Who will give the salvation of Israel from Zion?
</para>
  <para style="q1">When God restores the prosperity of his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Jacob will be glad, Israel will rejoice.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 53:6"/><verse eid="PSA 53:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 53"/>
  <chapter number="54" style="c" sid="PSA 54"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; with stringed instruments. A maskil of David. When the Ziphites came and said to Saul, “Is not David hiding himself among us?”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 54:1"/>Save me, God, by your name,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and vindicate me by your might.
<verse eid="PSA 54:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 54:2"/>Hear my prayer, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">listen to the words of my mouth.
<verse eid="PSA 54:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 54:3"/>For foreigners have arisen against me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and violent {ones} seek my life.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They do not set God before them.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 54:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 54:4"/>Behold, God is a helper to me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Lord {is} with the sustainers of my life.
<verse eid="PSA 54:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 54:5"/>He will return harm to my enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In your faithfulness, destroy them!
<verse eid="PSA 54:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 54:6"/>With a freewill offering, I will sacrifice to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise your name, Yahweh, for {it is} good.
<verse eid="PSA 54:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 54:7"/>For he delivers me from every trouble,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my eye looks at my enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 54:7"/><verse eid="PSA 54:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 54"/>
  <chapter number="55" style="c" sid="PSA 55"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; with stringed instruments. A maskil of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 55:1"/>Listen {to} my prayer, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not hide yourself from my plea.
<verse eid="PSA 55:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 55:2"/>Attend to me and answer me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am restless in my complaint, and let me moan
<verse eid="PSA 55:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 55:3"/>from the voice of the enemy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the face of the oppression of the wicked.
</para>
  <para style="q1">For they shake trouble onto me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in nose they persecute me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 55:4"/>My heart writhes in the midst of me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the terrors of death have fallen onto me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 55:5"/>Fear and trembling have come on me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and horror has covered me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 55:6"/>I have said, “Who will give the wing of a dove to me?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let me fly away and let me dwell.
<verse eid="PSA 55:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 55:7"/>Behold, I would make distance, wandering;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I would lodge in the wilderness.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 55:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 55:8"/>Let me hasten for myself
</para>
  <para style="q2">{to} an escape from the storming wind,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the tempest.”
<verse eid="PSA 55:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 55:9"/>Swallow {them}, Lord, divide their tongue!
</para>
  <para style="q2">For I have seen violence and strife in the city.
<verse eid="PSA 55:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 55:10"/>Day and night they go around it on its walls,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and iniquity and trouble {are} in the midst of it.
<verse eid="PSA 55:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 55:11"/>Calamity {is} in the midst of it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and oppression and deceit do not depart from its open square.
<verse eid="PSA 55:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 55:12"/>For an enemy does not reproach me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">then I would bear {it}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">One hating me has not made great against me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">then I would hide myself from him.
<verse eid="PSA 55:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 55:13"/>But {it was} you, a man according to my valuation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my companion and my acquaintance,
<verse eid="PSA 55:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 55:14"/>we who together made counsel sweet;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we walked in the house of God with the throng.
<verse eid="PSA 55:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 55:15"/>{May} desolations {be} upon them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they go down {to} Sheol alive,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for evils {are} in their dwelling,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the midst of them.
<verse eid="PSA 55:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 55:16"/>I, I will call to God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh will save me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 55:17"/>Evening and morning and noon,
</para>
  <para style="q2">let me complain and moan,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will hear my voice.
<verse eid="PSA 55:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 55:18"/>He redeems my life in peace from the battle against me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for with many they are against me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 55:19"/>God will hear and answer them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">even the one sitting {from} antiquity,
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
</para>
  <para style="q1">to whom {there are} no changes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so they do not fear God.
<verse eid="PSA 55:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 55:20"/>He stretches out his hands against his friends;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he defiles his covenant.
<verse eid="PSA 55:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 55:21"/>The curds of his mouth were smooth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but his heart {was} war.
</para>
  <para style="q1">His words were softer than oil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they {were} unsheathed {swords}.
<verse eid="PSA 55:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 55:22"/>Cast your burden on Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he, he will sustain you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Forever he will not allow shaking to the righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 55:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 55:23"/>But you, God, will make them go down to the pit of the grave.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Men of blood and treachery will not halve their days.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But I, I will trust in you.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 55:23"/><verse eid="PSA 55:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 55"/>
  <chapter number="56" style="c" sid="PSA 56"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on “A Faraway Silent Dove.” Of David. A miktam. When the Philistines seized him in Gath.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 56:1"/>Be gracious to me, God, for man tramples me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of the day, fighting, he oppresses me.
<verse eid="PSA 56:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 56:2"/>My enemies trample me all of the day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for many are fighting against me arrogantly.
<verse eid="PSA 56:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 56:3"/>The day I fear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I, I will trust in you.
<verse eid="PSA 56:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 56:4"/>In God—I praise his word—in God I trust.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not fear. What will flesh do to me?
<verse eid="PSA 56:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 56:5"/>All of the day they vex my matters;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of their thoughts {are} against me for harm.
<verse eid="PSA 56:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 56:6"/>They gather together, they hide;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they, they watch my heels because they await my life.
<verse eid="PSA 56:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 56:7"/>Upon iniquity {shall there be} an escape for them?
</para>
  <para style="q2">In nose, make the peoples go down, God.
<verse eid="PSA 56:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 56:8"/>You, you record my wandering.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Put my tears in your bag.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Are they} not in your record?
<verse eid="PSA 56:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 56:9"/>Then my enemies will turn back on the day I call.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This I know, for God {is} for me.
<verse eid="PSA 56:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 56:10"/>In God—I praise his word—
</para>
  <para style="q2">in Yahweh—I praise his word—
<verse eid="PSA 56:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 56:11"/>in God I trust.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will not fear. What will man do to me?
<verse eid="PSA 56:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 56:12"/>Your vows {are} on me, God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will pay a thank-offering to you.
<verse eid="PSA 56:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 56:13"/>For you deliver my life from death.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Are} not my feet from stumbling,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I may walk about to the face of God in the light of the living?

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 56:13"/><verse eid="PSA 56:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 56"/>
  <chapter number="57" style="c" sid="PSA 57"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; “May You Not Destroy.” Of David; a miktam. When he fled from the face of Saul, in the cave.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 57:1"/>Be gracious to me, God, be gracious to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for in you my soul takes refuge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in the shadow of your wings I take refuge
</para>
  <para style="q2">until the calamities have passed by.
<verse eid="PSA 57:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 57:2"/>I call to God Most High,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to God, the one accomplishing for me.
<verse eid="PSA 57:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 57:3"/>May he send from the heavens and save me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May he reproach the one trampling me.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
</para>
  <para style="q2">May God send his covenant faithfulness and his truth.
<verse eid="PSA 57:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 57:4"/>My soul {is} in the midst of lions;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I must lie down {among} blazing ones, sons of man.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Their teeth {are} a spear and arrows,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their tongue {is} a sharp sword.
<verse eid="PSA 57:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 57:5"/>Be high above the heavens, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{may} your glory {be} above all of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 57:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 57:6"/>They prepare a net for my steps;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my soul bows down.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They dig a pit to my face;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they fall into the midst of it.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 57:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 57:7"/>My heart is established, God, my heart is established.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let me sing and make music.
<verse eid="PSA 57:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 57:8"/>Awake, my glory!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Awake, lyre and harp!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let me awaken the dawn.
<verse eid="PSA 57:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 57:9"/>I will thank you, Lord, among the peoples;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will make music to you among the nations.
<verse eid="PSA 57:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 57:10"/>For your covenant faithfulness {is} great to the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your truth to the clouds.
<verse eid="PSA 57:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 57:11"/>Be high above the heavens, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{may} your glory {be} above all of the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 57:11"/><verse eid="PSA 57:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 57"/>
  <chapter number="58" style="c" sid="PSA 58"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; “May You Not Destroy.” Of David; a miktam.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 58:1"/>Truly {in} silence do you speak righteousness?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do you judge uprightly, sons of man?
<verse eid="PSA 58:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 58:2"/>No, in the heart you do wickedness.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Your hands weigh out violence on the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 58:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 58:3"/>The wicked turn aside from the womb;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they stray from the belly, speaking falsehood.
<verse eid="PSA 58:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 58:4"/>The poison to them {is} like the likeness of the poison of a serpent.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{They are} like a deaf adder {that} shuts its ears,
<verse eid="PSA 58:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 58:5"/>that does not listen to the voice of charmers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">one charming charms, being made wise.
<verse eid="PSA 58:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 58:6"/>God, break their teeth in their mouth!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Break out the fangs of the young lions, Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 58:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 58:7"/>May they be melted like waters {that} run off to them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{When} he treads his arrows, {may they be} as if they are cut off.
<verse eid="PSA 58:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 58:8"/>{May they be} like a snail {that} melts; it goes away.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{May they be like} the miscarriage of a woman; they do not see the sun.
<verse eid="PSA 58:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 58:9"/>Before your pots perceive the thorn, like the living, like the burning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will whirlwind it away.
<verse eid="PSA 58:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 58:10"/>The righteous will rejoice when he sees vengeance.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will wash his feet in the blood of the wicked.
<verse eid="PSA 58:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 58:11"/>Then man will say, “Truly, fruit {is} to the righteous.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Truly, there is a God judging the earth.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 58:11"/><verse eid="PSA 58:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 58"/>
  <chapter number="59" style="c" sid="PSA 59"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; “May You Not Destroy.” Of David; a miktam. When Saul sent and they watched the house to kill him.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 59:1"/>Deliver me from my enemies, my God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Set me on high, away from the ones rising up against me.
<verse eid="PSA 59:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 59:2"/>Deliver me from workers of iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and save me from men of blood.
<verse eid="PSA 59:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 59:3"/>For behold, they lie in wait for my life;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the mighty gather against me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Not {for} my transgression
</para>
  <para style="q2">and not {for} my sin, Yahweh,
<verse eid="PSA 59:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 59:4"/>without iniquity, they run and prepare themselves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Awake to meet me, and see!
<verse eid="PSA 59:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 59:5"/>So you, Yahweh, God of armies, the God of Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">wake up to punish all of the nations!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not be gracious {to} any treacherous workers of iniquity.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 59:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 59:6"/>They return at evening,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they growl like a dog and go around the city.
<verse eid="PSA 59:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 59:7"/>Behold, they belch out with their mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">swords {are} in their lips,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for, “Who is hearing?”
<verse eid="PSA 59:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 59:8"/>But you, Yahweh, laugh at them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You mock all of the nations.
<verse eid="PSA 59:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 59:9"/>Let me wait for you, his strength,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for God {is} my stronghold.
<verse eid="PSA 59:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 59:10"/>The God of my covenant faithfulness will meet me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God will make me look upon my enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 59:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 59:11"/>Do not slay them, lest my people forget.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Scatter them by your power and bring them down, Lord, our shield.
<verse eid="PSA 59:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 59:12"/>{For} the sin of their mouth, the word of their lips,
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they be taken in their pride,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for the curse and for the lying they tell.
<verse eid="PSA 59:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 59:13"/>Consume {them} in wrath;
</para>
  <para style="q2">consume {them} that they {may} not {be},
</para>
  <para style="q1">that they may know that God is ruling in Jacob
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the ends of the earth.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 59:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 59:14"/>They return at evening;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they growl like a dog and go around the city.
<verse eid="PSA 59:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 59:15"/>They, they wander around to eat.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If they are not full, then they lodge.
<verse eid="PSA 59:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 59:16"/>But I, I will sing {about} your strength,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will sing aloud in the morning {about} your covenant faithfulness!
</para>
  <para style="q1">For you are a stronghold to me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a refuge in the day of trouble to me.
<verse eid="PSA 59:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 59:17"/>Let me make music to you, my strength,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for God {is} my stronghold, the God of my covenant faithfulness.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 59:17"/><verse eid="PSA 59:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 59"/>
  <chapter number="60" style="c" sid="PSA 60"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on “The Lily.” A testimony. A miktam of David, for teaching. When he fought with Aram Naharaim and with Aram Zobah, and Joab returned and struck Edom in the Valley of Salt, 12, 000.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 60:1"/>God, you have rejected us; you have broken through us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have become angry; restore us!
<verse eid="PSA 60:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 60:2"/>You have made the earth tremble; you have broken it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Heal its breaches, for it shakes.
<verse eid="PSA 60:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 60:3"/>You have made your people see the difficult.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have made us drink the wine of staggering.
<verse eid="PSA 60:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 60:4"/>You have given a banner to the ones fearing you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to be displayed from the face of the bow.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 60:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 60:5"/>So that your beloved may be delivered,
</para>
  <para style="q2">save {us} {with} your right hand and answer me.
<verse eid="PSA 60:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 60:6"/>God has spoken in his holiness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“I will rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I divide Shechem and measure out the Valley of Succoth.
<verse eid="PSA 60:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 60:7"/>To me {is} Gilead, and to me {is} Manasseh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">And Ephraim {is} the protection of my head; Judah, my scepter.
<verse eid="PSA 60:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 60:8"/>Moab is the tub of my washing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Over Edom I throw my sandal.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Over me, Philistia, shout triumphantly.”
<verse eid="PSA 60:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 60:9"/>Who will bring me {into} the city of fortification?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Who will lead me to Edom?
<verse eid="PSA 60:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 60:10"/>You, God, have you not rejected us?
</para>
  <para style="q2">And you do not go out with our armies, God.
<verse eid="PSA 60:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 60:11"/>Give help against the enemy to us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the salvation of man {is} futility.
<verse eid="PSA 60:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 60:12"/>With God we will do valor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for he, he will trample our adversaries.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 60:12"/><verse eid="PSA 60:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 60"/>
  <chapter number="61" style="c" sid="PSA 61"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on a stringed instrument. Of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 61:1"/>Hear my cry, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">listen {to} my prayer.
<verse eid="PSA 61:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 61:2"/>From the end of the earth I call to you when my heart is faint.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lead me to the rock {that} is higher than me.
<verse eid="PSA 61:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 61:3"/>For you are a refuge to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a strong tower from the face of the enemy.
<verse eid="PSA 61:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 61:4"/>Let me sojourn in your tent forever!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will take refuge in the shelter of your wings.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 61:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 61:5"/>For you, God, have listened to my vows.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have given {me} the inheritance of the fearers of your name.
<verse eid="PSA 61:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 61:6"/>Days upon days of the king, may you add {to} his years,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as generation and generation.
<verse eid="PSA 61:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 61:7"/>May he dwell forever to the face of God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Appoint covenant faithfulness and truth; may they preserve him.
<verse eid="PSA 61:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 61:8"/>Thus let me make music {to} your name forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I may pay my vows day, day.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 61:8"/><verse eid="PSA 61:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 61"/>
  <chapter number="62" style="c" sid="PSA 62"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on Jeduthun. A psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 62:1"/>Truly toward God my soul {is in} silence.
</para>
  <para style="q2">From him {is} my salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 62:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 62:2"/>He alone {is} my rock and my salvation, my stronghold.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not be greatly shaken.
<verse eid="PSA 62:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 62:3"/>Until when will you shout at a man?
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will be smashed, all of you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a leaning wall, an overthrown fence.
<verse eid="PSA 62:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 62:4"/>They consult only to cast {him} down from his elevation.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They delight {in} a lie;
</para>
  <para style="q1">with his mouth, they bless,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but in their inside, they curse.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 62:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 62:5"/>Be silent, my soul, toward God alone,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for my hope is from him.
<verse eid="PSA 62:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 62:6"/>He alone {is} my rock and my salvation, my stronghold.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not be shaken.
<verse eid="PSA 62:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 62:7"/>In God {is} my salvation and my glory;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the rock of my strength, my refuge, {is} in God.
<verse eid="PSA 62:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 62:8"/>Trust in him in every time, people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Pour out your heart to his face.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God {is} a refuge for us.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 62:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 62:9"/>Surely sons of a human {are} vapor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">sons of a man {are} a lie.
</para>
  <para style="q1">To go up on the scales,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they together {would be lighter} than vapor.
<verse eid="PSA 62:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 62:10"/>Do not trust in oppression,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not hope vainly in robbery.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Wealth, if it increases, do not set the heart.
<verse eid="PSA 62:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 62:11"/>Once God has spoken, twice I have heard this,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that power {is} to God.
<verse eid="PSA 62:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 62:12"/>Also to you, Lord, {is} covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you, you repay to a man according to his doing.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 62:12"/><verse eid="PSA 62:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 62"/>
  <chapter number="63" style="c" sid="PSA 63"/>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David, when he was in the wilderness of Judah.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 63:1"/>God, you {are} my God. I seek you earnestly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">My soul thirsts for you, my flesh faints for you
</para>
  <para style="q2">in a land of dryness and weary, without water.
<verse eid="PSA 63:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 63:2"/>Thus in the sanctuary I have gazed {at} you
</para>
  <para style="q2">to see your power and your glory.
<verse eid="PSA 63:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 63:3"/>Because your covenant faithfulness {is} better than life,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my lips will praise you.
<verse eid="PSA 63:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 63:4"/>Thus I will bless you in my life;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will lift up my palms in your name.
<verse eid="PSA 63:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 63:5"/>As {with} fat and fatness my soul will be full,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {with} lips of joyful shouts my mouth will praise {you}.
<verse eid="PSA 63:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 63:6"/>When I remember you on my bed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I meditate on you in the night watches.
<verse eid="PSA 63:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 63:7"/>For you have been a help to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in the shadow of your wings I shout joyfully.
<verse eid="PSA 63:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 63:8"/>My soul clings after you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your right hand upholds me.
<verse eid="PSA 63:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 63:9"/>But they, they seek my life for devastation;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will come into the lowest parts of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 63:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 63:10"/>They will pour him into the hands of the sword;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will be a portion of jackals.
<verse eid="PSA 63:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 63:11"/>But the king will rejoice in God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of the swearers by him will exult,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the mouth of speakers of falsehood will be shut.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 63:11"/><verse eid="PSA 63:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 63"/>
  <chapter number="64" style="c" sid="PSA 64"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 64:1"/>Hear my voice, God, in my complaint.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Preserve my life from fear of the enemy.
<verse eid="PSA 64:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 64:2"/>Hide me from the council of evildoers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the throng of the workers of iniquity,
<verse eid="PSA 64:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 64:3"/>who have sharpened their tongue like a sword.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They tread their arrow, a bitter word,
<verse eid="PSA 64:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 64:4"/>to shoot the innocent from secret places;
</para>
  <para style="q2">suddenly they shoot, and they do not fear.
<verse eid="PSA 64:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 64:5"/>They strengthen for themselves an evil matter;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they recount hiding snares.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They say, “Who will see them?”
<verse eid="PSA 64:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 64:6"/>They devise iniquities.
</para>
  <para style="q2">“We have perfected a well-devised device!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">Both the inside of man and the heart {are} deep.
<verse eid="PSA 64:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 64:7"/>But God will shoot an arrow;
</para>
  <para style="q2">suddenly their wounds will happen.
<verse eid="PSA 64:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 64:8"/>And they will make it stumble over them, their tongue.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everyone seeing them will flee.
<verse eid="PSA 64:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 64:9"/>And all of mankind will fear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will declare the work of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for they will consider his deed.
<verse eid="PSA 64:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 64:10"/>The righteous will rejoice in Yahweh and take refuge in him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of the upright of heart will celebrate.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 64:10"/><verse eid="PSA 64:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 64"/>
  <chapter number="65" style="c" sid="PSA 65"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A psalm of David. A song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 65:1"/>Praise {is in} silence toward you, God, in Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to you a vow will be paid.
<verse eid="PSA 65:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 65:2"/>Hearer of prayer,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to you all flesh will come.
<verse eid="PSA 65:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 65:3"/>Matters of iniquities prevail against me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">our transgressions, you, you cover them.
<verse eid="PSA 65:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 65:4"/>The happinesses of {the one} you choose and bring near,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that he may dwell {in} your courts!
</para>
  <para style="q1">May we be full of the goodness of your house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the holiness of your temple.
<verse eid="PSA 65:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 65:5"/>Doing fearsome things, you answer us in righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">God of our salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the confidence of all of the ends of the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the distant seas,
<verse eid="PSA 65:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 65:6"/>the one establishing mountains by his strength,
</para>
  <para style="q2">being girded with might;
<verse eid="PSA 65:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 65:7"/>the one stilling the roar of the seas,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the roar of their waves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the tumult of the peoples.
<verse eid="PSA 65:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 65:8"/>And the dwellers of the ends fear at your signs;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you make the goings forth of the morning and the evening shout joyfully.
<verse eid="PSA 65:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 65:9"/>You visit the earth and saturate it;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you greatly enrich it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The channel of God {is} full of water;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you prepare their grain,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for thus you prepare it.
<verse eid="PSA 65:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 65:10"/>Watering its furrows,
</para>
  <para style="q2">settling its ridges,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you soften it with showers;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you bless its growth.
<verse eid="PSA 65:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 65:11"/>You crown the year {with} your goodness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your tracks drip fatness.
<verse eid="PSA 65:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 65:12"/>The pastures of the wilderness drip,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the hills gird on rejoicing.
<verse eid="PSA 65:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 65:13"/>The meadows put on a flock,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the valleys cover {themselves} {with} grain.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They shout joyfully;
</para>
  <para style="q2">indeed, they sing.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 65:13"/><verse eid="PSA 65:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 65"/>
  <chapter number="66" style="c" sid="PSA 66"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 66:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; a song; a psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Shout to God, all of the earth!
<verse eid="PSA 66:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 66:2"/>Make music {to} the glory of his name;
</para>
  <para style="q2">make his praise glorious.
<verse eid="PSA 66:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 66:3"/>Say to God, “How fearsome {are} your deeds!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because of the greatness of your power, your enemies cringe before you.
<verse eid="PSA 66:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 66:4"/>All of the earth bows down to you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and makes music to you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they make music {to} your name.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 66:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 66:5"/>Come and see the works of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">fearsome in doing toward the sons of man.
<verse eid="PSA 66:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 66:6"/>He turned the sea into dry land;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they passed through the river on foot.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There let us rejoice in him!
<verse eid="PSA 66:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 66:7"/>He is ruling by his might forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his eyes watch over the nations.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let the ones rebelling not exalt themselves.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 66:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 66:8"/>Bless our God, peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make the sound of his praise heard,
<verse eid="PSA 66:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 66:9"/>the one putting our soul among the living,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he does not allow our foot to slip.
<verse eid="PSA 66:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 66:10"/>For you tested us, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you refined us like the refining of silver.
<verse eid="PSA 66:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 66:11"/>You brought us into a net;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you put pressure on our loins.
<verse eid="PSA 66:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 66:12"/>You made man ride over our head;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we went through fire and through waters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you brought us out to abundance.
<verse eid="PSA 66:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 66:13"/>I will come {into} your house with burnt offerings;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will pay my vows to you,
<verse eid="PSA 66:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 66:14"/>{for} which my lips opened
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my mouth spoke when trouble {was} to me.
<verse eid="PSA 66:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 66:15"/>I will offer up burnt offerings of fatlings to you
</para>
  <para style="q2">with the smoke of rams;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will offer cattle with male goats.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 66:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 66:16"/>Come, listen, and let me recount,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all fearers of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">what he has done for my soul.
<verse eid="PSA 66:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 66:17"/>I called to him {with} my mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he was exalted from my tongue.
<verse eid="PSA 66:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 66:18"/>If I had regarded iniquity in my heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Lord would not have heard.
<verse eid="PSA 66:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 66:19"/>Surely God has heard;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has attended to the voice of my prayer.
<verse eid="PSA 66:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 66:20"/>Blessed {be} God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who has not turned away my prayer
</para>
  <para style="q2">or his covenant faithfulness from me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 66:20"/><verse eid="PSA 66:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 66"/>
  <chapter number="67" style="c" sid="PSA 67"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on stringed instruments. A psalm. A song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 67:1"/>May God be gracious to us and bless us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may he make his face shine on us,
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 67:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 67:2"/>for the knowing of your way on the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">your salvation among all of the nations.
<verse eid="PSA 67:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 67:3"/>May the peoples thank you, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may the peoples thank you, all of them.
<verse eid="PSA 67:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 67:4"/>May the nations rejoice and shout joyfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you judge the peoples {with} uprightness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the nations on the earth, you guide them.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 67:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 67:5"/>May the peoples thank you, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may the peoples thank you, all of them.
<verse eid="PSA 67:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 67:6"/>The earth has given its produce;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may God, our God, bless us.
<verse eid="PSA 67:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 67:7"/>May God bless us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may all of the ends of the earth fear him.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 67:7"/><verse eid="PSA 67:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 67"/>
  <chapter number="68" style="c" sid="PSA 68"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. A psalm of David. A song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 68:1"/>Let God arise, let his enemies scatter,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let the ones hating him flee from his face.
<verse eid="PSA 68:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 68:2"/>As smoke is driven away, drive {them} away;
</para>
  <para style="q2">as wax melts from the face of fire,
</para>
  <para style="q2">let the wicked perish from the face of God.
<verse eid="PSA 68:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 68:3"/>But let the righteous rejoice, let them exult to the face of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let them be glad with rejoicing.
<verse eid="PSA 68:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 68:4"/>Sing to God, make music {to} his name,
</para>
  <para style="q2">lift up to the one riding over the plains.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In Yah {is} his name; yes, exult to his face.
<verse eid="PSA 68:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 68:5"/>A father of orphans and a judge of widows
</para>
  <para style="q2">{is} God in the abode of his holiness.
<verse eid="PSA 68:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 68:6"/>God is making the lonely dwell in a house;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is bringing out prisoners into prosperity.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But the ones rebelling dwell in dryness.
<verse eid="PSA 68:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 68:7"/>God, when you went out to the face of your people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">when you marched in the wilderness,
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 68:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 68:8"/>the earth quaked; indeed, the heavens dripped
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the face of God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">this Sinai, from the face of God, the God of Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 68:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 68:9"/>A rain of generosities you shook out, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your inheritance, when it was wearied, you, you established it.
<verse eid="PSA 68:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 68:10"/>Your flock dwelt in it;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in your goodness, you prepared for the poor, God.
<verse eid="PSA 68:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 68:11"/>The Lord utters the word;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the {women} proclaiming good news {are} a great army.
<verse eid="PSA 68:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 68:12"/>Kings of armies flee, they flee,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the habitation of the house, she divides the spoil.
<verse eid="PSA 68:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 68:13"/>Though you lie down between the sheepfolds,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the wings of a dove covered with silver
</para>
  <para style="q2">and its feathers, with greenness of gold.
<verse eid="PSA 68:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 68:14"/>When Shaddai scattered kings in it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it snowed on Zalmon.
<verse eid="PSA 68:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 68:15"/>Mount Bashan {is} a mountain of God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Mount Bashan {is} a mountain of peaks.
<verse eid="PSA 68:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 68:16"/>Why do you look enviously, mountains, peaks,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{at} the mountain God desired for his dwelling?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, Yahweh will inhabit {it} forever.
<verse eid="PSA 68:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 68:17"/>The chariotry of God {is} two myriads, thousands of repetition.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The Lord {is} among them; Sinai {is} in the holy {place}.
<verse eid="PSA 68:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 68:18"/>You have ascended to the height,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have taken captivity captive,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have received gifts among men
</para>
  <para style="q2">and even {among} the ones rebelling,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that Yah God might dwell {there}.
<verse eid="PSA 68:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 68:19"/>Blessed {be} the Lord! Day, day he bears for us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the God of our salvation.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 68:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 68:20"/>God {is} to us a God of salvations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to Yahweh the Lord {are} exits from death.
<verse eid="PSA 68:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 68:21"/>Surely God will crush the head of his enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the pate of hair of the one walking ahead in his trespasses.
<verse eid="PSA 68:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 68:22"/>The Lord said, “I will bring back from Bashan,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will bring back from the depths of the sea,
<verse eid="PSA 68:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 68:23"/>so that your foot may smash in blood,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the tongue of your dogs, its portion from the enemies.”
<verse eid="PSA 68:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 68:24"/>They see your processions, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the processions of my God, my king, into the holy {place}.
<verse eid="PSA 68:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 68:25"/>The singers go ahead; the ones playing stringed instruments, behind,
</para>
  <para style="q2">maidens playing timbrels, in the midst.
<verse eid="PSA 68:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 68:26"/>Bless God in the assemblies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, from the fountain of Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 68:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 68:27"/>There {is} Benjamin, the littlest,
</para>
  <para style="q2">ruling them; the princes of Judah, their throngs;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the princes of Zebulun, the princes of Naphtali.
<verse eid="PSA 68:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 68:28"/>Your God has commanded your strength.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Be strong, God! You have done this for us.
<verse eid="PSA 68:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 68:29"/>Because of your temple over Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">kings will bring a gift to you.
<verse eid="PSA 68:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 68:30"/>Rebuke the beast of the reed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the assembly of the mighty with the calves of the peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q2">humbling himself with pieces of silver.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He scatters the peoples {who} delight in battles.
<verse eid="PSA 68:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 68:31"/>Nobles will come from Egypt;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Cush will make its hands run to God.
<verse eid="PSA 68:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 68:32"/>Kingdoms of the earth, sing to God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Make music {to} the Lord,
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 68:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 68:33"/>to the rider on the heavens, of the heavens of antiquity.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Behold, he utters with his voice, a voice of power.
<verse eid="PSA 68:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 68:34"/>Ascribe strength to God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his majesty {is} over Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his strength {is} in the clouds.
<verse eid="PSA 68:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 68:35"/>God, {you are} fearsome from your sanctuary!
</para>
  <para style="q2">The God of Israel, he is giving strength and forces to the people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Blessed {be} God!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 68:35"/><verse eid="PSA 68:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 68"/>
  <chapter number="69" style="c" sid="PSA 69"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on “Lilies”; of David
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 69:1"/>Save me, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for waters have come up to {my} life.
<verse eid="PSA 69:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 69:2"/>I have sunk in mire of depth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is no standing.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have come into depths of waters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a flood overflows me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 69:3"/>I am weary in my calling out;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my throat is parched.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My eyes fail
</para>
  <para style="q2">{as} I am waiting for my God.
<verse eid="PSA 69:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 69:4"/>The ones hating me gratuitously
</para>
  <para style="q2">are more than the hairs of my head.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The ones destroying me are mighty,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my enemies of falsehood.
</para>
  <para style="q1">What I did not steal,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yet I must restore.
<verse eid="PSA 69:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 69:5"/>God, you, you know my foolishness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my sins are not hidden from you.
<verse eid="PSA 69:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 69:6"/>May the ones waiting for you not have shame because of me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lord Yahweh of Armies.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May the ones seeking you not be humiliated because of me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">God of Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 69:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 69:7"/>For because of you I have borne reproach;
</para>
  <para style="q2">humiliation has covered my face.
<verse eid="PSA 69:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 69:8"/>I have become a stranger to my brothers
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a foreigner to the sons of my mother.
<verse eid="PSA 69:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 69:9"/>For zeal for your house has consumed me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the reproaches of the ones reproaching you have fallen on me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 69:10"/>Though I wept {in} my soul with fasting,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yet it became reproaches to me;
<verse eid="PSA 69:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 69:11"/>though I made my clothing sackcloth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yet I became a proverb to them.
<verse eid="PSA 69:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 69:12"/>The sitters at the gate speak about me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the songs of the drinkers of beer.
<verse eid="PSA 69:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 69:13"/>But I, my prayer {is} to you, Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{At} a time of favor, God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the greatness of your covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">answer me in the truth of your salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 69:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 69:14"/>Deliver me from the mire, and let me not sink.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let me be delivered from the ones hating me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from the depths of the waters.
<verse eid="PSA 69:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 69:15"/>Let the flood of waters not overflow me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let the deep not swallow me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let the pit not close its mouth over me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 69:16"/>Answer me, Yahweh, for your covenant faithfulness {is} good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">according to the greatness of your compassion, turn to me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 69:17"/>And may you not hide your face from your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for trouble {is} to me; hurry, answer me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 69:18"/>Draw near to my soul, redeem it;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of my enemies, ransom me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 69:19"/>You, you know my reproach
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my shame and my humiliation.
</para>
  <para style="q1">All of my adversaries {are} before you.
<verse eid="PSA 69:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 69:20"/>Reproach has broken my heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am sick.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Though I waited for sympathy, yet there was none,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for comforters, yet I did not find.
<verse eid="PSA 69:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 69:21"/>But they put gall in my food,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they made me drink vinegar for my thirst.
<verse eid="PSA 69:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 69:22"/>Let their table become a snare to their faces
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a trap for their welfare.
<verse eid="PSA 69:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 69:23"/>Let their eyes darken from seeing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make their loins tremble continually.
<verse eid="PSA 69:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 69:24"/>Pour your indignation on them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let the burning of your nose overtake them.
<verse eid="PSA 69:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 69:25"/>Let their encampment be deserted;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let there not be a dweller in their tents.
<verse eid="PSA 69:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 69:26"/>For you, whom you have struck, they have persecuted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they talk about the pain of your wounded.
<verse eid="PSA 69:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 69:27"/>Add iniquity to their iniquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let them not come into your righteousness.
<verse eid="PSA 69:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 69:28"/>Let them be wiped from the book of the living,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let them not be written with the righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 69:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 69:29"/>But I {am} poor and feeling pain;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may your salvation, God, set me on high.
<verse eid="PSA 69:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 69:30"/>I will praise the name of God with a song,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will magnify him with thanksgiving.
<verse eid="PSA 69:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 69:31"/>And this will be better to Yahweh than an ox,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a bull having horns and having hooves.
<verse eid="PSA 69:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 69:32"/>The poor will see, they will rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">seekers of God, let your heart live.
<verse eid="PSA 69:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 69:33"/>For Yahweh is hearing the needy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he does not despise his prisoners.
<verse eid="PSA 69:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 69:34"/>Let the heavens and the earth praise him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the seas and everything moving in them.
<verse eid="PSA 69:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 69:35"/>For God will save Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will build the cities of Judah,
</para>
  <para style="q1">that they may dwell there and possess it.
<verse eid="PSA 69:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 69:36"/>And the seed of his servants will inherit it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the ones loving his name will dwell in it.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 69:36"/><verse eid="PSA 69:36"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 69"/>
  <chapter number="70" style="c" sid="PSA 70"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. Of David. To cause to remember.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 70:1"/>Hurry, God, to deliver me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, to my help!
<verse eid="PSA 70:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 70:2"/>Let the ones seeking my life have shame and have confusion;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let the ones delighting in my harm be turned back and disgraced.
<verse eid="PSA 70:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 70:3"/>Let them turn back on account of their shame,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones saying, “Aha! Aha!”
<verse eid="PSA 70:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 70:4"/>Let all of the seekers of you rejoice and be glad in you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let the lovers of your salvation say continually, “God is great!”
<verse eid="PSA 70:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 70:5"/>But I {am} poor and needy;
</para>
  <para style="q2">God, hurry to me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">You {are} my help and my deliverer;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, do not delay!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 70:5"/><verse eid="PSA 70:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 70"/>
  <chapter number="71" style="c" sid="PSA 71"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 71:1"/>In you, Yahweh, I take refuge;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let me not ever have shame.
<verse eid="PSA 71:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 71:2"/>In your righteousness, deliver me and rescue me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">incline your ear to me and save me.
<verse eid="PSA 71:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 71:3"/>Be to me a rock of abode for coming continually;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you command to save me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you {are} my rock and my stronghold.
<verse eid="PSA 71:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 71:4"/>My God, rescue me from the hand of the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the palm of the one doing wrong and the one being cruel;
<verse eid="PSA 71:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 71:5"/>for you {are} my hope, Lord Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my confidence from my youth.
<verse eid="PSA 71:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 71:6"/>I have supported myself on you from the womb;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you were taking me from the belly of my mother.
</para>
  <para style="q2">My praise {is} about you continually.
<verse eid="PSA 71:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 71:7"/>I have become like a wonder to many,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you {are} my refuge of strength.
<verse eid="PSA 71:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 71:8"/>Let my mouth be filled {with} your praise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of the day {with} your splendor.
<verse eid="PSA 71:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 71:9"/>May you not cast me away in the time of old age;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may you not forsake me when my strength fails.
<verse eid="PSA 71:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 71:10"/>For my enemies have spoken against me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the ones watching my life have consulted together,
<verse eid="PSA 71:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 71:11"/>saying, “God has forsaken him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">pursue and seize him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for there is none delivering.”
<verse eid="PSA 71:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 71:12"/>God, may you not be far from me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my God, hasten to my help.
<verse eid="PSA 71:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 71:13"/>Let them shame and finish, the adversaries of my life;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let them cover {with} reproach and disgrace, the ones seeking my harm.
<verse eid="PSA 71:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 71:14"/>But I, I will hope continually,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will add to all of your praise.
<verse eid="PSA 71:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 71:15"/>My mouth will recount your righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of the day, your salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I do not know the numbers.
<verse eid="PSA 71:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 71:16"/>I will come in the forces of Lord Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will remember your righteousness, yours alone.
<verse eid="PSA 71:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 71:17"/>God, you have taught me from my youth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to this I declare your wonderful doings.
<verse eid="PSA 71:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 71:18"/>And also until old age and gray hair,
</para>
  <para style="q2">God, do not forsake me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">until I declare your arm to a generation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">your might to everyone {who} will come.
<verse eid="PSA 71:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 71:19"/>For your righteousness, God, {is} to height,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{you} who do great {things};
</para>
  <para style="q2">God, who {is} like you?
<verse eid="PSA 71:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 71:20"/>{You} who have made me see many and evil troubles,
</para>
  <para style="q2">may you return, may you revive me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may you return, may you bring me up from the depths of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 71:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 71:21"/>May you increase my greatness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may you turn around, may you comfort me.
<verse eid="PSA 71:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 71:22"/>Also I, I will praise you with the instrument of the lute
</para>
  <para style="q2">{for} your faithfulness, my God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let me make music to you with the harp, Holy {One} of Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 71:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 71:23"/>My lips will shout joyfully when I make music to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my soul, which you have redeemed.
<verse eid="PSA 71:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 71:24"/>Also my tongue will meditate {on} your righteousness all of the day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for they will shame, for they will confound the ones seeking my harm.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 71:24"/><verse eid="PSA 71:24"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 71"/>
  <chapter number="72" style="c" sid="PSA 72"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 72:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of Solomon.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God, give your judgments to the king
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your righteousness to the son of the king.
<verse eid="PSA 72:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 72:2"/>May he judge your people with righteousness
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your poor with justice.
<verse eid="PSA 72:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 72:3"/>May the mountains bring peace to the people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the hills, in righteousness.
<verse eid="PSA 72:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 72:4"/>May he judge the poor of the people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may he save the sons of the needy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may he crush the oppressor.
<verse eid="PSA 72:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 72:5"/>May they fear you with the sun
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to the face of the moon, generation of generations.
<verse eid="PSA 72:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 72:6"/>May he come down like rain on mown grass,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like showers, a drenching of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 72:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 72:7"/>May the righteous flourish in his days,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and abundance of peace until the moon {is} not.
<verse eid="PSA 72:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 72:8"/>May he rule from sea to sea
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from the River to the ends of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 72:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 72:9"/>May desert-dwellers kneel to his face,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may his enemies lick the dust.
<verse eid="PSA 72:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 72:10"/>May the kings of Tarshish and the coastlands return tribute;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may the kings of Sheba and Seba bring near a gift.
<verse eid="PSA 72:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 72:11"/>And may all kings bow down to him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may all nations serve him.
<verse eid="PSA 72:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 72:12"/>For may he deliver the needy crying out
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the poor when no helper {is} to him.
<verse eid="PSA 72:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 72:13"/>May he have pity on the weak and the needy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may he save the lives of the needy.
<verse eid="PSA 72:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 72:14"/>May he redeem their life from oppression and from violence,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may their blood be precious in his eyes.
<verse eid="PSA 72:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 72:15"/>May he live! And may one give to him from the gold of Sheba,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may one pray for him continually;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they bless him all of the day.
<verse eid="PSA 72:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 72:16"/>May there be an abundance of grain in the land;
</para>
  <para style="q2">on the head of the mountains may its fruit sway like Lebanon,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may they flourish from the city like the grass of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 72:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 72:17"/>May his name be forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may his name continue to the face of the sun.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And may they be blessed by him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may all of the nations acclaim him.
<verse eid="PSA 72:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 72:18"/>Blessed {be} Yahweh God, the God of Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one doing wonders, he alone.
<verse eid="PSA 72:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 72:19"/>And blessed {be} the name of his glory forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let all of the earth be filled {with} his glory.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Amen and amen.
<verse eid="PSA 72:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 72:20"/>The prayers of David son of Jesse are finished.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 72:20"/><verse eid="PSA 72:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 72"/>
  <chapter number="73" style="c" sid="PSA 73"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book Three
</para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 73:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of Asaph
</para>
  <para style="q1">Surely God is good to Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to those with a pure heart.
<verse eid="PSA 73:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 73:2"/>But as for me, my feet almost slipped;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my steps almost were caused to slide out {from under me}
<verse eid="PSA 73:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 73:3"/>because I was envious of the arrogant
</para>
  <para style="q1">{when} I saw the prosperity of the wicked.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 73:4"/>For {they have} no ropes until their death,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their belly is fat.
<verse eid="PSA 73:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 73:5"/>They {are} free from the trouble of man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with {the rest of} man they are not afflicted.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 73:6"/>Therefore pride is a necklace for them;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a garment of violence covers them.
<verse eid="PSA 73:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 73:7"/>Their eyes bulge out from fatness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the imaginations of {their} heart overflow.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 73:8"/>They mock and speak with evil of oppression;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they speak from an elevated place.
<verse eid="PSA 73:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 73:9"/>They set their mouth in the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their tongue goes through the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 73:10"/>Therefore his people turn here,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and waters of a full {cup} are drained by them.
<verse eid="PSA 73:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 73:11"/>And they say, “How does God know?
</para>
  <para style="q1">And is there knowledge in the Most High?”
<verse eid="PSA 73:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 73:12"/>Behold, these wicked;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they are always at ease, they increase in wealth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 73:13"/>Surely in vain I have kept my heart clean
</para>
  <para style="q1">and washed my hands in innocence.
<verse eid="PSA 73:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 73:14"/>For I have been stricken all of the day
</para>
  <para style="q1">and punished every morning.
<verse eid="PSA 73:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 73:15"/>If I had said, “I will recount such things,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">behold, I would have betrayed the generation of your children.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 73:16"/>And {when} I thought {how} to understand this,
</para>
  <para style="q1">it {was} troublesome in my eyes
<verse eid="PSA 73:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 73:17"/>until I went into the sanctuaries of God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{then} I discerned their end.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 73:18"/>Surely you set them in slippery places;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you make them fall to destruction.
<verse eid="PSA 73:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 73:19"/>How they are {brought} to desolation as in a moment!
</para>
  <para style="q1">They come to an end, they perish by terrors.
<verse eid="PSA 73:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 73:20"/>Like a dream after {one} awakes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Lord, when you rouse {yourself}, you will despise their image.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 73:21"/>When my heart was embittered,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I was pierced in my kidneys,
<verse eid="PSA 73:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 73:22"/>I {was} stupid and I was not knowing;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I was an animal with you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 73:23"/>Yet I {am} continuously with you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you hold {me} by my right hand.
<verse eid="PSA 73:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 73:24"/>You guide me with your counsel,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and afterward you will take me {to} glory.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 73:25"/>Whom have I in heaven {but you}?
</para>
  <para style="q1">And besides you {there is} nothing on the earth I desire.
<verse eid="PSA 73:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 73:26"/>My flesh and my heart fail,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{but} God {is} the rock of my heart and my portion forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 73:27"/>For behold, those who are far from you will perish;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you destroy every one being unfaithful to you.
<verse eid="PSA 73:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 73:28"/>But {for} me, the closeness of God for me {is} good.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have made the Lord, Yahweh, my refuge
</para>
  <para style="q1">in order to recount all your works.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 73:28"/><verse eid="PSA 73:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 73"/>
  <chapter number="74" style="c" sid="PSA 74"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 74:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A maskil. Of Asaph.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Why, God, have you rejected {us} forever?
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Why} does your nose smoke against the flock of your pasture?
<verse eid="PSA 74:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 74:2"/>Remember your congregation {that} you acquired {in} antiquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{which} you redeemed, the tribe of your inheritance,
</para>
  <para style="q2">this Mount Zion on which you have dwelt.
<verse eid="PSA 74:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 74:3"/>Lift up your feet to the destructions of perpetuity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{to} all the enemy has damaged in the holy place.
<verse eid="PSA 74:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 74:4"/>Your adversaries roared in the midst of your meeting place;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they set up their signs {as} signs.
<verse eid="PSA 74:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 74:5"/>It was known like one bringing upward
</para>
  <para style="q2">axes in a thicket of trees.
<verse eid="PSA 74:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 74:6"/>And now with hatchet and hammers
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have broken down its carvings altogether.
<verse eid="PSA 74:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 74:7"/>They sent your holy place into fire;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they profaned the dwelling of your name to the ground.
<verse eid="PSA 74:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 74:8"/>They said in their heart, “Let us oppress them altogether.”
</para>
  <para style="q2">They burned all of the meeting places of God in the land.
<verse eid="PSA 74:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 74:9"/>We do not see our signs;
</para>
  <para style="q2">there is no longer a prophet
</para>
  <para style="q2">and not one with us knowing until when.
<verse eid="PSA 74:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 74:10"/>Until when, God, will the adversary reproach?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Will the enemy despise your name forever?
<verse eid="PSA 74:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 74:11"/>Why do you hold back your hand, even your right hand?
</para>
  <para style="q2">From the midst of your bosom finish {them}!
<verse eid="PSA 74:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 74:12"/>But God {is} my king from antiquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">working salvations in the midst of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 74:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 74:13"/>You, you divided the sea by your strength;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you broke the heads of the sea monsters in the waters.
<verse eid="PSA 74:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 74:14"/>You, you crushed the heads of Leviathan;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you gave him {as} food to a people, to the desert-dwellers.
<verse eid="PSA 74:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 74:15"/>You, you split open spring and wadi;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you, you dry up perpetual rivers.
<verse eid="PSA 74:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 74:16"/>The day {is} to you; the night {is} also to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You, you established the light and the sun.
<verse eid="PSA 74:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 74:17"/>You, you set all of the boundaries of the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">summer and winter, you, you formed them.
<verse eid="PSA 74:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 74:18"/>Remember this: the enemy has reproached Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a foolish people has despised your name.
<verse eid="PSA 74:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 74:19"/>May you not give the life of your dove to a beast;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may you not forget the life of your poor forever.
<verse eid="PSA 74:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 74:20"/>Regard the covenant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for pastures of violence fill the dark places of the land.
<verse eid="PSA 74:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 74:21"/>May the weak not return ashamed;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may the poor and the needy praise your name.
<verse eid="PSA 74:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 74:22"/>Arise, God! Plead your case!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Remember your reproach from the fool all of the day.
<verse eid="PSA 74:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 74:23"/>Do not forget the voice of your adversaries,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the uproar of the ones rising against you, going up continually.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 74:23"/><verse eid="PSA 74:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 74"/>
  <chapter number="75" style="c" sid="PSA 75"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; “May You Not Destroy.” A psalm of Asaph; a song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 75:1"/>We give thanks to you, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we give thanks, and your name is near;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they recount your wonders.

<verse eid="PSA 75:1"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 75:2"/>When I take the appointed time;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I, I will judge {with} equity.
<verse eid="PSA 75:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 75:3"/>The earth and all its inhabitants are melting;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I, I established its pillars.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 75:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 75:4"/>I said to the boasters, “Do not boast,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to the wicked, “Do not lift up a horn.
<verse eid="PSA 75:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 75:5"/>Do not lift up your horn to the height,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or speak with an arrogant neck.”

<verse eid="PSA 75:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 75:6"/>For not from the east or from the west,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and not from the wilderness {comes} lifting up.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 75:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 75:7"/>For God {is} the judge;
</para>
  <para style="q2">this one he brings low, and this one he lifts up.
<verse eid="PSA 75:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 75:8"/>For a cup {is} in the hand of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the wine foams, a full mixture,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he pours out from this;
</para>
  <para style="q2">surely its dregs they will drain;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all the wicked of the earth will drink.

<verse eid="PSA 75:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 75:9"/>But I, I will declare to eternity;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing praise to the God of Jacob.

<verse eid="PSA 75:9"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 75:10"/>“And all the horns of the wicked I will cut off;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the horns of the righteous will be lifted up.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 75:10"/><verse eid="PSA 75:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 75"/>
  <chapter number="76" style="c" sid="PSA 76"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on stringed instruments. A psalm of Asaph, a song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 76:1"/>In Judah God is known;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in Israel his name is great.
<verse eid="PSA 76:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 76:2"/>And his abode is in Salem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his dwelling place is in Zion.
<verse eid="PSA 76:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 76:3"/>There he broke the flames of the bow,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the shield, and the sword, and the battle.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 76:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 76:4"/>You are shining, majestic,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the mountains of prey.
<verse eid="PSA 76:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 76:5"/>The stout of heart were plundered;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they slept their sleep,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of the men of strength found not their hands.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 76:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 76:6"/>At your rebuke, O God of Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">both rider and horse fell deeply asleep.

<verse eid="PSA 76:6"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 76:7"/>You, you are to be feared,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and who can stand before your face from the time of your nose?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 76:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 76:8"/>From heaven you caused judgment to be heard;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the earth feared and was quiet
<verse eid="PSA 76:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 76:9"/>when God arose to judgment,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to save all the humble of the earth.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 76:9"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 76:10"/>For the wrath of man will thank you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the remainder of wrath you will gird on.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 76:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 76:11"/>Vow and pay to Yahweh your God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let all who are around him bring a gift to the Fear.
<verse eid="PSA 76:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 76:12"/>He cuts off the spirit of princes;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is to be feared by the kings of the earth.


<verse eid="PSA 76:12"/><verse eid="PSA 76:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 76"/>
  <chapter number="77" style="c" sid="PSA 77"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on Jeduthun; a psalm of Asaph.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 77:1"/>My voice {is} to God, and I cry out;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my voice {is} to God, and he listens to me.
<verse eid="PSA 77:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 77:2"/>In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my hand was stretched out at night, and it did not slacken.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My soul refused to be comforted.
<verse eid="PSA 77:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 77:3"/>I remembered God and I groaned;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I meditated, and my spirit grew faint.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 77:4"/>You held the lids of my eyes;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I was troubled and I did not speak.
<verse eid="PSA 77:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 77:5"/>I thought about days from antiquity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">years of long ago.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 77:6"/>I will remember my song in the night;
</para>
  <para style="q2">with my heart I will meditate,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my spirit searches.
<verse eid="PSA 77:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 77:7"/>Will the Lord reject {me} forever?
</para>
  <para style="q2">And will he not again add to show favor?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 77:8"/>Has his covenant faithfulness ceased forever?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Has a promise ended for generation and generation?
<verse eid="PSA 77:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 77:9"/>Has God forgotten to be gracious?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Or has he shut up his compassions in {his} nose?
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 77:10"/>And I said, “This is my wounding:
</para>
  <para style="q2">the changing of the right hand of the Most High.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 77:11"/>I will remember the deeds of Yah;
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I will remember your wonder from antiquity.
<verse eid="PSA 77:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 77:12"/>And I will ponder on all your deeds,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on your works I will meditate.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 77:13"/>Your way, God, is in holiness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">what god is great like God?
<verse eid="PSA 77:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 77:14"/>You are the God who does wonders;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have revealed your strength among the peoples.
<verse eid="PSA 77:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 77:15"/>You have redeemed your people with {your} arm,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the sons of Jacob and Joseph.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 77:16"/>The waters saw you, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the waters saw you, and they trembled;
</para>
  <para style="q2">indeed the depths shook.
<verse eid="PSA 77:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 77:17"/>The clouds poured down water;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the skies gave a sound;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your arrows also flew about.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 77:18"/>The sound of your thunder {was} in the whirlwind;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the lightning lit up the world;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the earth trembled and shook.
<verse eid="PSA 77:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 77:19"/>Your way went through the sea
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your path through many waters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but your footprints were not discerned.
<verse eid="PSA 77:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 77:20"/>You led your people like a flock
</para>
  <para style="q2">by the hand of Moses and Aaron.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 77:20"/><verse eid="PSA 77:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 77"/>
  <chapter number="78" style="c" sid="PSA 78"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 78:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A maskil of Asaph.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hear my teaching, my people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">incline your ears to the words of my mouth.
<verse eid="PSA 78:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 78:2"/>I will open my mouth in a parable;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will pour out riddles from antiquity.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 78:3"/>These are things that we have heard and learned,
</para>
  <para style="q2">things that our fathers have told us.
<verse eid="PSA 78:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 78:4"/>We will not keep them from their descendants.
</para>
  <para style="q1">We will tell the next generation about the praises of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his strength, and his wonders that he has done.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 78:5"/>And he established a testimony in Jacob
</para>
  <para style="q2">and appointed a law in Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q1">which he commanded our fathers
</para>
  <para style="q1">to teach them to their children,
<verse eid="PSA 78:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 78:6"/>So that the later generation might know, the children yet to be born,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will rise up and tell to their children.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 78:7"/>And they would place their confidence in God
</para>
  <para style="q2">and not forget the deeds of God
</para>
  <para style="q2">but keep his commandments.
<verse eid="PSA 78:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 78:8"/>And they would not be like their fathers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a stubborn generation and a rebellious generation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{which} did not cause its heart to be steadfast,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and its spirit was not faithful with God.

<verse eid="PSA 78:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 78:9"/>The sons of Ephraim being armed {with} shooters of bows,
</para>
  <para style="q1">they turned back on the day of battle.
<verse eid="PSA 78:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 78:10"/>They did not keep the covenant of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they refused to walk in his law.
<verse eid="PSA 78:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 78:11"/>And they forgot his deeds,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his wonders that he had shown them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 78:12"/>He did wonders before their fathers
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the land of Egypt, in the territory of Zoan.
<verse eid="PSA 78:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 78:13"/>He divided the sea and led them across it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he made the waters to stand like a heap.
<verse eid="PSA 78:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 78:14"/>And by day he led them with the cloud
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all the night with the light of fire.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 78:15"/>He split open the rocks in the wilderness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he gave drink abundantly as the deep.
<verse eid="PSA 78:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 78:16"/>He made streams flow out of the rock
</para>
  <para style="q1">and made the water flow like rivers.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 78:17"/>And they added still to sin against him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to rebel against the Most High in the dry land.
<verse eid="PSA 78:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 78:18"/>And they tested God in their hearts
</para>
  <para style="q1">by asking {for} food for their appetite.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 78:19"/>And they spoke against God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They said, “Can God arrange a table in the wilderness?
<verse eid="PSA 78:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 78:20"/>Behold, he struck the rock
</para>
  <para style="q2">and waters gushed out
</para>
  <para style="q2">and streams overflowed.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Is he able to give bread also?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Or can he provide meat for his people?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 78:21"/>Therefore, Yahweh heard and was furious,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a fire was kindled against Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and also {his} nose went up against Israel,
<verse eid="PSA 78:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 78:22"/>because they did not believe in God
</para>
  <para style="q2">and did not trust in his salvation.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 78:23"/>Yet he commanded the clouds from above
</para>
  <para style="q2">and opened the doors of the sky.
<verse eid="PSA 78:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 78:24"/>And he rained down manna to eat on them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and gave to them the grain of heaven.
<verse eid="PSA 78:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 78:25"/>Man ate the bread of the mighty.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He sent to them provision to {their} satisfaction.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 78:26"/>He caused the east wind to blow in the sky,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and by his power he guided the south wind.
<verse eid="PSA 78:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 78:27"/>And he rained down meat on them like dust,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and birds of wing as the sands of the sea.
<verse eid="PSA 78:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 78:28"/>And he caused them to fall in the middle of his camp,
</para>
  <para style="q2">around his dwellings.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 78:29"/>And they ate and were very satisfied.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And he brought their craving to them.
<verse eid="PSA 78:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 78:30"/>They were not separated from their craving,
</para>
  <para style="q2">their food was still in their mouth,
<verse eid="PSA 78:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 78:31"/>and the nose of God went up in them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he killed some of their stoutest people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he caused the young men of Israel to bow down.
<verse eid="PSA 78:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 78:32"/>In all this they sinned again,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and did not believe in his wonders.

<verse eid="PSA 78:32"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 78:33"/>So he consumed their days in a vapor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their years in terror.
<verse eid="PSA 78:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 78:34"/>When he killed them, then they would seek him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they would return and look earnestly for God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 78:35"/>And they would remember that God was their rock
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {that} God Most High was their redeemer.
<verse eid="PSA 78:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 78:36"/>And they would deceive him with their mouth
</para>
  <para style="q2">and lie to him with their tongues.
<verse eid="PSA 78:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 78:37"/>And their hearts were not steadfast with him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they were not faithful in his covenant.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 78:38"/>Yet he, {being} merciful, atoned for their iniquity and did not destroy them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">And many times he held back his nose
</para>
  <para style="q2">and did not stir up all his wrath.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 78:39"/>And he remembered that they were flesh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a wind going and it does not return.

<verse eid="PSA 78:39"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 78:40"/>How often they rebelled against him in the wilderness!
</para>
  <para style="q2">They grieved him in the desert!
<verse eid="PSA 78:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 78:41"/>And they returned and they tested God
</para>
  <para style="q2">and grieved the Holy {One} of Israel.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 78:42"/>They did not remember his hand,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the day when he redeemed them from the adversary,
<verse eid="PSA 78:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 78:43"/>when he set his signs in Egypt
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his wonders in the field of Zoan.
<verse eid="PSA 78:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 78:44"/>And he turned their rivers to blood
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their streams they could not drink.
<verse eid="PSA 78:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 78:45"/>He sent a swarm among them, and it devoured them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the frog and it destroyed them.
<verse eid="PSA 78:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 78:46"/>And he gave their produce to the locust
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their labor to the swarming locust.
<verse eid="PSA 78:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 78:47"/>He slew their vines with hail
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their sycamore trees with frost.
<verse eid="PSA 78:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 78:48"/>And he gave over their cattle to the hail
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their livestock to the bolts of lightning.
<verse eid="PSA 78:48"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 78:49"/>He sent among them the burning of his nose,
</para>
  <para style="q2">fury and indignation and distress,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a group of messengers of calamity.
<verse eid="PSA 78:49"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 78:50"/>He made level a path for his anger;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he did not spare their soul from death,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their life he gave over to the plague.
<verse eid="PSA 78:50"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 78:51"/>And he struck every firstborn in Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the beginning of strength in the tents of Ham.
<verse eid="PSA 78:51"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 78:52"/>And he made his people journey like sheep,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he led them like a flock in the wilderness.
<verse eid="PSA 78:52"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="PSA 78:53"/>And he guided them in security, and they did not fear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the sea covered their enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 78:53"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="PSA 78:54"/>And he brought them to the border of his holiness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">this mountain that his right hand acquired.
<verse eid="PSA 78:54"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="PSA 78:55"/>And he drove out nations from before them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and caused them to fall in a portion of inheritance,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he caused the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:55"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="PSA 78:56"/>But they tested and rebelled against God Most High,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they did not keep his testimonies.
<verse eid="PSA 78:56"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="PSA 78:57"/>And they turned back and acted treacherously like their fathers;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they turned themselves like a bow of deceit.
<verse eid="PSA 78:57"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="PSA 78:58"/>And they provoked him to anger with their high places,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and with their carved images they moved him to jealousy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:58"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="PSA 78:59"/>God heard and was furious,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he rejected Israel greatly.
<verse eid="PSA 78:59"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="PSA 78:60"/>And he abandoned the dwelling of Shiloh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the tent {in which} he had dwelt among mankind.
<verse eid="PSA 78:60"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="61" style="v" sid="PSA 78:61"/>And he gave his strength to captivity
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his splendor into the hand of the enemy.
<verse eid="PSA 78:61"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="62" style="v" sid="PSA 78:62"/>And he delivered his people over to the sword,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he was furious with his inheritance.
<verse eid="PSA 78:62"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="63" style="v" sid="PSA 78:63"/>Fire consumed his young men,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his virgins were not praised {in} wedding songs.
<verse eid="PSA 78:63"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="64" style="v" sid="PSA 78:64"/>His priests fell by the sword,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his widows did not weep.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:64"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="65" style="v" sid="PSA 78:65"/>Then the Lord awoke as one sleeping,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as a mighty man shouting from wine.
<verse eid="PSA 78:65"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="66" style="v" sid="PSA 78:66"/>And he struck his adversaries backward;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he gave to them a reproach of perpetuity.
<verse eid="PSA 78:66"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="67" style="v" sid="PSA 78:67"/>And he rejected the tent of Joseph,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he did not choose the tribe of Ephraim.
<verse eid="PSA 78:67"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="68" style="v" sid="PSA 78:68"/>But he chose the tribe of Judah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Mount Zion, which he loved.
<verse eid="PSA 78:68"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="69" style="v" sid="PSA 78:69"/>And he built his sanctuary like the heights,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like the earth he founded it forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:69"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="70" style="v" sid="PSA 78:70"/>And he chose David his servant
</para>
  <para style="q2">and took him from the folds of the flock.
<verse eid="PSA 78:70"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="71" style="v" sid="PSA 78:71"/>From behind the nursing ewes he brought him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to shepherd Jacob his people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Israel his inheritance.
<verse eid="PSA 78:71"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="72" style="v" sid="PSA 78:72"/>And he shepherded them according to the integrity of his heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and with the skillfulness of his hands he guided them.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 78:72"/><verse eid="PSA 78:72"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 78"/>
  <chapter number="79" style="c" sid="PSA 79"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 79:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm. Of Asaph.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God, nations have come into your inheritance;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have defiled the temple of your holiness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have made Jerusalem into heaps.
<verse eid="PSA 79:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 79:2"/>They have given the corpse of your servants {as} food to the bird of the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the flesh of your faithful to the beast of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 79:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 79:3"/>They have poured out their blood like water around Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is no burying.
<verse eid="PSA 79:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 79:4"/>We have become a reproach to our neighbors,
</para>
  <para style="q2">scorn and derision to the ones around us.
<verse eid="PSA 79:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 79:5"/>Until when, Yahweh? Will you be angry forever?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Will your jealousy burn like fire?
<verse eid="PSA 79:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 79:6"/>Pour out your wrath on the nations that have not known you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on the kingdoms that have not called on your name.
<verse eid="PSA 79:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 79:7"/>For one has devoured Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they have desolated his habitation.
<verse eid="PSA 79:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 79:8"/>Do not remember former iniquities against us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">hasten, let your compassions meet us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for we have become very weak.
<verse eid="PSA 79:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 79:9"/>Help us, God of our salvation, on account of the glory of your name, and deliver us
</para>
  <para style="q2">and cover over our sins for the sake of your name.
<verse eid="PSA 79:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 79:10"/>Why should the nations say, “Where {is} their God?”
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let the vengeance of the poured-out blood of your servants
</para>
  <para style="q2">be known among the nations to our eyes.
<verse eid="PSA 79:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 79:11"/>Let the groaning of the prisoner come to your face;
</para>
  <para style="q2">according to the greatness of your arm, preserve the sons of death.
<verse eid="PSA 79:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 79:12"/>And return to our neighbors sevenfold, into their bosom,
</para>
  <para style="q2">their reproach {with} which they have reproached you, Lord.
<verse eid="PSA 79:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 79:13"/>And we, your people and the flock of your pasture,
</para>
  <para style="q2">will give thanks to you forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">to generation and generation we will recount your praise.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 79:13"/><verse eid="PSA 79:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 79"/>
  <chapter number="80" style="c" sid="PSA 80"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on “Lilies.” A testimony. Of Asaph; a psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 80:1"/>Shepherd of Israel, give ear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one leading Joseph like a flock.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Sitter {on} the cherubim, shine forth.
<verse eid="PSA 80:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 80:2"/>To the face of Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasseh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">awaken your might and come to us for salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 80:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 80:3"/>God, restore us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make your face shine and let us be saved.
<verse eid="PSA 80:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 80:4"/>Yahweh, God of armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">until when will you smolder against the prayer of your people?
<verse eid="PSA 80:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 80:5"/>You have made them eat bread of tears,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have made them drink tears {in} triple measure.
<verse eid="PSA 80:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 80:6"/>You have made us strife to our neighbors,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and our enemies mock among themselves.
<verse eid="PSA 80:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 80:7"/>God of armies, restore us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make your face shine and let us be saved.
<verse eid="PSA 80:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 80:8"/>You pulled up a vine from Egypt;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you drove out nations and planted it.
<verse eid="PSA 80:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 80:9"/>You cleared to the face of it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it rooted its roots and filled the land.
<verse eid="PSA 80:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 80:10"/>The mountains were covered {with} its shadow,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and its branches {were} cedars of God.
<verse eid="PSA 80:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 80:11"/>It sent out its branches to the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and its shoots to the River.
<verse eid="PSA 80:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 80:12"/>Why have you broken down its walls,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that all the ones passing {on} the way pluck it?
<verse eid="PSA 80:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 80:13"/>The boar from the forest ravages it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the creature of the field grazes on it.
<verse eid="PSA 80:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 80:14"/>God of armies, return, please.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Look down from heaven and see,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and visit this vine,
<verse eid="PSA 80:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 80:15"/>even the stock that your right hand planted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on the son you strengthened for yourself.
<verse eid="PSA 80:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 80:16"/>It is burned with fire, it is cut down;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the rebuke of your face they perish.
<verse eid="PSA 80:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 80:17"/>Let your hand be on the man of your right hand,
</para>
  <para style="q2">on the son of man you strengthened for yourself.
<verse eid="PSA 80:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 80:18"/>And we will not turn back from you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">revive us, and we will call on your name.
<verse eid="PSA 80:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 80:19"/>Yahweh, God of armies, restore us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Make your face shine, and let us be saved.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 80:19"/><verse eid="PSA 80:19"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 80"/>
  <chapter number="81" style="c" sid="PSA 81"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on Gittith; of Asaph.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 81:1"/>Shout joyfully to God, our strength;
</para>
  <para style="q2">shout out to the God of Jacob.
<verse eid="PSA 81:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 81:2"/>Raise a song and put forth the tambourine,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the pleasant harp with the lyre.
<verse eid="PSA 81:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 81:3"/>Blow a shofar at the new moon,
</para>
  <para style="q2">at the full moon for the day of our festival.
<verse eid="PSA 81:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 81:4"/>For {it is} a statute for Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a judgment of the God of Jacob.
<verse eid="PSA 81:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 81:5"/>He set it as a testimony in Joseph
</para>
  <para style="q2">when he went out over the land of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{where} I heard a lip I did not know.
<verse eid="PSA 81:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 81:6"/>“I removed his shoulder from the burden;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his palms passed from the basket.
<verse eid="PSA 81:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 81:7"/>In distress you called, and I delivered you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I answered you from the secret place of thunder.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I tested you at the waters of Meribah.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 81:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 81:8"/>Hear, my people, and let me testify against you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Israel, if you would listen to me!
<verse eid="PSA 81:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 81:9"/>There shall not be a strange god among you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you shall not bow down to a god of foreignness.
<verse eid="PSA 81:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 81:10"/>I {am} Yahweh your God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one having brought you up from the land of Egypt.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Open wide your mouth, and I will fill it.
<verse eid="PSA 81:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 81:11"/>But my people did not listen to my voice,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Israel did not submit to me.
<verse eid="PSA 81:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 81:12"/>So I sent them away in the stubbornness of their heart;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they walked in their counsels.
<verse eid="PSA 81:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 81:13"/>If only my people were listening to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{if} Israel would walk in my ways!
<verse eid="PSA 81:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 81:14"/>As a little {thing} I would subdue their enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I would turn my hand against their adversaries.
<verse eid="PSA 81:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 81:15"/>The haters of Yahweh would cringe before him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their time would be forever.
<verse eid="PSA 81:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 81:16"/>And he would feed him with the fat of the wheat,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I would satisfy you with honey from the rock.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 81:16"/><verse eid="PSA 81:16"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 81"/>
  <chapter number="82" style="c" sid="PSA 82"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 82:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm. Of Asaph.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God is standing in the congregation of God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the midst of gods he judges:
<verse eid="PSA 82:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 82:2"/>“Until when will you judge {with} injustice
</para>
  <para style="q2">and lift up the faces of the wicked?
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 82:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 82:3"/>Judge the poor and the orphan;
</para>
  <para style="q2">vindicate the poor and the destitute.
<verse eid="PSA 82:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 82:4"/>Rescue the poor and the needy;
</para>
  <para style="q2">deliver {them} from the hand of the wicked.
<verse eid="PSA 82:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 82:5"/>They do not know and they do not understand;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they walk about in darkness.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of the foundations of the earth are shaken.
<verse eid="PSA 82:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 82:6"/>I, I said, ‘You {are} gods
</para>
  <para style="q2">and sons of the Most High, all of you.
<verse eid="PSA 82:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 82:7"/>But you will die like man,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and like one of the princes, you will fall.’”
<verse eid="PSA 82:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 82:8"/>Arise, God, judge the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you, you will inherit among all of the nations.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 82:8"/><verse eid="PSA 82:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 82"/>
  <chapter number="83" style="c" sid="PSA 83"/>
  <para style="d">A song. A psalm. Of Asaph.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 83:1"/>God, {may} silence not {be} to you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not be still, and do not be quiet, God!
<verse eid="PSA 83:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 83:2"/>For behold, your enemies roar,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the ones hating you lift up {the} head.
<verse eid="PSA 83:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 83:3"/>They are cunning {with} counsel against your people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they conspire against your treasured ones.
<verse eid="PSA 83:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 83:4"/>They have said, “Come, and let us destroy them from {being} a nation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that the name of Israel may not be remembered anymore.”
<verse eid="PSA 83:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 83:5"/>For they have conspired against you, heart together;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have cut a covenant:
<verse eid="PSA 83:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 83:6"/>the tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Moab and the Hagrites,
<verse eid="PSA 83:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 83:7"/>Gebal and Ammon and Amalek,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Philistia with the dwellers of Tyre.
<verse eid="PSA 83:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 83:8"/>Also Assyria has joined with them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they {are} an arm to the sons of Lot.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 83:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 83:9"/>Do to them as {to} Midian,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as {to} Sisera, as {to} Jabin at the river of Kishon.
<verse eid="PSA 83:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 83:10"/>They were destroyed at En Dor;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they became dung for the ground.
<verse eid="PSA 83:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 83:11"/>Make them, their nobles, like Oreb and like Zeeb
</para>
  <para style="q2">and like Zebah and like Zalmunna, all of their princes,
<verse eid="PSA 83:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 83:12"/>who said, “Let us possess for ourselves
</para>
  <para style="q2">the pastures of God.”
<verse eid="PSA 83:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 83:13"/>My God, make them like tumbleweed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like chaff to the face of the wind.
<verse eid="PSA 83:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 83:14"/>As fire burns a forest,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and as flame kindles mountains,
<verse eid="PSA 83:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 83:15"/>thus pursue them with your tempest,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and terrify them with your whirlwind.
<verse eid="PSA 83:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 83:16"/>Fill their faces {with} shame,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that they may seek your name, Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 83:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 83:17"/>May they have shame and be terrified, eternities of eternity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may they have disgrace and may they perish.
<verse eid="PSA 83:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 83:18"/>And may they know that you, your name {is} Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you alone {are} the Most High over all of the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 83:18"/><verse eid="PSA 83:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 83"/>
  <chapter number="84" style="c" sid="PSA 84"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; on Gittith. Of the sons of Korah. A psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 84:1"/>How amiable {are} your dwellings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh of Armies!
<verse eid="PSA 84:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 84:2"/>My soul longs and even faints
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the courts of Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my heart and my flesh cry out
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the living God.
<verse eid="PSA 84:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 84:3"/>Even the sparrow has found a house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the swallow, a nest for herself,
</para>
  <para style="q2">where she may lay her young—
</para>
  <para style="q1">your altars, Yahweh of Armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my king and my God.
<verse eid="PSA 84:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 84:4"/>The happinesses of the dwellers of your house!
</para>
  <para style="q2">They praise you continually.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 84:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 84:5"/>The happinesses of the man, strength to him {is} in you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Highways {are} in their heart.
<verse eid="PSA 84:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 84:6"/>Passing through in the Valley of Baca,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they make it a spring;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the early rain also covers {it} {with} blessings.
<verse eid="PSA 84:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 84:7"/>They go from strength to strength;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{each} one appears before God in Zion.
<verse eid="PSA 84:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 84:8"/>Yahweh, God of armies, hear my prayer;
</para>
  <para style="q2">listen, God of Jacob.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 84:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 84:9"/>See our shield, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and regard the face of your anointed.
<verse eid="PSA 84:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 84:10"/>For a day in your courts {is} better than a thousand.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I choose to stand at the threshold in the house of my God
</para>
  <para style="q2">{rather} than dwell in the tents of wickedness.
<verse eid="PSA 84:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 84:11"/>For Yahweh God {is} a sun and a shield;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh gives favor and glory.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He does not withhold good
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the ones walking in blamelessness.
<verse eid="PSA 84:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 84:12"/>Yahweh of Armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the happinesses of the man trusting in you!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 84:12"/><verse eid="PSA 84:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 84"/>
  <chapter number="85" style="c" sid="PSA 85"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician. Of the sons of Korah. A psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 85:1"/>You favored your land, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you restored the captivity of Jacob.
<verse eid="PSA 85:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 85:2"/>You bore the iniquity of your people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you covered all of their sin.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 85:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 85:3"/>You gathered up all of your wrath;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you turned back from the burning of your nose.
<verse eid="PSA 85:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 85:4"/>Restore us, God of our salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and break up your vexation with us.
<verse eid="PSA 85:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 85:5"/>Will you be angry with us forever?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Will you prolong your nose to generation and generation?
<verse eid="PSA 85:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 85:6"/>You, will you not return?
</para>
  <para style="q2">May you revive us, that your people may rejoice in you.
<verse eid="PSA 85:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 85:7"/>Make us see your covenant faithfulness, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and give your salvation to us.
<verse eid="PSA 85:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 85:8"/>Let me hear what God Yahweh will speak,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for he will speak peace to his people and to his faithful ones,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but let them not return to folly.
<verse eid="PSA 85:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 85:9"/>Surely his salvation {is} near to his reverent {ones},
</para>
  <para style="q2">for glory to dwell in our land.
<verse eid="PSA 85:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 85:10"/>Covenant faithfulness and truth will meet together;
</para>
  <para style="q2">righteousness and peace will kiss.
<verse eid="PSA 85:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 85:11"/>Truth will sprout from the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and righteousness will look down from the heavens.
<verse eid="PSA 85:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 85:12"/>Also, Yahweh will give the good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and our land will give its produce.
<verse eid="PSA 85:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 85:13"/>Righteousness walks before him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it puts his steps in the way.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 85:13"/><verse eid="PSA 85:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 85"/>
  <chapter number="86" style="c" sid="PSA 86"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 86:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A prayer. Of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Incline your ear, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">answer me, for I {am} poor and needy.
<verse eid="PSA 86:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 86:2"/>Guard my soul, for I {am} faithful.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You, my God, save your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one trusting in you.
<verse eid="PSA 86:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 86:3"/>Favor me, Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for to you I call all of the day.
<verse eid="PSA 86:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 86:4"/>Gladden the soul of your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for to you, Lord, I lift up my soul.
<verse eid="PSA 86:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 86:5"/>For you, Lord, {are} good and forgiving
</para>
  <para style="q2">and plentiful of covenant faithfulness to all of the ones calling on you.
<verse eid="PSA 86:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 86:6"/>Listen {to} my prayer, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and attend to the voice of my pleas.
<verse eid="PSA 86:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 86:7"/>In the day of my trouble I call on you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you will answer me.
<verse eid="PSA 86:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 86:8"/>There is none like you among the gods, Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is nothing like your works.
<verse eid="PSA 86:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 86:9"/>All of the nations that you have made
</para>
  <para style="q2">will come and bow down to your face, Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will glorify your name.
<verse eid="PSA 86:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 86:10"/>For you {are} great and are doing wonderful things;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you {are} God, you alone.
<verse eid="PSA 86:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 86:11"/>Teach me your way, Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I may walk in your truth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Unite my heart to fear your name.
<verse eid="PSA 86:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 86:12"/>I will thank you, Lord my God, with all of my heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will glorify your name forever.
<verse eid="PSA 86:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 86:13"/>For your covenant faithfulness {is} great toward me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have delivered my soul from lowest Sheol.
<verse eid="PSA 86:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 86:14"/>God, the arrogant arise against me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the congregation of the violent seek my life,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they do not set you before them.
<verse eid="PSA 86:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 86:15"/>But you, Lord, {are} a merciful and gracious God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">long of nostrils and plentiful of covenant faithfulness and truth.
<verse eid="PSA 86:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 86:16"/>Turn to me and favor me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">give your strength to your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and save the son of your female servant.
<verse eid="PSA 86:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 86:17"/>Work for me a sign for good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that the ones hating me may see and have shame,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you, Yahweh, you help me and comfort me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 86:17"/><verse eid="PSA 86:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 86"/>
  <chapter number="87" style="c" sid="PSA 87"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 87:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of the sons of Korah. A psalm. A song.
</para>
  <para style="q1">His foundation {is} on the mountains of holiness.
<verse eid="PSA 87:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 87:2"/>Yahweh is loving the gates of Zion
</para>
  <para style="q2">more than all of the dwellings of Jacob.
<verse eid="PSA 87:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 87:3"/>Glorious things are spoken of you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">city of God.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 87:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 87:4"/>I will mention Rahab and Babylon
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the ones knowing me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">behold, Philistia and Tyre
</para>
  <para style="q2">with Cush—
</para>
  <para style="q1">“This one was born there.”
<verse eid="PSA 87:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 87:5"/>And of Zion it will be said,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Man and man was born in her,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he, he will establish her,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Most High.”
<verse eid="PSA 87:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 87:6"/>Yahweh will recount in the writing of the peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“This {one} was born there.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 87:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 87:7"/>And the singers, like the pipers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“All of my springs {are} in you.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 87:7"/><verse eid="PSA 87:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 87"/>
  <chapter number="88" style="c" sid="PSA 88"/>
  <para style="d">A song. A psalm. Of the sons of Korah. For the chief musician. On “Weakness of Afflicting.” A maskil of Heman the Ezrahite.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 88:1"/>Yahweh, God of my salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{by} day, in the night, I cry out before you.
<verse eid="PSA 88:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 88:2"/>Let my prayer come to your face;
</para>
  <para style="q2">incline your ear to my cry.
<verse eid="PSA 88:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 88:3"/>For my soul is full of troubles,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my life has come near to Sheol.
<verse eid="PSA 88:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 88:4"/>I am reckoned with the ones going down {into} the pit;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have become like a man without strength,
<verse eid="PSA 88:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 88:5"/>free among the ones having died,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like the slain lying in the grave,
</para>
  <para style="q2">whom you do not remember them anymore,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they, they are cut off from your hand.
<verse eid="PSA 88:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 88:6"/>You have set me in the pit of the depths,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in dark places, in deep places.
<verse eid="PSA 88:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 88:7"/>Your wrath rests heavily on me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you overwhelm {me} {with} all of your waves.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 88:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 88:8"/>You have distanced my acquaintances from me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have made me abominations to them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I am} shut in, and I do not go out.
<verse eid="PSA 88:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 88:9"/>My eye mourns from affliction.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I call out to you, Yahweh, in all of the day;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I spread out my palms to you.
<verse eid="PSA 88:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 88:10"/>Will you do a wonder for the ones having died?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Or will the Raphaites arise? Will they thank you?
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 88:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 88:11"/>Will your covenant faithfulness be recounted in the grave,
</para>
  <para style="q2">your faithfulness in Abaddon?
<verse eid="PSA 88:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 88:12"/>Will your wonder be known in the darkness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or your righteousness, in the land of forgetfulness?
<verse eid="PSA 88:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 88:13"/>But I, I cry out to you, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in the morning my prayer precedes you.
<verse eid="PSA 88:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 88:14"/>Why, Yahweh, do you reject my soul?
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Why} do you hide your face from me?
<verse eid="PSA 88:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 88:15"/>I {have been} weak and expiring since youth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have borne your terrors; I must despair.
<verse eid="PSA 88:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 88:16"/>Your indignations pass over me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your terrors destroy me.
<verse eid="PSA 88:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 88:17"/>They surround me like water all of the day;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they close in upon me together.
<verse eid="PSA 88:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 88:18"/>You have distanced friend and acquaintance from me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones known to me {are} darkness.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 88:18"/><verse eid="PSA 88:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 88"/>
  <chapter number="89" style="c" sid="PSA 89"/>
  <para style="d">A maskil. Of Ethan the Ezrahite.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 89:1"/>I will sing the covenant faithfulness of Yahweh forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">to generation and generation I will make known your faithfulness with my mouth.
<verse eid="PSA 89:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 89:2"/>For I said, “Covenant faithfulness will be built up forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the heavens, you establish your faithfulness in them.”
<verse eid="PSA 89:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 89:3"/>“I have cut a covenant with my chosen;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have sworn to David my servant:
<verse eid="PSA 89:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 89:4"/>‘Until forever I will establish your seed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will build up your throne to generation and generation.’”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 89:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 89:5"/>And the heavens praise your wonder, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your faithfulness also, in the assembly of the holy ones.
<verse eid="PSA 89:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 89:6"/>For who in the sky arrays with Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">compares to Yahweh among the sons of God?
<verse eid="PSA 89:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 89:7"/>God is greatly dreaded in the council of the holy ones
</para>
  <para style="q2">and feared above all of the ones around him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 89:8"/>Yahweh, God of Armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who {is} like you, mighty Yah?
</para>
  <para style="q2">And your faithfulness {is} your surroundings.
<verse eid="PSA 89:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 89:9"/>You are ruling over the surging of the sea;
</para>
  <para style="q2">when its waves rise, you, you still them.
<verse eid="PSA 89:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 89:10"/>You, you shattered Rahab like a slain one;
</para>
  <para style="q2">with the arm of your strength you scattered your enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 89:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 89:11"/>To you {are} the heavens, also to you, the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the world and its fullness, you, you founded them.
<verse eid="PSA 89:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 89:12"/>The north and the south, you, you created them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Tabor and Hermon shout joyfully in your name.
<verse eid="PSA 89:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 89:13"/>To you {is} an arm with might;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your hand is strong; your right hand is high.
<verse eid="PSA 89:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 89:14"/>Righteousness and justice {are} the foundation of your throne;
</para>
  <para style="q2">covenant faithfulness and truth precede your face.
<verse eid="PSA 89:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 89:15"/>The happinesses of the people knowing the joyful shout!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, they walk in the light of your face.
<verse eid="PSA 89:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 89:16"/>In your name they rejoice all of the day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in your righteousness they rise high;
<verse eid="PSA 89:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 89:17"/>for you {are} the splendor of their strength,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and by your favor you raise up our horn.
<verse eid="PSA 89:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 89:18"/>For our shield {is} to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and our king, to the Holy {One} of Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 89:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 89:19"/>Then you spoke in a vision to your faithful ones and said,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“I have placed help on a warrior;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have raised up a chosen one from the people.
<verse eid="PSA 89:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 89:20"/>I have found David my servant;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have anointed him with the oil of my holiness,
<verse eid="PSA 89:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 89:21"/>with whom my hand will be established;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my arm will also strengthen him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 89:22"/>The enemy will not exact from him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a son of wickedness will not oppress him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 89:23"/>And I will crush his adversaries from his face,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will strike down the ones hating him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 89:24"/>And my faithfulness and my covenant faithfulness {will be} with him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in my name his horn will be high.
<verse eid="PSA 89:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 89:25"/>And I will set his hand on the sea
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his right hand on the rivers.
<verse eid="PSA 89:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 89:26"/>He, he will call to me, ‘You {are} my Father,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my God and the rock of my salvation.’
<verse eid="PSA 89:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 89:27"/>And I, I will make him the firstborn,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the highest of the kings of the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 89:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 89:28"/>I will keep my covenant faithfulness for him forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my covenant will be confirmed to him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 89:29"/>And I will set up his seed forever
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his throne like the days of the heavens.
<verse eid="PSA 89:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 89:30"/>If his sons forsake my law
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they do not walk in my judgments,
<verse eid="PSA 89:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 89:31"/>if they profane my statutes
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they do not keep my commandments,
<verse eid="PSA 89:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 89:32"/>then I will punish their transgression with a rod
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their iniquity with blows.
<verse eid="PSA 89:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 89:33"/>But my covenant faithfulness I will not break off from him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will not deal falsely in my faithfulness.
<verse eid="PSA 89:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 89:34"/>I will not profane my covenant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will not change the utterance of my lips
<verse eid="PSA 89:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 89:35"/>Once I have sworn by my holiness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">‘If I should lie to David!
<verse eid="PSA 89:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 89:36"/>His seed will be forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his throne, like the sun before me.
<verse eid="PSA 89:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 89:37"/>It will be established forever like the moon,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, the attested witness in the sky.’”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 89:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 89:38"/>But you, you have rejected and spurned;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have passed yourself over from your anointed one.
<verse eid="PSA 89:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 89:39"/>You have voided the covenant of your servant;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have profaned his crown to the ground.
<verse eid="PSA 89:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 89:40"/>You have broken down all of his walls;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have made his fortifications a ruin.
<verse eid="PSA 89:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 89:41"/>All of the passers of the way plunder him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has become a reproach to his neighbors.
<verse eid="PSA 89:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 89:42"/>You have raised up the right hand of his adversaries;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have made all of his enemies rejoice.
<verse eid="PSA 89:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 89:43"/>You have also turned back the edge of his sword,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have not made him stand in battle.
<verse eid="PSA 89:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 89:44"/>You have made his splendor cease,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have cast his throne to the ground.
<verse eid="PSA 89:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 89:45"/>You have shortened the days of his youth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have covered him over with shame.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 89:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 89:46"/>Until when, Yahweh? Will you hide yourself forever?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Will your wrath burn like fire?
<verse eid="PSA 89:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 89:47"/>Remember me, what life {is},
</para>
  <para style="q2">for what emptiness you created all of the sons of man.
<verse eid="PSA 89:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 89:48"/>What man will live and not see death,
</para>
  <para style="q2">will deliver his soul from the hand of Sheol?
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 89:48"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 89:49"/>Where {are} your former covenant faithfulnesses, Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{which} you swore to David in your faithfulness?
<verse eid="PSA 89:49"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 89:50"/>Remember, Lord, the reproach of your servants;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my carrying in my bosom all of many peoples
<verse eid="PSA 89:50"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 89:51"/>with which your enemies have taunted, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">with which they have taunted the footsteps of your anointed.
<verse eid="PSA 89:51"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 89:52"/>Blessed {be} Yahweh forever!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Amen and amen.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 89:52"/><verse eid="PSA 89:52"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 89"/>
  <chapter number="90" style="c" sid="PSA 90"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book Four
</para>
  <para style="d">A prayer of Moses, the man of God.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 90:1"/>Lord, you have been a habitation to us
</para>
  <para style="q1">in generation and generation.
<verse eid="PSA 90:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 90:2"/>Before the mountains were born
</para>
  <para style="q1">or you brought forth the earth and the world,
</para>
  <para style="q1">even from forever to forever, you {are} God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 90:3"/>You cause man to return to dust,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you say, “Return, sons of man.”
<verse eid="PSA 90:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 90:4"/>For a thousand years in your eyes
</para>
  <para style="q1">{are} like the day before when it has passed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a watch in the night.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 90:5"/>You flood them away—they are sleep;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the morning, like grass, it passes along.
<verse eid="PSA 90:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 90:6"/>In the morning it sprouts and passes along;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the evening it withers and dries up.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 90:7"/>For by your nose, we perish,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and by your wrath we are terrified.
<verse eid="PSA 90:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 90:8"/>You have set our iniquities before you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">our hidden {sin} in the light of your face.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 90:9"/>For all of our days turn in your wrath;
</para>
  <para style="q1">we end our years like a sigh.
<verse eid="PSA 90:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 90:10"/>The days of our years, in them {are} 70 years,
</para>
  <para style="q1">or, if by strength, 80 years
</para>
  <para style="q1">but their expanse is trouble and sorrow,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for it passes quickly, and we fly away.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 90:11"/>Who knows the power of your nose,
</para>
  <para style="q1">or your wrath according to your fear?
<verse eid="PSA 90:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 90:12"/>So teach {us} to number our days
</para>
  <para style="q1">that we might bring in a heart of wisdom.
<verse eid="PSA 90:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 90:13"/>Return, Yahweh! Until when?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Have compassion on your servants.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 90:14"/>Satisfy us in the morning {with} your covenant faithfulness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and we will rejoice and be glad in all of our days.
<verse eid="PSA 90:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 90:15"/>Make us glad according to the days you afflicted us
</para>
  <para style="q1">the years we have seen trouble.
<verse eid="PSA 90:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 90:16"/>May your work be seen by your servants,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your majesty by their sons.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 90:17"/>May the favor of the Lord our God be upon us.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And the work of our hands, establish for us;
</para>
  <para style="q1">indeed, the work of our hands, establish it.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 90:17"/><verse eid="PSA 90:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 90"/>
  <chapter number="91" style="c" sid="PSA 91"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 91:1"/>The one dwelling in the shelter of the Most High
</para>
  <para style="q1">will remain in the shadow of Shaddai.
<verse eid="PSA 91:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 91:2"/>I will say to Yahweh, “My refuge and my fortress,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my God, I trust in him.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 91:3"/>For he will rescue you from the snare of the trapper,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the plague of calamities.
<verse eid="PSA 91:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 91:4"/>He will cover you with his feathers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and under his wings you will shelter.
</para>
  <para style="q1">His faithfulness {is} a shield and rampart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 91:5"/>You will not be afraid of the terror of the night,
</para>
  <para style="q1">of the arrow {that} flies by day,
<verse eid="PSA 91:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 91:6"/>of the plague {that} walks in darkness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">of the destruction that wastes {at} midday.
<verse eid="PSA 91:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 91:7"/>A thousand may fall at your side,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a myriad at your right hand;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it will not approach toward you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 91:8"/>You will only observe with your eyes
</para>
  <para style="q1">and see the recompense of the wicked.
<verse eid="PSA 91:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 91:9"/>Because you have made Yahweh, my refuge,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the Most High, your dwelling,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 91:10"/>evil will not happen to you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a plague will not approach your tent.
<verse eid="PSA 91:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 91:11"/>For he will command his angels concerning you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to guard you in all of your ways.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 91:12"/>They will lift you up in their hands,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest you hit your foot against a stone.
<verse eid="PSA 91:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 91:13"/>You will tread on the lion and the adder;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you will trample the young lion and the serpent.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 91:14"/>“Because he clings to me, indeed I will deliver him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will protect him because he knows my name.
<verse eid="PSA 91:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 91:15"/>He will call me and I will answer him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I {will be} with him in trouble;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will rescue him and I will honor him.
<verse eid="PSA 91:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 91:16"/>I will satisfy him {with} length of days,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will show him my salvation.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 91:16"/><verse eid="PSA 91:16"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 91"/>
  <chapter number="92" style="c" sid="PSA 92"/>
  <para style="d">A psalm, a song for the Sabbath day.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 92:1"/>It is good to give thanks to Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to sing praises to your name, Most High,
<verse eid="PSA 92:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 92:2"/>to proclaim your covenant faithfulness in the morning
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your truthfulness in the nights,
<verse eid="PSA 92:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 92:3"/>with a ten {string}
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with a lyre;
</para>
  <para style="q1">with a melody on a harp.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 92:4"/>For you, Yahweh, have made me glad through your deeds.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will sing for joy because of the deeds of your hands.
<verse eid="PSA 92:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 92:5"/>How great are your deeds, Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Your thoughts are very deep.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 92:6"/>A brutish person does not know,
</para>
  <para style="q1">nor does a stupid {one} understand this:
<verse eid="PSA 92:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 92:7"/>When the wicked sprout like grass,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all evildoers thrive,
</para>
  <para style="q1">they will be destroyed for eternity.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 92:8"/>But you, Yahweh, {are} exalted forever.
<verse eid="PSA 92:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 92:9"/>For behold your enemies, Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">For behold your enemies—they will perish!
</para>
  <para style="q1">All those who do evil will be scattered.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 92:10"/>But you have lifted up my horn like a wild ox;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I am saturated with fresh oil.
<verse eid="PSA 92:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 92:11"/>My eye has looked on my foes, those rising up against me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">those doing evil my ears have heard.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 92:12"/>The righteous {one} will flourish like the palm tree;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will grow like a cedar in Lebanon.
<verse eid="PSA 92:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 92:13"/>They are planted in the house of Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they flourish in the courts of our God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 92:14"/>They bear fruit even when they are old;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they are juicy and green,
<verse eid="PSA 92:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 92:15"/>to proclaim that Yahweh is just,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my rock, and {there is} no unrighteousness in him.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 92:15"/><verse eid="PSA 92:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 92"/>
  <chapter number="93" style="c" sid="PSA 93"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 93:1"/>Yahweh reigns; he wears majesty;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh wears, he girds himself with, strength.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Indeed, the world is firmly established; it cannot be moved.
<verse eid="PSA 93:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 93:2"/>Your throne is established from before;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you are from everlasting.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 93:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 93:3"/>The seas rise, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the seas have lifted up their voice;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the seas lift up their pounding {waves}.
<verse eid="PSA 93:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 93:4"/>More than the sounds of many waters,
</para>
  <para style="q1">than the mighty breakers of the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh on high is mighty.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 93:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 93:5"/>Your decrees are very trustworthy;
</para>
  <para style="q1">holiness adorns your house,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, for length of days.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 93:5"/><verse eid="PSA 93:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 93"/>
  <chapter number="94" style="c" sid="PSA 94"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 94:1"/>God of vengeance,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, God of vengeance,
</para>
  <para style="q1">shine forth!
<verse eid="PSA 94:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 94:2"/>Rise up, judge of the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">return recompense upon the proud.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 94:3"/>Until when will the wicked, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">until when will the wicked rejoice?
<verse eid="PSA 94:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 94:4"/>They pour out, they speak, arrogance;
</para>
  <para style="q1">all doers of evil praise themselves.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 94:5"/>They crush your people, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they afflict your inheritance.
<verse eid="PSA 94:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 94:6"/>They kill the widow and the sojourner,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they murder the fatherless.
<verse eid="PSA 94:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 94:7"/>They say, “Yah does not see,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the God of Jacob does not perceive.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 94:8"/>Understand, stupid ones among the people!
</para>
  <para style="q1">O fools, when will you have insight?
<verse eid="PSA 94:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 94:9"/>The one planting the ear, does he not hear?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Or the one forming the eye, does he not observe?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 94:10"/>The one instructing nations, does he not rebuke?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Does the one teaching mankind lack knowledge?
<verse eid="PSA 94:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 94:11"/>Yahweh knows the thoughts of mankind,
</para>
  <para style="q1">that they are vapor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 94:12"/>The joys of the man whom you instruct, Yah,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and from your law you teach him,
<verse eid="PSA 94:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 94:13"/>to give rest to him from days of evil
</para>
  <para style="q1">until a pit is dug for the wicked.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 94:14"/>For Yahweh will not forsake his people
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will not abandon his inheritance.
<verse eid="PSA 94:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 94:15"/>For judgment will return to the right;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all the upright in heart {are} after it.
<verse eid="PSA 94:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 94:16"/>Who will rise up for me against the evildoers?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Who will stand up for me against the workers of wickedness?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 94:17"/>Unless Yahweh {had been} a help to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">shortly my soul would have dwelt in silence.
<verse eid="PSA 94:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 94:18"/>When I said, “My foot is slipping,”
</para>
  <para style="q1">Your covenant faithfulness, Yahweh, supported me.
<verse eid="PSA 94:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 94:19"/>When my cares within me {are} many, your consolations gladden my soul.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 94:20"/>Can a throne of destruction be your ally,
</para>
  <para style="q1">one creating injustice by statute?
<verse eid="PSA 94:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 94:21"/>They conspire together against the life of the righteous
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they condemn innocent blood.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 94:22"/>But Yahweh has been to me a high tower,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my God, the rock of my refuge.
<verse eid="PSA 94:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 94:23"/>He will return on them their iniquity
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will destroy them in their wickedness.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh our God will destroy them.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 94:23"/><verse eid="PSA 94:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 94"/>
  <chapter number="95" style="c" sid="PSA 95"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 95:1"/>Come, let us sing to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let us shout to the rock of our salvation!
<verse eid="PSA 95:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 95:2"/>Let us meet his face with thanksgiving;
</para>
  <para style="q1">with psalms, let us sing joyfully to him.
<verse eid="PSA 95:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 95:3"/>For Yahweh {is} a great God
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a great king above all gods,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 95:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 95:4"/>who in his hand {has} the depths of the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the heights of the mountains {are} to him,
<verse eid="PSA 95:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 95:5"/>who to him {is} the sea, and he, he made it,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his hands formed the dry land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 95:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 95:6"/>Come, let us worship and bow down;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let us kneel to the face of Yahweh, our maker:
<verse eid="PSA 95:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 95:7"/>For he {is} our God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and we {are} the people of his pasture and the flock of his hand.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Today—if only you would listen to his voice!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 95:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 95:8"/>“Do not harden your heart, as {at} Meribah,
</para>
  <para style="q1">as {on} the day of Massah in the wilderness,
<verse eid="PSA 95:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 95:9"/>where your fathers tested me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">tried me, though they had seen my deeds.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 95:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 95:10"/>For 40 years I was angry with the generation
</para>
  <para style="q1">and said, ‘They are a people wandering of heart
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they, they have not known my ways.’
<verse eid="PSA 95:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 95:11"/>Therefore I vowed in my nose,
</para>
  <para style="q1">‘if they enter into my rest.’”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 95:11"/><verse eid="PSA 95:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 95"/>
  <chapter number="96" style="c" sid="PSA 96"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 96:1"/>Sing to Yahweh a new song;
</para>
  <para style="q1">sing to Yahweh, all the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 96:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 96:2"/>Sing to Yahweh, bless his name;
</para>
  <para style="q1">announce his salvation from day to day.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 96:3"/>Recount his glory among the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his marvelous deeds among all the peoples.
<verse eid="PSA 96:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 96:4"/>For Yahweh is great and is to be praised greatly.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He is to be feared above all gods.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 96:5"/>For all the gods of the peoples are idols,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but Yahweh made the heavens.
<verse eid="PSA 96:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 96:6"/>Splendor and majesty {are} to his face.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Strength and beauty {are} in his sanctuary.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 96:7"/>Ascribe to Yahweh, clans of peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q1">ascribe to Yahweh glory and strength.
<verse eid="PSA 96:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 96:8"/>Give to Yahweh the glory of his name.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Bring an offering and come into his courts.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 96:9"/>Bow down to Yahweh in the splendor of holiness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">tremble from his face, all the earth.

<verse eid="PSA 96:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 96:10"/>Say among the nations, “Yahweh reigns.”
</para>
  <para style="q1">Indeed, the world is established; it cannot be shaken.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He judges the peoples with evenness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 96:11"/>Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let the sea roar and its fullness.
<verse eid="PSA 96:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 96:12"/>Let the fields rejoice and all that is in them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then let all the trees in the forest shout for joy
<verse eid="PSA 96:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 96:13"/>to the face of Yahweh, for he is coming,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for he is coming to judge the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He will judge the world with righteousness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the peoples with his faithfulness.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 96:13"/><verse eid="PSA 96:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 96"/>
  <chapter number="97" style="c" sid="PSA 97"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 97:1"/>Yahweh reigns; let the earth rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let the many coastlands be glad.
<verse eid="PSA 97:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 97:2"/>Clouds and darkness surround him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Righteousness and justice {are} the foundation of his throne.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 97:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 97:3"/>Fire goes to his face
</para>
  <para style="q1">and burns his adversaries all around.
<verse eid="PSA 97:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 97:4"/>His lightning lights up the world;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the earth sees and trembles.
<verse eid="PSA 97:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 97:5"/>The mountains melt like wax from to the face of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from to the face of the Lord of all the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 97:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 97:6"/>The heavens declare his righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all the peoples see his glory.
<verse eid="PSA 97:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 97:7"/>Let all those serving a carved image have shame,
</para>
  <para style="q1">those boasting in worthless idols—
</para>
  <para style="q1">bow down to him, all you gods!
<verse eid="PSA 97:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 97:8"/>Zion heard and was glad,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the daughters of Judah rejoiced
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of your judgments, Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 97:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 97:9"/>For you, Yahweh, are most high above all the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You are exalted far above all gods.
<verse eid="PSA 97:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 97:10"/>Lovers of Yahweh, hate evil!
</para>
  <para style="q1">The protector of the lives of his faithful,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the hand of the wicked he snatches them.
<verse eid="PSA 97:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 97:11"/>Light is sown for the righteous
</para>
  <para style="q1">and for the upright of heart, gladness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 97:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 97:12"/>Be glad in Yahweh, you righteous;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and give thanks to the remembrance of his holiness!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 97:12"/><verse eid="PSA 97:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 97"/>
  <chapter number="98" style="c" sid="PSA 98"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 98:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Sing to Yahweh a new song,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for he has done marvelous things;
</para>
  <para style="q1">his right hand and the arm of his holiness have brought him salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 98:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 98:2"/>Yahweh has made known his salvation;
</para>
  <para style="q1">to the eyes of the nations he has revealed his righteousness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 98:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 98:3"/>He remembers his covenant loyalty and his faithfulness to the house of Israel;
</para>
  <para style="q1">all the ends of the earth will see the salvation of our God.
<verse eid="PSA 98:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 98:4"/>Shout to Yahweh, all the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q1">burst into song, sing for joy, and make music!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 98:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 98:5"/>Make music to Yahweh with the harp,
</para>
  <para style="q1">with the harp and the voice of a song.
<verse eid="PSA 98:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 98:6"/>With trumpets and the sound of the shofar,
</para>
  <para style="q1">shout to the face of the King, Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 98:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 98:7"/>Let the sea roar and its fulness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the world and the dwellers in it!
<verse eid="PSA 98:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 98:8"/>Let the rivers clap palm;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let the mountains rejoice together
<verse eid="PSA 98:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 98:9"/>to the face of Yahweh who is coming to judge the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will judge the world with righteousness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the peoples with fairness.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 98:9"/><verse eid="PSA 98:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 98"/>
  <chapter number="99" style="c" sid="PSA 99"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 99:1"/>Yahweh reigns—let the peoples tremble—
</para>
  <para style="q1">sitting {above} the cherubim; let the earth quake!
<verse eid="PSA 99:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 99:2"/>Yahweh in Zion {is} great,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he is high above all the peoples.
<verse eid="PSA 99:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 99:3"/>Let them praise your great and fearsome name;
</para>
  <para style="q1">holy {is} he.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 99:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 99:4"/>And the strength of the king: he loves justice.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You, you have established fairness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you, you have done justice and righteousness in Jacob.
<verse eid="PSA 99:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 99:5"/>Exalt Yahweh our God
</para>
  <para style="q1">and worship at the stool for his feet.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Holy {is} he.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 99:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 99:6"/>Moses and Aaron {were} among his priests,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Samuel {was} among those calling his name.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They called to Yahweh, and he, he answered them.
<verse eid="PSA 99:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 99:7"/>In the pillar of cloud he spoke to them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They kept his testimonies
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the statutes he gave to them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 99:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 99:8"/>Yahweh our God, you, you answered them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">A forgiving God you were to them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but avenging concerning their deeds.
<verse eid="PSA 99:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 99:9"/>Exalt Yahweh our God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and worship at the hill of his holiness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for Yahweh our God is holy.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 99:9"/><verse eid="PSA 99:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 99"/>
  <chapter number="100" style="c" sid="PSA 100"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 100:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of thanksgiving.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Shout to Yahweh, all the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 100:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 100:2"/>Serve Yahweh with gladness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">come to his face with rejoicing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 100:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 100:3"/>Know that Yahweh, he {is} God;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he, he made us, and not we,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his people and the sheep of his pasture.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 100:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 100:4"/>Enter his gates with thanksgiving
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his courts with praise.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Give thanks to him; bless his name.
<verse eid="PSA 100:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 100:5"/>For Yahweh {is} good; his covenant faithfulness {is} to eternity
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his truthfulness until generation and generation.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 100:5"/><verse eid="PSA 100:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 100"/>
  <chapter number="101" style="c" sid="PSA 101"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 101:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">I shall sing {of} covenant faithfulness and justice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">to you, Yahweh, I shall sing praises.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 101:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 101:2"/>I shall study the blameless way.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When will you come to me?
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will walk in the integrity of my heart within my house.
<verse eid="PSA 101:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 101:3"/>I will not put a worthless thing before my eyes;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I hate to do transgressions;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it will not cling to me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 101:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 101:4"/>A perverse heart will turn away from me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will not know evil.
<verse eid="PSA 101:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 101:5"/>The one slandering his neighbor in secret, him I will destroy.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The {one} lofty of eyes and the {one} wide of heart, him I cannot.
<verse eid="PSA 101:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 101:6"/>My eyes {are} on the faithful {ones} of the land to sit with me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">The {one} walking in the way of integrity, he may serve me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 101:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 101:7"/>A doer of deceit will not remain within my house;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a speaker of lies will not be established before my eyes.
<verse eid="PSA 101:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 101:8"/>In the mornings I will destroy all the wicked of the land,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to cut off all workers of evil from the city of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 101:8"/><verse eid="PSA 101:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 101"/>
  <chapter number="102" style="c" sid="PSA 102"/>
  <para style="d">A prayer of the lowly when he is faint and pours out his meditation to the face of Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 102:1"/>Hear my prayer, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let my cry come unto you.
<verse eid="PSA 102:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 102:2"/>Do not hide your face from me on the day it distresses me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Incline your ear to me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">On the day I call out, hurry, answer me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 102:3"/>For my days expire like smoke,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and my bones are charred like a fireplace.
<verse eid="PSA 102:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 102:4"/>My heart is struck like grass and withered,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I have forgotten to eat my bread.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 102:5"/>From the voice of my groaning,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my bone clings to my flesh.
<verse eid="PSA 102:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 102:6"/>I am like an owl of the wilderness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have become like a screech owl in the ruins.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 102:7"/>I am alert,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I have become like a bird alone on a roof.
<verse eid="PSA 102:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 102:8"/>My enemies taunt me all the day;
</para>
  <para style="q1">those mocking me swear by me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 102:9"/>As ashes as bread I eat,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I mix my drink with weeping
<verse eid="PSA 102:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 102:10"/>from the face of your fury and rage,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you have lifted me up and thrown me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 102:11"/>My days {are} like a lengthening shadow,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I, like grass, have withered.
<verse eid="PSA 102:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 102:12"/>But you, Yahweh, sit forever,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your remembrance {is} to generation and generation.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 102:13"/>You, you will arise, you will have mercy on Zion;
</para>
  <para style="q1">for {it is} the time to favor her;
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the appointed time has come.
<verse eid="PSA 102:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 102:14"/>For your servants cherish her stones
</para>
  <para style="q1">and favor her dust.
<verse eid="PSA 102:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 102:15"/>The nations will fear the name of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all the kings of the earth, your glory.
<verse eid="PSA 102:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 102:16"/>For Yahweh builds Zion;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he appears in his glory.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 102:17"/>He turns to the prayer of the destitute
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he does not despise their prayer.
<verse eid="PSA 102:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 102:18"/>This will be written for a future generation,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a people being created will praise Yah;

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 102:19"/>that he looked down from the height of his holiness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh from heaven regarded the earth,
<verse eid="PSA 102:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 102:20"/>to hear the groaning of the prisoner,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to release the sons of execution.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 102:21"/>To recount the name of Yahweh in Zion
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his praise in Jerusalem
<verse eid="PSA 102:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 102:22"/>when peoples and kingdoms gather together
</para>
  <para style="q1">to serve Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 102:23"/>He has broken my strength on the road.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He has shortened my days.
<verse eid="PSA 102:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 102:24"/>I said, “My God, do not take me away in the middle of my days;
</para>
  <para style="q1">your years {are} a generation of generations.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 102:25"/>Formerly you set the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the heavens {are} the work of your hands.
<verse eid="PSA 102:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 102:26"/>They, they will perish, but you, you will stand,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all of them will wear out like a garment;
</para>
  <para style="q1">like clothing, you will pass them off, and they will pass away.
<verse eid="PSA 102:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 102:27"/>But you {are} he,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your years will not end.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 102:28"/>The sons of your servants will abide,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their seed will be established to your face.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 102:28"/><verse eid="PSA 102:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 102"/>
  <chapter number="103" style="c" sid="PSA 103"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 103:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Bless Yahweh, my soul!
</para>
  <para style="q1">And all of my inward parts, the name of his holiness.
<verse eid="PSA 103:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 103:2"/>Bless Yahweh, my soul!
</para>
  <para style="q1">And do not forget all of his benefits.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 103:3"/>The one pardoning all your sins;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one healing all your diseases.
<verse eid="PSA 103:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 103:4"/>The one redeeming your life from the pit;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one crowning you with covenant faithfulness and mercy.
<verse eid="PSA 103:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 103:5"/>The one satisfying your ornaments with good;
</para>
  <para style="q1">your youth renews itself like the eagle.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 103:6"/>Yahweh, doing righteousness and justice for all those being oppressed.
<verse eid="PSA 103:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 103:7"/>He made known his ways to Moses,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his deeds to the children of Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 103:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 103:8"/>Yahweh {is} merciful and gracious,
</para>
  <para style="q1">long of nostrils and abundant in covenant faithfulness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 103:9"/>He will not contend to the end,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will not maintain forever.
<verse eid="PSA 103:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 103:10"/>He does not deal with us according to our sins,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he does not treat us according to our iniquities.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 103:11"/>For as the heavens are high above the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his covenant faithfulness is strong toward those fearing him.
<verse eid="PSA 103:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 103:12"/>As far as the sunrise {is} from the sunset,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he has removed our transgressions from us.
<verse eid="PSA 103:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 103:13"/>As a father has compassion on his children,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh has compassion on those fearing him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 103:14"/>For he, he knows our form;
</para>
  <para style="q1">remembering that we {are} dust.
<verse eid="PSA 103:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 103:15"/>A man, his days {are} like grass;
</para>
  <para style="q1">like a flower of the field, thus he flourishes.
<verse eid="PSA 103:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 103:16"/>For the wind passes over it, and it is no more,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and its place does not acknowledge it again.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 103:17"/>But the covenant faithfulness of Yahweh {is} from everlasting to everlasting on those fearing him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his righteousness {is} to the children of children,
<verse eid="PSA 103:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 103:18"/>to the ones keeping his covenant,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to the ones remembering his precepts, to do them.
<verse eid="PSA 103:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 103:19"/>Yahweh has established his throne in the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his kingdom rules over all.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 103:20"/>Bless Yahweh, his angels,
</para>
  <para style="q1">warriors of strength, doers of his word,
</para>
  <para style="q1">listening to the voice of his word!
<verse eid="PSA 103:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 103:21"/>Bless Yahweh, all his hosts,
</para>
  <para style="q1">ministering to him, doing his pleasure!
<verse eid="PSA 103:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 103:22"/>Bless Yahweh, all his works,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in all the places of his reign!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Bless Yahweh, my soul!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 103:22"/><verse eid="PSA 103:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 103"/>
  <chapter number="104" style="c" sid="PSA 104"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 104:1"/>Bless Yahweh, my soul!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh my God, you are very great;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you are clothed with splendor and majesty,
<verse eid="PSA 104:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 104:2"/>wrapping light as the garment;
</para>
  <para style="q1">spreading out the heavens as the tent curtain;
<verse eid="PSA 104:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 104:3"/>the one setting his upper chambers on the waters;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one appointing the clouds his chariot;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one walking on the wings of the wind;

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 104:4"/>making the winds his messengers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">flaming fire, his servants.
<verse eid="PSA 104:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 104:5"/>He set the earth upon its foundations;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it will not be moved forever and ever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 104:6"/>You covered it {with} the deep like a garment;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the waters stood above the mountains.
<verse eid="PSA 104:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 104:7"/>From your rebuke they fled;
</para>
  <para style="q1">from your voice of thunder they hurried away.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 104:8"/>They ascended the mountains; they descended the valleys,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to the place that you had appointed for them.
<verse eid="PSA 104:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 104:9"/>You set a boundary they cannot pass;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they will not return to cover the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 104:10"/>The one sending springs into the wadis—
</para>
  <para style="q1">between the mountains they flow.
<verse eid="PSA 104:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 104:11"/>They give drink to all his animals of the field;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the wild donkeys break their thirst.
<verse eid="PSA 104:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 104:12"/>Alongside them the birds of the heavens dwell;
</para>
  <para style="q1">from between the branches they give voice.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 104:13"/>The one watering the mountains from his upper chambers—
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the fruit of your works the earth is satisfied.
<verse eid="PSA 104:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 104:14"/>The one making grass grow for the cattle
</para>
  <para style="q1">and plants for the work of man
</para>
  <para style="q1">to bring forth bread from the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 104:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 104:15"/>And wine—he gladdens the heart of man,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to make the face shine from oil,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and bread—he sustains the heart of man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 104:16"/>The trees of Yahweh are satisfied—
</para>
  <para style="q1">the cedars of Lebanon which he planted,
<verse eid="PSA 104:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 104:17"/>where birds make their nests there,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the stork, the cypress tree her home,
<verse eid="PSA 104:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 104:18"/>the high mountains for the wild goats,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the cliffs, a refuge for the hyraxes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 104:19"/>He made the moon for appointed times;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the sun knows its setting.
<verse eid="PSA 104:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 104:20"/>You set darkness and it is night;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in it all of his creatures of the forest crawl—

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 104:21"/>the young lions roaring for prey
</para>
  <para style="q1">and seeking their food from God.
<verse eid="PSA 104:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 104:22"/>The sun rises, they retreat,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and lie down in their dens.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 104:23"/>Man goes out to his work
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to his labor until evening.
<verse eid="PSA 104:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 104:24"/>How many {are} your works, Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">You made all of them with wisdom;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the earth is full of your creation.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 104:25"/>There {is} the sea, great and broad of hands;
</para>
  <para style="q1">creeping things {are} there,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and there is no number,
</para>
  <para style="q1">living things, small with great.
<verse eid="PSA 104:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 104:26"/>Ships travel there;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Leviathan, which you formed to play in it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 104:27"/>All of them look to you to give
</para>
  <para style="q1">their food at its time.
<verse eid="PSA 104:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 104:28"/>You give to them; they gather {it};
</para>
  <para style="q1">you open your hand; they are satisfied {with} good.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 104:29"/>You hide your face; they are terrified;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you take away their breath; they expire
</para>
  <para style="q1">and return to their dust.
<verse eid="PSA 104:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 104:30"/>You send out your breath; they are created,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you renew the face of the land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 104:31"/>May the glory of Yahweh be forever;
</para>
  <para style="q1">may Yahweh rejoice in his creation!
<verse eid="PSA 104:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 104:32"/>The one looking at the earth, and it shakes—
</para>
  <para style="q1">he touches the mountains, and they smoke.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 104:33"/>I shall sing to Yahweh in my life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I shall sing praise to my God during my existence.
<verse eid="PSA 104:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 104:34"/>May my meditation be sweet to him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I, I will rejoice in Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 104:35"/>May sinners cease from the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the wicked be no more.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Bless Yahweh, my soul!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 104:35"/><verse eid="PSA 104:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 104"/>
  <chapter number="105" style="c" sid="PSA 105"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 105:1"/>Give thanks to Yahweh, call on his name;
</para>
  <para style="q1">make known his deeds among the peoples!
<verse eid="PSA 105:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 105:2"/>Sing to him, make music to him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">exclaim about all of his marvelous deeds!
<verse eid="PSA 105:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 105:3"/>Boast in the name of his holiness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let the heart of the seekers of Yahweh rejoice.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 105:4"/>Seek Yahweh and his strength;
</para>
  <para style="q1">search for his face continually.
<verse eid="PSA 105:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 105:5"/>Recall the marvelous things that he has done,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his miracles and the decrees from his mouth,
<verse eid="PSA 105:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 105:6"/>seed of Abraham his servant,
</para>
  <para style="q1">sons of Jacob, his chosen ones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 105:7"/>He is Yahweh, our God.
</para>
  <para style="q1">His decrees {are} in all the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 105:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 105:8"/>He remembers his covenant forever,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the word he commanded for a thousand generations,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 105:9"/>that he cut with Abraham
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his oath to Isaac.
<verse eid="PSA 105:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 105:10"/>He confirmed it to Jacob as a statute;
</para>
  <para style="q1">to Israel, an everlasting covenant,
<verse eid="PSA 105:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 105:11"/>saying, “I will give to you the land of Canaan
</para>
  <para style="q1">{as} the portion of your inheritance,”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 105:12"/>when they were few in number,
</para>
  <para style="q1">very few, and strangers in it.
<verse eid="PSA 105:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 105:13"/>They wandered from nation to nation,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from a kingdom to other people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 105:14"/>He did not allow anyone to oppress them;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he rebuked kings because of them.
<verse eid="PSA 105:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 105:15"/>“Do not touch my anointed ones,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and do not harm my prophets.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 105:16"/>He called for a famine on the land;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he broke all of the staff of bread.
<verse eid="PSA 105:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 105:17"/>He sent a man ahead of them;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Joseph was sold as a servant.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 105:18"/>They oppressed his feet in a shackle;
</para>
  <para style="q1">his neck went into the iron,
<verse eid="PSA 105:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 105:19"/>until the time of his word coming to pass.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The speaking of Yahweh refined him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 105:20"/>The king sent and released him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one ruling the people, and liberated him.
<verse eid="PSA 105:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 105:21"/>He appointed him lord of his house
</para>
  <para style="q1">and ruler over all of his possessions
<verse eid="PSA 105:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 105:22"/>to bind his princes according to his soul
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he taught his elders wisdom.
<verse eid="PSA 105:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 105:23"/>Then Israel came into Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Jacob sojourned in the land of Ham.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 105:24"/>He made his people very fruitful,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he made him stronger than his enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 105:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 105:25"/>He turned their hearts to hate his people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to plot against his servants.
<verse eid="PSA 105:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 105:26"/>He sent Moses, his servant,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Aaron, whom he had chosen him.
<verse eid="PSA 105:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 105:27"/>They performed among them the matters of his signs,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his wonders in the land of Ham.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 105:28"/>He sent darkness and made it dark,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they did not rebel against his words.
<verse eid="PSA 105:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 105:29"/>He turned their water into blood
</para>
  <para style="q1">and killed their fish.
<verse eid="PSA 105:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 105:30"/>Their land swarmed with frogs—
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the rooms of their kings!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 105:31"/>He spoke, and flies came;
</para>
  <para style="q1">gnats in all their territory.
<verse eid="PSA 105:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 105:32"/>He made their rain hail,
</para>
  <para style="q1">fire of flames on their land.
<verse eid="PSA 105:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 105:33"/>He struck their vines and their figs;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he shattered the trees of their territory.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 105:34"/>He spoke, and the locust came,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the young locust, and there was no number.
<verse eid="PSA 105:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 105:35"/>And they ate all of the vegetation in their land;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they ate the fruit of their ground.
<verse eid="PSA 105:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 105:36"/>Then he struck every firstborn in their land,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the first of all their strength.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 105:37"/>He brought them out with silver and gold;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and there was no stumbling among his tribes.
<verse eid="PSA 105:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 105:38"/>Egypt was glad when they departed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the dread of them had fallen upon them.
<verse eid="PSA 105:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 105:39"/>He spread a cloud for a covering
</para>
  <para style="q1">and fire to light up the night.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 105:40"/>He asked, and he brought quail
</para>
  <para style="q1">and satisfied them with bread from heaven.
<verse eid="PSA 105:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 105:41"/>He split the rock and waters gushed out;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they went forth in the desert a river.
<verse eid="PSA 105:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 105:42"/>For he remembered the word of his holiness
</para>
  <para style="q1">with Abraham his servant.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 105:43"/>He led his people out with joy,
</para>
  <para style="q1">his chosen with shouts of triumph.
<verse eid="PSA 105:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 105:44"/>Then he gave to them the lands of the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they took possession of the toil of the peoples
<verse eid="PSA 105:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 105:45"/>so that they might keep his statutes
</para>
  <para style="q1">and comply with his laws.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 105:45"/><verse eid="PSA 105:45"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 105"/>
  <chapter number="106" style="c" sid="PSA 106"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 106:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Give thanks to Yahweh, for {he is} good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 106:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 106:2"/>Who can utter the mighty acts of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">proclaim all of his praise?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 106:3"/>The happinesses of the guardians of justice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the doers of righteousness at all times!
<verse eid="PSA 106:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 106:4"/>Remember me, Yahweh, in the favor of your people;
</para>
  <para style="q1">visit me in your salvation,
<verse eid="PSA 106:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 106:5"/>to look on the good of your chosen,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to rejoice in the gladness of your nation,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to boast with your inheritance.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 106:6"/>We have sinned like our fathers;
</para>
  <para style="q1">we have done wrong; we have done evil.
<verse eid="PSA 106:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 106:7"/>Our fathers did not consider your marvelous deeds in Egypt;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they did not remember the abundance of your covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they rebelled at the sea, the Sea of Reeds.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 106:8"/>But he saved them on account of his name,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to make known his power.
<verse eid="PSA 106:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 106:9"/>He rebuked the Sea of Reeds, and it dried up.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then he led them through the depths, as {through} a desert.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 106:10"/>So he saved them from the hand of the hater,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he rescued them from the hand of the enemy.
<verse eid="PSA 106:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 106:11"/>Then the waters covered their adversaries;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one of them was not left.
<verse eid="PSA 106:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 106:12"/>Then they believed his words;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they sang his praise.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 106:13"/>But they hurried, they forgot his deeds;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they did not wait for his instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 106:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 106:14"/>And they craved a craving in the wilderness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they tested God in the wasteland.
<verse eid="PSA 106:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 106:15"/>So he gave to them their request,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he sent a wasting disease upon their lives.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 106:16"/>And they became envious of Moses in the camp,
</para>
  <para style="q1">of Aaron, the holy one of Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 106:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 106:17"/>The earth opened and swallowed Dathan
</para>
  <para style="q1">and covered over the congregation of Abiram.
<verse eid="PSA 106:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 106:18"/>Fire blazed up in their congregation;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a flame burned up the wicked.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 106:19"/>They made a calf at Horeb
</para>
  <para style="q1">and worshiped a cast image.
<verse eid="PSA 106:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 106:20"/>Thus they traded their Glory
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the likeness of a bull eating grass.
<verse eid="PSA 106:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 106:21"/>They forgot God their Savior,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the doer of great {deeds} in Egypt:

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 106:22"/>wonders in the land of Ham,
</para>
  <para style="q1">awesome {acts} at the Sea of Reeds.
<verse eid="PSA 106:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 106:23"/>So he said to annihilate them—
</para>
  <para style="q1">had not Moses, his chosen one, stood in the breach to his face,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to turn away his heat from destroying.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 106:24"/>Then they despised the delightful land;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they did not believe his word,
<verse eid="PSA 106:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 106:25"/>but grumbled in their tents;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they did not listen to the voice of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 106:26"/>Then he raised his hand to them
</para>
  <para style="q1">to make them fall in the desert,
<verse eid="PSA 106:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 106:27"/>and to make their seed fall among the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to scatter them among the lands.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 106:28"/>They joined themselves to the Baal of Peor
</para>
  <para style="q1">and ate the sacrifices of the dead.
<verse eid="PSA 106:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 106:29"/>And they angered with their actions,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a plague broke out among them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 106:30"/>Then Phinehas stood and intervened,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the plague was restrained.
<verse eid="PSA 106:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 106:31"/>It was counted to him as righteousness
</para>
  <para style="q1">to generation and generation until forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 106:32"/>And they angered at the waters of Meribah,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and it was bad for Moses on account of them.
<verse eid="PSA 106:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 106:33"/>For they rebelled against his spirit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he spoke rashly with his lips.
<verse eid="PSA 106:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 106:34"/>They did not destroy the peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q1">which Yahweh had said to them,
<verse eid="PSA 106:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 106:35"/>but they mingled with the nations
</para>
  <para style="q1">and learned their ways
<verse eid="PSA 106:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 106:36"/>and served their idols,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they became a snare to them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 106:37"/>And they sacrificed their sons and their daughters to demons.
<verse eid="PSA 106:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 106:38"/>And they shed innocent blood,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the blood of their sons and their daughters,
</para>
  <para style="q1">whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the land was desecrated by bloodshed.
<verse eid="PSA 106:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 106:39"/>And they became unclean by their deeds;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they prostituted themselves by their actions.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 106:40"/>So Yahweh’s nose burned with his people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he despised his inheritance.
<verse eid="PSA 106:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 106:41"/>And he gave them into the hand of the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the haters of them ruled over them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 106:42"/>And their enemies oppressed them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they were humbled under their hand.
<verse eid="PSA 106:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 106:43"/>Many times he rescued them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but they, they were rebellious in their counsel
</para>
  <para style="q1">and sank in their sin.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 106:44"/>Yet he saw in the narrow to them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">when he was hearing their cry.
<verse eid="PSA 106:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 106:45"/>And he remembered his covenant with them
</para>
  <para style="q1">and relented because of the abundance of his covenant faithfulness.
<verse eid="PSA 106:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 106:46"/>He gave them for compassion to the face of all of their captors.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 106:47"/>Save us, Yahweh, our God!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Gather us from the nations
</para>
  <para style="q1">to give thanks to the name of your holiness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to glory in your praises.
<verse eid="PSA 106:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 106:48"/>May Yahweh, the God of Israel, be blessed
</para>
  <para style="q1">from everlasting and to everlasting,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all the people say, “Amen.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 106:48"/><verse eid="PSA 106:48"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 106"/>
  <chapter number="107" style="c" sid="PSA 107"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book Five
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 107:1"/>Give thanks to Yahweh, for {he is} good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 107:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 107:2"/>Let the redeemed of Yahweh say {it},
</para>
  <para style="q1">who he rescued them from the hand of the opponent.
<verse eid="PSA 107:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 107:3"/>And he has gathered them from lands,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the sunrise and from the evening,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the north and from the sea.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 107:4"/>They wandered in the desert with wilderness for a road;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a city for a home they did not find.
<verse eid="PSA 107:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 107:5"/>Hungry and thirsty,
</para>
  <para style="q1">their soul fainted within them.
<verse eid="PSA 107:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 107:6"/>Then they called out to Yahweh in the distressing to them;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he rescued them from their distresses.
<verse eid="PSA 107:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 107:7"/>He led them by a direct path
</para>
  <para style="q1">to go to a city of dwelling.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 107:8"/>May they thank Yahweh {for} his covenant faithfulness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his amazing deeds for the sons of man!
<verse eid="PSA 107:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 107:9"/>For he satisfies the thirsty soul,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the hungry soul he fills with good.
<verse eid="PSA 107:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 107:10"/>Sitting in darkness and gloom,
</para>
  <para style="q1">prisoners of affliction and iron

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 107:11"/>because they had rebelled against the words of God
</para>
  <para style="q1">and despised the counsel of the Most High,
<verse eid="PSA 107:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 107:12"/>he humbled their hearts through hardship;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they stumbled and there was no helper.
<verse eid="PSA 107:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 107:13"/>Then they cried out to Yahweh in the distressing to them;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he saved them from their distresses.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 107:14"/>He brought them out of darkness and gloom
</para>
  <para style="q1">and broke apart their bonds.
<verse eid="PSA 107:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 107:15"/>May they thank Yahweh {for} his covenant faithfulness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his amazing deeds for the sons of man!
<verse eid="PSA 107:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 107:16"/>For he has broken the gates of bronze
</para>
  <para style="q1">and cut through the bars of iron.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 107:17"/>Foolish from their rebellious way
</para>
  <para style="q1">and afflicted from their sins,
<verse eid="PSA 107:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 107:18"/>their soul detested all food,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they touched the gates of death.
<verse eid="PSA 107:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 107:19"/>Then they cried out to Yahweh in the distressing to them;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he saved them from their distresses.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 107:20"/>He sent his word and healed them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he delivered them from their destruction.
<verse eid="PSA 107:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 107:21"/>May they thank Yahweh {for} his covenant faithfulness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his amazing deeds for the sons of man!
<verse eid="PSA 107:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 107:22"/>May they sacrifice sacrifices of thanksgiving
</para>
  <para style="q1">and recount his deeds with a shout!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 107:23"/>Going down to the sea in ships,
</para>
  <para style="q1">doing business on abundant waters,
<verse eid="PSA 107:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 107:24"/>they, they saw the deeds of Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his wonders in the deep.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 107:25"/>Then he spoke and aroused the wind of a hurricane
</para>
  <para style="q1">and raised up his waves.
<verse eid="PSA 107:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 107:26"/>They went up {to} the sky; they went down {to} the depths.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Their souls melted in the disaster.
<verse eid="PSA 107:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 107:27"/>They swayed and staggered as intoxicated
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all their wisdom became confounded.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 107:28"/>Then they cried out to Yahweh in the distressing to them
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he rescued them from their distresses.
<verse eid="PSA 107:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 107:29"/>He raised the storm to calmness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he quieted the waves.
<verse eid="PSA 107:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 107:30"/>Then they rejoiced because they subsided,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he guided them to the harbor of their desire.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 107:31"/>May they thank Yahweh {for} his covenant faithfulness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his amazing deeds for the sons of man!
<verse eid="PSA 107:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 107:32"/>May they exalt him in the assembly of the people
</para>
  <para style="q1">and praise him at the seat of the elders.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 107:33"/>He turns rivers into a desert
</para>
  <para style="q1">and springs of water into thirsty land,
<verse eid="PSA 107:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 107:34"/>fruitful ground into salt land,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the wickedness of the dwellers in it.
<verse eid="PSA 107:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 107:35"/>He turns the wilderness into a pool of water
</para>
  <para style="q1">and dry land into springs of water.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 107:36"/>He settles the hungry there,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they build a city of dwelling.
<verse eid="PSA 107:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 107:37"/>Then they sow fields and plant vineyards,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they produce the fruit of the harvest.
<verse eid="PSA 107:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 107:38"/>He blesses them and they become very many
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their cattle do not become few.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 107:39"/>Then they become few and become low
</para>
  <para style="q1">from distress of evil and sorrow.
<verse eid="PSA 107:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 107:40"/>He pours contempt on the leaders
</para>
  <para style="q1">and causes them to wander in an empty place of no road.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 107:41"/>But he raises up the needy from affliction
</para>
  <para style="q1">and establishes families like a flock.
<verse eid="PSA 107:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 107:42"/>The upright see and rejoice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all wickedness shuts its mouth.
<verse eid="PSA 107:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 107:43"/>Who is wise? Then may he keep these things
</para>
  <para style="q1">and may they ponder the covenant faithfulness of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 107:43"/><verse eid="PSA 107:43"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 107"/>
  <chapter number="108" style="c" sid="PSA 108"/>
  <para style="d">A song; a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 108:1"/>My heart is made steadfast, God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing and I will make music, indeed, {with} my glory!
<verse eid="PSA 108:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 108:2"/>Awaken, lyre and harp;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will awaken the dawn.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 108:3"/>I will thank you, Yahweh, among the peoples;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will make music to you among the nations.
<verse eid="PSA 108:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 108:4"/>For your covenant faithfulness {is} great from above the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your trustworthiness, above the clouds.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 108:5"/>Be exalted, God, above the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your glory, over all the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 108:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 108:6"/>So that your beloved ones may be rescued,
</para>
  <para style="q2">save {with} your right hand and answer me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 108:7"/>God has spoken in his holiness: “I shall rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I shall divide Shechem and measure out the Valley of Succoth.
<verse eid="PSA 108:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 108:8"/>To me {is} Gilead; to me {is} Manasseh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Ephraim {is} the protection of my head,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Judah, my scepter.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 108:9"/>Moab {is} a tub for my washing;
</para>
  <para style="q2">over Edom I throw my sandal;
</para>
  <para style="q2">over Philistia I shout triumphantly.”
<verse eid="PSA 108:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 108:10"/>Who will bring me {into} the strong city?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Who will lead me to Edom?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 108:11"/>God, have you not rejected us?
</para>
  <para style="q2">And you do not go out with our army, God.
<verse eid="PSA 108:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 108:12"/>Give to us help against the enemy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and futility {is} the deliverance of man.
<verse eid="PSA 108:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 108:13"/>With God we will accomplish valor;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he, he will trample our adversaries.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 108:13"/><verse eid="PSA 108:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 108"/>
  <chapter number="109" style="c" sid="PSA 109"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 109:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">To the chief musician: a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God of my praise, do not be silent!
<verse eid="PSA 109:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 109:2"/>For a wicked mouth and a mouth of deceit open against me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they speak a tongue of untruth with me,
<verse eid="PSA 109:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 109:3"/>and words of hatred surround me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they attack me without cause.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 109:4"/>In return for my love they accuse me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I—prayer.
<verse eid="PSA 109:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 109:5"/>They put upon me evil in return for good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and hatred in return for my love.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 109:6"/>Appoint a wicked one over him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may an accuser stand at his right hand.
<verse eid="PSA 109:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 109:7"/>When he is judged, may he come out guilty;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may his prayer be as sin.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 109:8"/>May his days be few;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may another take his position.
<verse eid="PSA 109:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 109:9"/>May his children be fatherless,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his wife a widow.
<verse eid="PSA 109:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 109:10"/>And wandering, may his children wander and beg
</para>
  <para style="q2">and seek from their desolations.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 109:11"/>May a creditor snare all that {is} to him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may strangers plunder his work.
<verse eid="PSA 109:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 109:12"/>May there not be to him {one} extending covenant faithfulness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may there not be {one} pitying his orphans.
<verse eid="PSA 109:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 109:13"/>May his posterity be to cut off;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may their name be blotted out in the next generation.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 109:14"/>May the sin of his fathers be remembered to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the offense of his mother not be blotted out.
<verse eid="PSA 109:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 109:15"/>May they be before Yahweh continually
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may he cut off their remembrance from the earth,
<verse eid="PSA 109:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 109:16"/>because he never remembered to do covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but pursued the humble man and the needy
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the dejected in heart to death.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 109:17"/>And he loved cursing, and it came to him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he did not delight in blessing, and it was far from him.
<verse eid="PSA 109:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 109:18"/>And he put on cursing as his garment,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it entered into his inner being like water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and like oil into his bones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 109:19"/>May it be to him like the clothing he wears,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for the belt he always girds himself with it.
<verse eid="PSA 109:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 109:20"/>This, the payment of my accusers from Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and those speaking evil against my soul.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 109:21"/>But you, Yahweh, my Lord, do with me on account of your name.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because your covenant faithfulness {is} good, rescue me!
<verse eid="PSA 109:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 109:22"/>For I am poor and needy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my heart breaks within me.
<verse eid="PSA 109:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 109:23"/>Like a shadow when it lengthens I am made to go;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am shaken off like a locust.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 109:24"/>My knees are weak from fasting
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my flesh is gaunt from fatness.
<verse eid="PSA 109:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 109:25"/>And I, I am a disgrace to them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they see me; they shake their head.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 109:26"/>Help me, Yahweh my God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">save me according to your covenant faithfulness,
<verse eid="PSA 109:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 109:27"/>so that they know that this {is} your hand;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you, Yahweh, you have done it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 109:28"/>They, they will curse, but you, you will bless;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they arise, but then become ashamed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your servant will rejoice.
<verse eid="PSA 109:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 109:29"/>May my accusers be clothed with disgrace;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they wear their shame like a robe.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 109:30"/>With my mouth I greatly thank Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in the midst of many I will praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 109:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 109:31"/>For he stands at the right hand of the needy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to save {him} from the judges of his soul.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 109:31"/><verse eid="PSA 109:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 109"/>
  <chapter number="110" style="c" sid="PSA 110"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 110:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David, a psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The declaration of Yahweh to my lord {the king}:
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Sit at my right hand
</para>
  <para style="q2">until I make your enemies a footstool for your feet.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 110:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 110:2"/>Yahweh will stretch out the scepter of your strength from Zion;
</para>
  <para style="q2">rule in the midst of your enemies!
<verse eid="PSA 110:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 110:3"/>Your people, freewill offerings on the day of your strength, in the beauty of holiness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the womb of the dawn, the dew of your youth {is} to you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 110:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 110:4"/>Yahweh has sworn, and will not revoke {it}:
</para>
  <para style="q1">“You {are} a priest forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">after the manner of Melchizedek.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 110:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 110:5"/>The Lord {is} at your right hand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He crushes kings on the day of his nose.
<verse eid="PSA 110:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 110:6"/>He will judge the nations;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he fills {with} bodies, he crushes the head,
</para>
  <para style="q2">upon abundant land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 110:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 110:7"/>He will drink from the stream along the path,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Therefore, he will lift up the head.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 110:7"/><verse eid="PSA 110:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 110"/>
  <chapter number="111" style="c" sid="PSA 111"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 111:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will thank Yahweh with the whole heart
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the assembly of the upright and congregation.
<verse eid="PSA 111:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 111:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="q1">The works of Yahweh {are} great,
</para>
  <para style="q2">searched by everyone desirous of them.
<verse eid="PSA 111:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 111:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="q1">His work {is} splendor and majesty,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his righteousness stands forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 111:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 111:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="q1">He makes a remembrance for his wonders;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh {is} gracious and merciful.
<verse eid="PSA 111:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 111:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="q1">He gives food to those fearing him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He remembers his covenant forever.
<verse eid="PSA 111:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 111:6"/>He showed the power of his works to his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to give to them the inheritance of the nations.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 111:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 111:7"/>The works of his hands {are} truth and justice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of his precepts are reliable.
<verse eid="PSA 111:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 111:8"/>They are established forever, for eternity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">done in faithfulness, and upright.
<verse eid="PSA 111:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 111:9"/>He has sent redemption to his people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he ordained his covenant forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">holy and awesome {is} his name.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 111:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 111:10"/>The fear of Yahweh {is} the beginning of wisdom;
</para>
  <para style="q2">good understanding to all those doing them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">His praise stands forever!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 111:10"/><verse eid="PSA 111:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 111"/>
  <chapter number="112" style="c" sid="PSA 112"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 112:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">The happinesses of the man fearing Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">greatly delighting in his commandments!
<verse eid="PSA 112:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 112:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="q1">His seed will be powerful on the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">a generation of upright ones will be blessed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 112:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 112:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="q1">Wealth and riches {are} in his house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his righteousness stands forever.
<verse eid="PSA 112:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 112:4"/>Light shines in the darkness for the upright ones;
</para>
  <para style="q1">gracious and compassionate and just.
<verse eid="PSA 112:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 112:5"/>a gracious and lending man {is} good;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he conducts his affairs with justice.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 112:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 112:6"/>For he will not be moved for forever;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the righteous will be for an eternal remembrance.
<verse eid="PSA 112:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 112:7"/>He does not fear bad news;
</para>
  <para style="q1">his heart is sure, trusting in Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 112:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 112:8"/>His heart is upheld, he does not fear,
</para>
  <para style="q1">until he looks over his adversaries.
<verse eid="PSA 112:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 112:9"/>He scatters, he gives to the poor;
</para>
  <para style="q1">his righteousness stands forever;
</para>
  <para style="q1">his horn is high with honor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 112:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 112:10"/>The wicked will see and be angry;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will grind his teeth and he will melt away;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the desire of the wicked will perish.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 112:10"/><verse eid="PSA 112:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 112"/>
  <chapter number="113" style="c" sid="PSA 113"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 113:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise him, servants of Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">praise the name of Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 113:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 113:2"/>Blessed be the name of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">from now and to forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 113:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 113:3"/>From the rising of the sun to its setting,
</para>
  <para style="q1">may the name of Yahweh be praised.
<verse eid="PSA 113:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 113:4"/>Yahweh is high above all nations;
</para>
  <para style="q1">his glory above the skies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 113:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 113:5"/>Who is like Yahweh our God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one making high to sit,
<verse eid="PSA 113:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 113:6"/>the one making low to look
</para>
  <para style="q1">on the sky and on the earth?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 113:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 113:7"/>raising up the poor from the dust,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he lifts the needy from the garbage,
<verse eid="PSA 113:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 113:8"/>to seat him with princes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">with the princes of his people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 113:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 113:9"/>He causes the barren woman of the house to dwell,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the joyful mother of children!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 113:9"/><verse eid="PSA 113:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 113"/>
  <chapter number="114" style="c" sid="PSA 114"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 114:1"/>When Israel went out from Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the house of Jacob from a people speaking a foreign language,
<verse eid="PSA 114:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 114:2"/>Judah became his sanctuary,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Israel his realm.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 114:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 114:3"/>The sea looked and fled;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Jordan turned backward.
<verse eid="PSA 114:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 114:4"/>The mountains skipped like rams,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the hills like sons of the flock.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 114:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 114:5"/>What {is} to you, sea, that you flee?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Jordan, you turn backwards?
<verse eid="PSA 114:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 114:6"/>Mountains, you skip like rams,
</para>
  <para style="q2">hills, like sons of the flock?
<verse eid="PSA 114:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 114:7"/>Tremble, earth, from to the face of the Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from to the face of the God of Jacob,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 114:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 114:8"/>the one turning the rock into a pool of water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">flint into a spring of water!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 114:8"/><verse eid="PSA 114:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 114"/>
  <chapter number="115" style="c" sid="PSA 115"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 115:1"/>Not to us, Yahweh, not to us,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but to your name give honor,
</para>
  <para style="q1">upon your covenant faithfulness, upon your trustworthiness.
<verse eid="PSA 115:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 115:2"/>Why should the nations say,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Where, then, {is} their God?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 115:3"/>And our God {is} in heaven;
</para>
  <para style="q1">everything that he desires, he does.
<verse eid="PSA 115:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 115:4"/>Their idols {are} silver and gold,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the work of the hands of man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 115:5"/>A mouth {is} to them, but they do not speak;
</para>
  <para style="q1">eyes {are} to them, but they do not see;
<verse eid="PSA 115:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 115:6"/>ears {are} to them, but they do not hear;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a nose {is} to them, but they do not smell.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 115:7"/>Their hands, but they do not feel;
</para>
  <para style="q1">their feet, but they cannot walk;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they do not murmur in their throats.
<verse eid="PSA 115:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 115:8"/>Their makers are like them—
</para>
  <para style="q1">everyone who is trusting in them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 115:9"/>Israel, trust in Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he {is} their help and their shield.
<verse eid="PSA 115:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 115:10"/>House of Aaron, trust in Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he {is} their help and their shield.
<verse eid="PSA 115:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 115:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="q1">Fearers of Yahweh, trust in Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he {is} their help and their shield.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 115:12"/>Yahweh remembers us; he will bless;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will bless the house of Israel;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will bless the house of Aaron.
<verse eid="PSA 115:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 115:13"/>He will bless those fearing Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the small with the great.
<verse eid="PSA 115:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 115:14"/>May Yahweh add to you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to you and to your sons.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 115:15"/>May you be blessed by Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the maker of heaven and earth.
<verse eid="PSA 115:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 115:16"/>The heavens of heavens {are} to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the earth he has given to the sons of man.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 115:17"/>The dead do not praise Yah,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and not any descending {to} silence;
<verse eid="PSA 115:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 115:18"/>But we, we will bless Yah
</para>
  <para style="q1">from now and to forever!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 115:18"/><verse eid="PSA 115:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 115"/>
  <chapter number="116" style="c" sid="PSA 116"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 116:1"/>I love {him} because Yahweh hears
</para>
  <para style="q1">my voice, my pleas,
<verse eid="PSA 116:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 116:2"/>because he extends his ear to me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and throughout my days I will call out.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 116:3"/>The cords of death surrounded me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the constrictions of Sheol found me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I found anguish and sorrow.
<verse eid="PSA 116:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 116:4"/>Then I called on the name of Yahweh:
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Please Yahweh, rescue my life.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 116:5"/>Yahweh {is} merciful and righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and our God {is} compassionate.
<verse eid="PSA 116:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 116:6"/>Yahweh guards the naive;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I was low, and he saved me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 116:7"/>Return to your rest, my soul,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for Yahweh has repaid you.
<verse eid="PSA 116:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 116:8"/>For you rescued my soul from death,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my eye from weeping,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my foot from stumbling.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 116:9"/>I will walk to the face of Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the lands of the living.
<verse eid="PSA 116:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 116:10"/>I trusted, though I spoke,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“I, I am very wretched.”
<verse eid="PSA 116:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 116:11"/>I, I said in my panic,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“All mankind lies.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 116:12"/>How can I return to Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">all of his bestowments to me?
<verse eid="PSA 116:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 116:13"/>I will raise the cup of salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and call on the name of Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 116:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 116:14"/>I will fulfill my vows to Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">right in front of all of his people.
<verse eid="PSA 116:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 116:15"/>Precious in the eyes of Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">{is} the death of his faithful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 116:16"/>Indeed, Yahweh, for I {am} your servant;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I {am} your servant, the son of your servant woman;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have undone my bonds.
<verse eid="PSA 116:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 116:17"/>I will sacrifice to you the sacrifice of thanksgiving
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will call on the name of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 116:18"/>I will fulfill my vows to Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">right in front of all of his people,
<verse eid="PSA 116:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 116:19"/>in the courts of the house of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">in your midst, Jerusalem.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 116:19"/><verse eid="PSA 116:19"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 116"/>
  <chapter number="117" style="c" sid="PSA 117"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 117:1"/>Praise Yahweh, all nations;
</para>
  <para style="q1">extol him, all peoples!
<verse eid="PSA 117:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 117:2"/>For his covenant faithfulness is strong toward us,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the trustworthiness of Yahweh {is} to forever.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 117:2"/><verse eid="PSA 117:2"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 117"/>
  <chapter number="118" style="c" sid="PSA 118"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 118:1"/>Give thanks to Yahweh, for {he is} good,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever!
<verse eid="PSA 118:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 118:2"/>Let Israel indeed say,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 118:3"/>Let the house of Aaron indeed say,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.”
<verse eid="PSA 118:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 118:4"/>Let the fearers of Yahweh indeed say,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 118:5"/>From the constriction I called out to Yah;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yah answered me with wideness.
<verse eid="PSA 118:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 118:6"/>Yahweh {is} for me; I will not be afraid;
</para>
  <para style="q1">what can man do to me?
<verse eid="PSA 118:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 118:7"/>Yahweh {is} for me as my helper,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I, I will gaze on the haters of me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 118:8"/>Better to take shelter in Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">than to trust in man.
<verse eid="PSA 118:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 118:9"/>Better to take shelter in Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">than to trust in princes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 118:10"/>All the nations surrounded me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the name of Yahweh, indeed I fended them off.
<verse eid="PSA 118:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 118:11"/>They surrounded me; yes, they surrounded me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the name of Yahweh, indeed I fended them off.
<verse eid="PSA 118:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 118:12"/>They surrounded me like bees;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they were extinguished like a fire of thorns;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the name of Yahweh, indeed I fended them off.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 118:13"/>To push down, you pushed me down to fall,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but Yahweh helped me.
<verse eid="PSA 118:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 118:14"/>Yah {is} my strength and song,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he is to me for salvation.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 118:15"/>The voice of a shout and salvation {is} in the tents of the righteous;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the right hand of Yahweh does valor!
<verse eid="PSA 118:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 118:16"/>The right hand of Yahweh is high;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the right hand of Yahweh does valor!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 118:17"/>I will not die, but live
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will declare the deeds of Yah.
<verse eid="PSA 118:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 118:18"/>To chastise, Yah has chastised me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">but to death he has not given me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 118:19"/>Open to me the gates of righteousness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will enter them; I will thank Yah.
<verse eid="PSA 118:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 118:20"/>This {is} the gate of Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the righteous may enter through it.
<verse eid="PSA 118:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 118:21"/>I will thank you, for you answered me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you have become salvation for me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 118:22"/>The stone that the builders rejected
</para>
  <para style="q1">has become the head of the corner.
<verse eid="PSA 118:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 118:23"/>This is from Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">it is marvelous in our eyes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 118:24"/>This {is} the day Yahweh made;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let us rejoice and be glad in it.
<verse eid="PSA 118:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 118:25"/>Please, Yahweh, save please!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Please, Yahweh, give success please!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 118:26"/>Blessed is the one coming in the name of Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">we bless you from the house of Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 118:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 118:27"/>Yahweh {is} God, and he has given light to us;
</para>
  <para style="q1">bind the sacrifice with cords to the horns of the altar.
<verse eid="PSA 118:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 118:28"/>You {are} my God, and I will thank you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my God, I will exalt you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 118:29"/>Give thanks to Yahweh; for {he is} good;
</para>
  <para style="q1">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 118:29"/><verse eid="PSA 118:29"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 118"/>
  <chapter number="119" style="c" sid="PSA 119"/>
  <para style="qa">ALEPH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 119:1"/>The happinesses of the blameless of way,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones walking in the teaching of Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 119:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 119:2"/>The happinesses of the keepers of his testimonies!
</para>
  <para style="q1">They seek him with a whole heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 119:3"/>Surely they do not practice injustice;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they walk in his ways.
<verse eid="PSA 119:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 119:4"/>You, you have commanded your precepts
</para>
  <para style="q1">to keep diligently.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 119:5"/>Oh, that my paths would be established
</para>
  <para style="q1">to keep your statutes!
<verse eid="PSA 119:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 119:6"/>Then I would not have shame
</para>
  <para style="q1">when I look to all of your commandments.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 119:7"/>I will thank you with uprightness of heart
</para>
  <para style="q1">when I learn the judgments of your righteousness.
<verse eid="PSA 119:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 119:8"/>I will keep your statutes;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not utterly leave me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:8"/></para>
  <para style="qa">BETH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 119:9"/>How can a young man keep his path pure?
</para>
  <para style="q1">By keeping according to your word.
<verse eid="PSA 119:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 119:10"/>With all of my heart I seek you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not let me stray from your commandments.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 119:11"/>I have hidden your word in my heart
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that I might not sin against you.
<verse eid="PSA 119:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 119:12"/>Blessed {are} you, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">teach me your statutes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 119:13"/>With my lips I have recounted
</para>
  <para style="q1">all of the judgments of your mouth.
<verse eid="PSA 119:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 119:14"/>I rejoice in the way of your testimonies
</para>
  <para style="q1">as upon all riches.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 119:15"/>I will meditate on your precepts
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will study your paths.
<verse eid="PSA 119:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 119:16"/>I delight in your statutes;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will not forget your word.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:16"/></para>
  <para style="qa">GIMEL
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 119:17"/>Deal kindly with your servant
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that I may live and keep your word.
<verse eid="PSA 119:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 119:18"/>Uncover my eyes so that I may gaze
</para>
  <para style="q1">on the marvelous things from your teaching.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 119:19"/>I am a sojourner in the land;
</para>
  <para style="q1">do not hide your commandments from me.
<verse eid="PSA 119:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 119:20"/>My soul languishes with longing
</para>
  <para style="q1">for your judgments at all times.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 119:21"/>You rebuke the proud, the cursed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">those wandering from your commandments.
<verse eid="PSA 119:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 119:22"/>Roll from upon me disgrace and humiliation,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I have guarded your testimonies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 119:23"/>Though rulers sit and discuss against me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">your servant meditates on your statutes.
<verse eid="PSA 119:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 119:24"/>Indeed, your testimonies are my pleasure,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my men of counsel.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:24"/></para>
  <para style="qa">DALETH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 119:25"/>My soul clings to the dust!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Revive me according to your word.
<verse eid="PSA 119:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 119:26"/>I recounted my ways, and you answered me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Teach me your statutes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 119:27"/>Make me understand the way of your precepts,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that I can meditate on your wonders.
<verse eid="PSA 119:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 119:28"/>My soul melts from grief.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Lift me up by your word.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 119:29"/>Turn from me the path of deceit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and favor me with your teaching.
<verse eid="PSA 119:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 119:30"/>I have chosen the way of faithfulness;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I agree with your judgments.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 119:31"/>I cling to your testimonies;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, do not let me be shamed.
<verse eid="PSA 119:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 119:32"/>I run in the way of your commandments,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you enlarge my heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:32"/></para>
  <para style="qa">HE
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 119:33"/>Teach me, Yahweh, the way of your statutes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will keep it {to} the end.
<verse eid="PSA 119:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 119:34"/>Give me understanding, and I will guard your teaching,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will keep it with a whole heart.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 119:35"/>Guide me in the path of your commandments,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I delight in it.
<verse eid="PSA 119:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 119:36"/>Incline my heart toward your testimonies
</para>
  <para style="q1">and not toward unrighteous gain.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 119:37"/>Turn away my eyes from looking at worthless things;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in your ways, revive me.
<verse eid="PSA 119:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 119:38"/>Fulfill for your servant your word,
</para>
  <para style="q1">which {is} for the fear of you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 119:39"/>Turn away my reproach, which I dread,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for your judgments are good.
<verse eid="PSA 119:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 119:40"/>Behold, I long for your precepts!
</para>
  <para style="q1">In your righteousness, revive me!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:40"/></para>
  <para style="qa">WAW
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 119:41"/>And let your covenant faithfulness come to me, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">your salvation, according to your word;
<verse eid="PSA 119:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 119:42"/>then I will answer the one reproaching me {with} a word,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I trust in your word.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 119:43"/>So do not utterly snatch the word of truth from my mouth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I wait for your judgments.
<verse eid="PSA 119:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 119:44"/>Then I will observe your teaching continually,
</para>
  <para style="q1">forever and ever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 119:45"/>And I will walk about in the broad,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I seek your precepts.
<verse eid="PSA 119:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 119:46"/>And I will speak of your testimonies before kings,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will not have shame.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 119:47"/>And I delight in your commandments,
</para>
  <para style="q1">which I love.
<verse eid="PSA 119:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 119:48"/>And I will lift up my palms to your commandments, which I love,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will meditate on your statutes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:48"/></para>
  <para style="qa">ZAYIN
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 119:49"/>Remember the word to your servant
</para>
  <para style="q1">by which you have given me hope.
<verse eid="PSA 119:49"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 119:50"/>This {is} my comfort in my affliction
</para>
  <para style="q1">because your promise revives me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:50"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 119:51"/>The proud utterly scoff at me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">from your teaching I do not turn aside.
<verse eid="PSA 119:51"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 119:52"/>I remember your judgments from ancient times, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I comfort myself.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:52"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="PSA 119:53"/>Rage has seized me
</para>
  <para style="q1">from the wicked rejecting your teaching.
<verse eid="PSA 119:53"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="PSA 119:54"/>Your statutes are music to me
</para>
  <para style="q1">in the house of my sojourning.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:54"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="PSA 119:55"/>I remember your name during the night, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I shall observe your teaching.
<verse eid="PSA 119:55"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="PSA 119:56"/>This is for me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">that I keep your precepts.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:56"/></para>
  <para style="qa">HETH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="PSA 119:57"/>Yahweh {is} my portion;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I promise to observe your words.
<verse eid="PSA 119:57"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="PSA 119:58"/>I entreat your face with a whole heart;
</para>
  <para style="q1">be merciful to me according to your word.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:58"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="PSA 119:59"/>I examine my ways
</para>
  <para style="q1">and turn my feet to your testimonies.
<verse eid="PSA 119:59"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="PSA 119:60"/>I hurry and do not delay
</para>
  <para style="q1">to observe your commandments.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:60"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="61" style="v" sid="PSA 119:61"/>The cords of the wicked ensnare me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I do not forget your teaching.
<verse eid="PSA 119:61"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="62" style="v" sid="PSA 119:62"/>In the middle of the night I rise to praise you
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of the judgments of your righteousness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:62"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="63" style="v" sid="PSA 119:63"/>I {am} a companion to all who fear you
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to observers of your precepts.
<verse eid="PSA 119:63"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="64" style="v" sid="PSA 119:64"/>Your covenant faithfulness fills the earth, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">teach me your statutes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:64"/></para>
  <para style="qa">TETH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="65" style="v" sid="PSA 119:65"/>You do good to your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, according to your word.
<verse eid="PSA 119:65"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="66" style="v" sid="PSA 119:66"/>Teach me good discernment and understanding,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I trust in your commandments.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:66"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="67" style="v" sid="PSA 119:67"/>Before I was afflicted, I was going astray,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but now I observe your word.
<verse eid="PSA 119:67"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="68" style="v" sid="PSA 119:68"/>You {are} good, and you do good.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Teach me your statutes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:68"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="69" style="v" sid="PSA 119:69"/>The arrogant smear lies on me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I, with a whole heart, I keep your precepts.
<verse eid="PSA 119:69"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="70" style="v" sid="PSA 119:70"/>Their hearts {are} unfeeling like fat,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I, {in} your teaching, I delight.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:70"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="71" style="v" sid="PSA 119:71"/>{It is} good for me that I have suffered
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that I would learn your statutes.
<verse eid="PSA 119:71"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="72" style="v" sid="PSA 119:72"/>The teaching of your mouth {is} good for me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">more than thousands of gold and silver.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:72"/></para>
  <para style="qa">YODH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="73" style="v" sid="PSA 119:73"/>Your hands have made me and established me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">give me understanding so that I may learn your commandments.
<verse eid="PSA 119:73"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="74" style="v" sid="PSA 119:74"/>May the fearful of you see me and rejoice
</para>
  <para style="q1">because I hope in your word.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:74"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="75" style="v" sid="PSA 119:75"/>Yahweh, I know that your judgments {are} just,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and {in} faithfulness you humble me.
<verse eid="PSA 119:75"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="76" style="v" sid="PSA 119:76"/>Please may your covenant faithfulness be to comfort me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">according to your word to your servant.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:76"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="77" style="v" sid="PSA 119:77"/>May your compassion come to me so that I may live,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for your teaching {is} my delight.
<verse eid="PSA 119:77"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="78" style="v" sid="PSA 119:78"/>Let the proud have shame,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for they have slandered me {with} a lie;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I, I will meditate on your precepts.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:78"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="79" style="v" sid="PSA 119:79"/>May the fearful of you turn to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that they may know your testimonies.
<verse eid="PSA 119:79"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="80" style="v" sid="PSA 119:80"/>May my heart be blameless in your statutes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may not have shame.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:80"/></para>
  <para style="qa">KAPH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="81" style="v" sid="PSA 119:81"/>My soul faints for your salvation!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I wait for your word.
<verse eid="PSA 119:81"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="82" style="v" sid="PSA 119:82"/>My eyes faint for your promise;
</para>
  <para style="q1">saying, “When will you comfort me?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:82"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="83" style="v" sid="PSA 119:83"/>For I have become like a wineskin in the smoke;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I do not forget your statutes.
<verse eid="PSA 119:83"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="84" style="v" sid="PSA 119:84"/>How many {are} the days of your servant?
</para>
  <para style="q1">When will you act in pursuing justice for me?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:84"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="85" style="v" sid="PSA 119:85"/>The proud have dug pits for me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">which is not according to your teaching.
<verse eid="PSA 119:85"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="86" style="v" sid="PSA 119:86"/>All of your commandments are truth.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They pursue me {in} deceit; help me!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:86"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="87" style="v" sid="PSA 119:87"/>As a little they have made an end of me in the land,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but I, I have not rejected your precepts.
<verse eid="PSA 119:87"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="88" style="v" sid="PSA 119:88"/>According to your covenant faithfulness, keep me alive,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that I may observe the testimony of your mouth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:88"/></para>
  <para style="qa">LAMEDH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="89" style="v" sid="PSA 119:89"/>Forever, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">your word is established in the heavens.
<verse eid="PSA 119:89"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="90" style="v" sid="PSA 119:90"/>Your faithfulness {is} to generation and generation;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have established the earth, and it stands.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:90"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="91" style="v" sid="PSA 119:91"/>By your judgments, they stand today,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for all things are your servants.
<verse eid="PSA 119:91"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="92" style="v" sid="PSA 119:92"/>If your teaching {had} not {been} my delight,
</para>
  <para style="q1">then I would have perished in my affliction.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:92"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="93" style="v" sid="PSA 119:93"/>I will not forget your precepts forever,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for through them you have preserved me alive.
<verse eid="PSA 119:93"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="94" style="v" sid="PSA 119:94"/>I am yours; save me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I seek your precepts.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:94"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="95" style="v" sid="PSA 119:95"/>The wicked wait for me to destroy me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I pay attention to your testimonies.
<verse eid="PSA 119:95"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="96" style="v" sid="PSA 119:96"/>I have seen an end for all perfection;
</para>
  <para style="q1">your commandment is very broad.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:96"/></para>
  <para style="qa">MEM
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="97" style="v" sid="PSA 119:97"/>How I love your teaching!
</para>
  <para style="q1">It is my meditation all the day.
<verse eid="PSA 119:97"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="98" style="v" sid="PSA 119:98"/>Your commandment makes me wiser than my enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for it is with me forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:98"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="99" style="v" sid="PSA 119:99"/>I have more insight than all my teachers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for your testimonies are a meditation to me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:99"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="100" style="v" sid="PSA 119:100"/>I understand more than the elders,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I have kept your precepts.

<verse eid="PSA 119:100"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="101" style="v" sid="PSA 119:101"/>I have restrained my feet from every evil path,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I might keep your word.

<verse eid="PSA 119:101"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="102" style="v" sid="PSA 119:102"/>I have not turned aside from your judgments,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you, you have taught me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:102"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="103" style="v" sid="PSA 119:103"/>How your word is sweet to my palate,
</para>
  <para style="q2">more than honey to my mouth!

<verse eid="PSA 119:103"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="104" style="v" sid="PSA 119:104"/>From your precepts I gain understanding;
</para>
  <para style="q2">therefore, I hate every path of falsehood.

<verse eid="PSA 119:104"/></para>
  <para style="qa">NUN

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="105" style="v" sid="PSA 119:105"/>Your word {is} a lamp to my foot
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a light to my path.

<verse eid="PSA 119:105"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="106" style="v" sid="PSA 119:106"/>I have sworn and I will confirm {it},
</para>
  <para style="q2">to keep the judgments of your righteousness.

<verse eid="PSA 119:106"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="107" style="v" sid="PSA 119:107"/>I have been afflicted exceedingly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, revive me according to your word.

<verse eid="PSA 119:107"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="108" style="v" sid="PSA 119:108"/>Please accept the freewill offerings of my mouth, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and teach me your judgments.

<verse eid="PSA 119:108"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="109" style="v" sid="PSA 119:109"/>My soul {is} in my palm continually,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I do not forget your teaching.

<verse eid="PSA 119:109"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="110" style="v" sid="PSA 119:110"/>The wicked have set a snare for me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I have not wandered from your precepts.

<verse eid="PSA 119:110"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="111" style="v" sid="PSA 119:111"/>I have inherited your testimonies forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for they {are} the joy of my heart.

<verse eid="PSA 119:111"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="112" style="v" sid="PSA 119:112"/>I have inclined my heart to do your statutes
</para>
  <para style="q2">to forever, the end.

<verse eid="PSA 119:112"/></para>
  <para style="qa">SAMEKH

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="113" style="v" sid="PSA 119:113"/>The double-minded I have hated,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but your teaching I have loved.

<verse eid="PSA 119:113"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="114" style="v" sid="PSA 119:114"/>My hiding place and my shield {are} you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">for your word I wait.

<verse eid="PSA 119:114"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="115" style="v" sid="PSA 119:115"/>Turn aside from me, doers of evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let me keep the commandments of my God.

<verse eid="PSA 119:115"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="116" style="v" sid="PSA 119:116"/>Sustain me according to your word so that I may live,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not make me ashamed of my hope.

<verse eid="PSA 119:116"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="117" style="v" sid="PSA 119:117"/>Support me so that I will be saved,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and so I may gaze on your statutes continually.

<verse eid="PSA 119:117"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="118" style="v" sid="PSA 119:118"/>You reject all those straying from your statutes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for their deceit {is} falsehood.

<verse eid="PSA 119:118"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="119" style="v" sid="PSA 119:119"/>You cause to cease {as} dross all the wicked of the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">therefore, I love your testimonies.

<verse eid="PSA 119:119"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="120" style="v" sid="PSA 119:120"/>My flesh shudders from dread of you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I fear your judgments.

<verse eid="PSA 119:120"/></para>
  <para style="qa">AYIN

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="121" style="v" sid="PSA 119:121"/>I have done justice and righteousness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not leave me to those oppressing me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:121"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="122" style="v" sid="PSA 119:122"/>Be surety for your servant for good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not let the arrogant oppress me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:122"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="123" style="v" sid="PSA 119:123"/>My eyes have failed for your salvation
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for the word of your righteousness.

<verse eid="PSA 119:123"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="124" style="v" sid="PSA 119:124"/>Deal with your servant according to your covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and teach me your statutes.

<verse eid="PSA 119:124"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="125" style="v" sid="PSA 119:125"/>I {am} your servant; give me understanding,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I can know your testimonies.

<verse eid="PSA 119:125"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="126" style="v" sid="PSA 119:126"/>{It is} time for Yahweh to act;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have broken your law.

<verse eid="PSA 119:126"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="127" style="v" sid="PSA 119:127"/>Therefore, I love your commandments
</para>
  <para style="q2">more than gold and more than fine gold.

<verse eid="PSA 119:127"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="128" style="v" sid="PSA 119:128"/>Therefore, all the precepts of everything I carefully observe;
</para>
  <para style="q2">every path of falsehood I hate.

<verse eid="PSA 119:128"/></para>
  <para style="qa">PE

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="129" style="v" sid="PSA 119:129"/>Your testimonies {are} wonderful;
</para>
  <para style="q2">therefore, my soul has kept them.

<verse eid="PSA 119:129"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="130" style="v" sid="PSA 119:130"/>The doorway of your words gives light,
</para>
  <para style="q2">giving understanding to the simple.

<verse eid="PSA 119:130"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="131" style="v" sid="PSA 119:131"/>I open wide my mouth and I pant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I long for your commandments.

<verse eid="PSA 119:131"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="132" style="v" sid="PSA 119:132"/>Turn to me and be gracious to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">according to the judgment for the ones loving your name.

<verse eid="PSA 119:132"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="133" style="v" sid="PSA 119:133"/>Establish my steps in your word,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not let any iniquity rule over me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:133"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="134" style="v" sid="PSA 119:134"/>Redeem me from the oppression of man,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I may keep your precepts.

<verse eid="PSA 119:134"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="135" style="v" sid="PSA 119:135"/>Make your face shine on your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and teach me your statutes.

<verse eid="PSA 119:135"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="136" style="v" sid="PSA 119:136"/>Streams of water go down {from} my eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they do not keep your law.

<verse eid="PSA 119:136"/></para>
  <para style="qa">TSADE

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="137" style="v" sid="PSA 119:137"/>Righteous {are} you, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and upright {are} your judgments.

<verse eid="PSA 119:137"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="138" style="v" sid="PSA 119:138"/>You have commanded your testimonies {in} righteousness
</para>
  <para style="q2">and faithfulness exceedingly.

<verse eid="PSA 119:138"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="139" style="v" sid="PSA 119:139"/>My zeal consumes me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for my adversaries have forgotten your words.

<verse eid="PSA 119:139"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="140" style="v" sid="PSA 119:140"/>Your word {is} refined exceedingly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your servant loves it.

<verse eid="PSA 119:140"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="141" style="v" sid="PSA 119:141"/>Small {am} I and despised;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your precepts I have not forgotten.

<verse eid="PSA 119:141"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="142" style="v" sid="PSA 119:142"/>Your righteousness {is} righteousness forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your law {is} truth.

<verse eid="PSA 119:142"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="143" style="v" sid="PSA 119:143"/>Narrow and distress have found me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your commandments {are} my delight.

<verse eid="PSA 119:143"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="144" style="v" sid="PSA 119:144"/>The righteousness of your testimonies {is} forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">give me understanding, so that I may live.

<verse eid="PSA 119:144"/></para>
  <para style="qa">QOPH

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="145" style="v" sid="PSA 119:145"/>I call out with a whole heart; answer me, Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I shall keep your statutes.

<verse eid="PSA 119:145"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="146" style="v" sid="PSA 119:146"/>I call out to you; save me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may keep your testimonies.

<verse eid="PSA 119:146"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="147" style="v" sid="PSA 119:147"/>I preempt the dawn and cry for help;
</para>
  <para style="q2">for your words I wait.

<verse eid="PSA 119:147"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="148" style="v" sid="PSA 119:148"/>My eyes preempt the night watches,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to meditate on your word.

<verse eid="PSA 119:148"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="149" style="v" sid="PSA 119:149"/>Hear my voice according to your covenant faithfulness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, according to your judgment, revive me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:149"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="150" style="v" sid="PSA 119:150"/>The pursuers of evil purpose have drawn near;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from your law they are far away.

<verse eid="PSA 119:150"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="151" style="v" sid="PSA 119:151"/>Near {are} you, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all your commandments {are} truth.

<verse eid="PSA 119:151"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="152" style="v" sid="PSA 119:152"/>Long ago, I knew from your testimonies
</para>
  <para style="q2">that you have founded them forever.

<verse eid="PSA 119:152"/></para>
  <para style="qa">RESH

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="153" style="v" sid="PSA 119:153"/>See my affliction and rescue me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I have not forgotten your law.

<verse eid="PSA 119:153"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="154" style="v" sid="PSA 119:154"/>Plead my plea and redeem me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">for your word, revive me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:154"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="155" style="v" sid="PSA 119:155"/>Salvation {is} far from the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for they have not sought your statutes.

<verse eid="PSA 119:155"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="156" style="v" sid="PSA 119:156"/>Your compassions {are} many, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">according to your judgments, revive me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:156"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="157" style="v" sid="PSA 119:157"/>Many {are} my pursuers and my adversaries;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from your testimonies I do not turn aside.

<verse eid="PSA 119:157"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="158" style="v" sid="PSA 119:158"/>I have seen the treacherous, and I was disgusted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they have not kept your word.

<verse eid="PSA 119:158"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="159" style="v" sid="PSA 119:159"/>See that I have loved your precepts;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, according to your covenant faithfulness, revive me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:159"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="160" style="v" sid="PSA 119:160"/>The head of your word {is} truth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and every judgment of your righteousness {is} forever.

<verse eid="PSA 119:160"/></para>
  <para style="qa">SHIN

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="161" style="v" sid="PSA 119:161"/>Princes pursue me without cause,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my heart trembles from your words.

<verse eid="PSA 119:161"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="162" style="v" sid="PSA 119:162"/>I am rejoicing over your word,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like one finding great plunder.

<verse eid="PSA 119:162"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="163" style="v" sid="PSA 119:163"/>Falsehood I hate and I abhor;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your law I love.

<verse eid="PSA 119:163"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="164" style="v" sid="PSA 119:164"/>Seven times in the day I praise you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of the judgments of your righteousness.

<verse eid="PSA 119:164"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="165" style="v" sid="PSA 119:165"/>Great peace {is} to the ones loving your law,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is no stumbling block for them.

<verse eid="PSA 119:165"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="166" style="v" sid="PSA 119:166"/>I hope for your salvation, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I do your commandments.

<verse eid="PSA 119:166"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="167" style="v" sid="PSA 119:167"/>My soul keeps your testimonies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I love them exceedingly.

<verse eid="PSA 119:167"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="168" style="v" sid="PSA 119:168"/>I keep your precepts and your testimonies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for all my ways {are} before you.

<verse eid="PSA 119:168"/></para>
  <para style="qa">TAV

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="169" style="v" sid="PSA 119:169"/>May my cry come near to your face, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">according to your word, give me understanding.

<verse eid="PSA 119:169"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="170" style="v" sid="PSA 119:170"/>May my plea come to your face;
</para>
  <para style="q2">according to your word, deliver me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:170"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="171" style="v" sid="PSA 119:171"/>May my lips gush out praise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for you teach me your statutes.

<verse eid="PSA 119:171"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="172" style="v" sid="PSA 119:172"/>May my tongue sing of your word,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for all your commandments {are} righteousness.

<verse eid="PSA 119:172"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="173" style="v" sid="PSA 119:173"/>May your hand be to help me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I have chosen your precepts.

<verse eid="PSA 119:173"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="174" style="v" sid="PSA 119:174"/>I long for your salvation, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your law {is} my delight.

<verse eid="PSA 119:174"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="175" style="v" sid="PSA 119:175"/>May my soul live, and may it praise you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may your judgments help me.

<verse eid="PSA 119:175"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="176" style="v" sid="PSA 119:176"/>I have strayed like a perishing sheep;
</para>
  <para style="q2">seek your servant, for I have not forgotten your commandments.


<verse eid="PSA 119:176"/><verse eid="PSA 119:176"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 119"/>
  <chapter number="120" style="c" sid="PSA 120"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 120:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">To Yahweh, in the distress to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I called, and he answered me.
<verse eid="PSA 120:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 120:2"/>Yahweh, deliver my soul
</para>
  <para style="q2">from a lip of falsehood,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from a tongue of deceit.
<verse eid="PSA 120:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 120:3"/>What will he give to you, and what will he add to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">O tongue of deceit?
<verse eid="PSA 120:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 120:4"/>Arrows of a warrior, sharpened,
</para>
  <para style="q2">with coals of broom trees.
<verse eid="PSA 120:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 120:5"/>Woe to me, for I am sojourning {in} Meshech;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am dwelling with the tents of Kedar.
<verse eid="PSA 120:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 120:6"/>My soul has dwelt much to itself
</para>
  <para style="q2">with a hater of peace.
<verse eid="PSA 120:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 120:7"/>I {am} peace, but when I speak,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they {are} for war.


<verse eid="PSA 120:7"/><verse eid="PSA 120:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 120"/>
  <chapter number="121" style="c" sid="PSA 121"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 121:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I lift up my eyes to the mountains.
</para>
  <para style="q2">From where does my help come?

<verse eid="PSA 121:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 121:2"/>My help {is} from with Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">maker of heaven and earth.

<verse eid="PSA 121:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 121:3"/>May he not give your foot to the slipping;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may your keeper not slumber.

<verse eid="PSA 121:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 121:4"/>Behold, he will not slumber,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will not sleep,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the keeper of Israel.

<verse eid="PSA 121:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 121:5"/>Yahweh {is} your keeper;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh {is} your shade upon your right hand.

<verse eid="PSA 121:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 121:6"/>By day the sun will not strike you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the moon by night.

<verse eid="PSA 121:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 121:7"/>Yahweh will keep you from all evil;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will keep your soul.

<verse eid="PSA 121:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 121:8"/>Yahweh will keep your going out and your coming in,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from now and to forever.


<verse eid="PSA 121:8"/><verse eid="PSA 121:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 121"/>
  <chapter number="122" style="c" sid="PSA 122"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 122:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents; of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I rejoiced in the ones saying to me, “Let us go {to} the house of Yahweh.”

<verse eid="PSA 122:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 122:2"/>Our feet are standing
</para>
  <para style="q2">in your gates, Jerusalem.

<verse eid="PSA 122:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 122:3"/>Jerusalem, the one built
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a city that is joined to itself together.

<verse eid="PSA 122:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 122:4"/>Where the tribes go up,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the tribes of Yah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a testimony to Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to give thanks to the name of Yahweh.

<verse eid="PSA 122:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 122:5"/>For there sit thrones for judgment,
</para>
  <para style="q2">thrones for the house of David.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 122:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 122:6"/>Ask {for} the peace of Jerusalem;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may the ones loving you prosper.

<verse eid="PSA 122:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 122:7"/>Let there be peace within your rampart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">prosperity in your citadels.

<verse eid="PSA 122:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 122:8"/>For the sake of my brothers and my companions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">let me speak, please, peace in you.

<verse eid="PSA 122:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 122:9"/>For the sake of the house of Yahweh our God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">let me seek good for you.


<verse eid="PSA 122:9"/><verse eid="PSA 122:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 122"/>
  <chapter number="123" style="c" sid="PSA 123"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 123:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">To you I lift up my eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one dwelling in the heavens.

<verse eid="PSA 123:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 123:2"/>Behold, as the eyes of servants {are} to the hand of their masters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as the eyes of a maidservant {are} to the hand of her mistress,
</para>
  <para style="q2">thus our eyes {are} to Yahweh our God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">until he is gracious to us.

<verse eid="PSA 123:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 123:3"/>Be gracious to us, Yahweh, be gracious to us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for we are greatly satiated with contempt.

<verse eid="PSA 123:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 123:4"/>Greatly our soul is
</para>
  <para style="q2">satiated with it, the scorn of the arrogant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the contempt of the proud.


<verse eid="PSA 123:4"/><verse eid="PSA 123:4"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 123"/>
  <chapter number="124" style="c" sid="PSA 124"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 124:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents; of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If not Yahweh who was for us—
</para>
  <para style="q2">let Israel indeed say—

<verse eid="PSA 124:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 124:2"/>if not Yahweh who was for us
</para>
  <para style="q2">when man rose up against us,

<verse eid="PSA 124:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 124:3"/>then they would have swallowed us alive
</para>
  <para style="q2">when their nose burned against us.

<verse eid="PSA 124:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 124:4"/>Then the waters would have overflowed us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the torrent would have passed over our soul.

<verse eid="PSA 124:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 124:5"/>Then the raging waters would have passed over our soul.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 124:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 124:6"/>Blessed {be} Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who did not make us prey for their teeth.

<verse eid="PSA 124:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 124:7"/>Our soul {is} like a bird {that} escaped from the snare of the trappers;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the snare was broken, and we, we escaped.

<verse eid="PSA 124:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 124:8"/>Our help {is} in the name of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the maker of heaven and earth.


<verse eid="PSA 124:8"/><verse eid="PSA 124:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 124"/>
  <chapter number="125" style="c" sid="PSA 125"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 125:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Those trusting in Yahweh {are} like Mount Zion;
</para>
  <para style="q2">it will not be shaken; forever it abides.

<verse eid="PSA 125:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 125:2"/>Jerusalem—mountains {are} around her,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh {is} around his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from now and to forever.

<verse eid="PSA 125:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 125:3"/>For the rod of wickedness will not rest on the lot of the righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that the righteous will not stretch out their hands in unrighteousness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 125:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 125:4"/>Do good, Yahweh, to the good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to the upright in their hearts.

<verse eid="PSA 125:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 125:5"/>And those twisting their crooked {ways},
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh will make them go with the workers of iniquity.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Peace {be} upon Israel.


<verse eid="PSA 125:5"/><verse eid="PSA 125:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 125"/>
  <chapter number="126" style="c" sid="PSA 126"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 126:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When Yahweh returned the captivity of Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">we were like ones dreaming.

<verse eid="PSA 126:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 126:2"/>Then our mouth was filled {with} laughter,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and our tongue {with} a shout of joy.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then they said among the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Yahweh has made great to do with these.”

<verse eid="PSA 126:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 126:3"/>Yahweh has made great to do with us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we are joyful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 126:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 126:4"/>Return, Yahweh, our captivity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like the streams in the Negev.

<verse eid="PSA 126:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 126:5"/>The ones sowing in tears
</para>
  <para style="q2">will reap in a shout of joy.

<verse eid="PSA 126:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 126:6"/>Going, he may go and weeping,
</para>
  <para style="q2">carrying the bag of seed.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Coming, he will come in a shout of joy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">carrying his sheaves.


<verse eid="PSA 126:6"/><verse eid="PSA 126:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 126"/>
  <chapter number="127" style="c" sid="PSA 127"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 127:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents; of Solomon.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If Yahweh does not build a house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{in} vain its builders have labored on it.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If Yahweh does not watch a city,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{in} vain the watchman has stayed awake.
<verse eid="PSA 127:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 127:2"/>{It is} vain for you, the ones rising early to get up,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones being late to sit down,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones eating the bread of toils;
</para>
  <para style="q1">certainly he gives to his beloved one sleep.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 127:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 127:3"/>Behold, the inheritance of Yahweh {is} sons;
</para>
  <para style="q2">a reward {is} the fruit of the womb.
<verse eid="PSA 127:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 127:4"/>Like arrows in the hand of a warrior,
</para>
  <para style="q2">thus {are} the sons of the youth.
<verse eid="PSA 127:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 127:5"/>The happinesses of the man who has filled his quiver of them!
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will not have shame
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they speak with adversaries in the gate.


<verse eid="PSA 127:5"/><verse eid="PSA 127:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 127"/>
  <chapter number="128" style="c" sid="PSA 128"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 128:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The happinesses of everyone fearing Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one walking in his ways.
<verse eid="PSA 128:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 128:2"/>The labor of your palms, when you eat {it},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{is} your happiness, and good for you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 128:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 128:3"/>Your wife {is} like a fruitful vine
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the recesses of your house.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Your sons {are} like shoots of olive trees,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all around your table.
<verse eid="PSA 128:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 128:4"/>Behold, for thus the man fearing Yahweh will be blessed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 128:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 128:5"/>May Yahweh bless you from Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that you may look on the good of Jerusalem
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of the days of your life,
<verse eid="PSA 128:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 128:6"/>and that you may see sons to your sons.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Peace {be} upon Israel!


<verse eid="PSA 128:6"/><verse eid="PSA 128:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 128"/>
  <chapter number="129" style="c" sid="PSA 129"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 129:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Abundantly they have afflicted me from my youth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let Israel indeed say:
<verse eid="PSA 129:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 129:2"/>Abundantly they have afflicted me from my youth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">however, they did not prevail against me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 129:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 129:3"/>Upon my back the plowers plowed;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they made long their furrows.
<verse eid="PSA 129:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 129:4"/>Yahweh {is} righteous;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has cut the cords of the wicked.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 129:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 129:5"/>Let them have shame and withdraw backward,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all the haters of Zion.
<verse eid="PSA 129:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 129:6"/>Let them be like grass of the rooftops,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that before one pulls {it} out, it dries up,
<verse eid="PSA 129:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 129:7"/>that the reaper does not fill his palm {with},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the one binding sheaves, {does} not fill his bosom,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 129:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 129:8"/>and those passing by do not say, “The blessing of Yahweh {be} upon you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we bless you in the name of Yahweh.”


<verse eid="PSA 129:8"/><verse eid="PSA 129:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 129"/>
  <chapter number="130" style="c" sid="PSA 130"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 130:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Out of the depths I cry to you, Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 130:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 130:2"/>Lord, hear my voice;
</para>
  <para style="q1">let your ears be attentive
</para>
  <para style="q1">to the voice of my supplications.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 130:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 130:3"/>If you, Yah, would mark sins,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Lord, who could stand?
<verse eid="PSA 130:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 130:4"/>However, {there is} forgiveness with you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that you may be feared.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 130:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 130:5"/>I wait for Yahweh; my soul waits,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and in his word I hope;
<verse eid="PSA 130:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 130:6"/>my soul for the Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q1">more than watchmen for the morning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">watchmen for the morning.
<verse eid="PSA 130:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 130:7"/>Israel, hope in Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for with Yahweh {is} covenant faithfulness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and with him {is} abundant redemption.
<verse eid="PSA 130:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 130:8"/>And he, he will redeem Israel
</para>
  <para style="q1">from all his sins.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 130:8"/><verse eid="PSA 130:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 130"/>
  <chapter number="131" style="c" sid="PSA 131"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 131:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents; of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, my heart is not high and my eyes are not raised up,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I do not walk in great and marvelous {things} beyond me.
<verse eid="PSA 131:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 131:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1">Rather, I have stilled and quieted my soul
</para>
  <para style="q1">like a weaned child upon his mother;
</para>
  <para style="q1">like a weaned child upon me {is} my soul.
<verse eid="PSA 131:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 131:3"/>Israel, hope in Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">from now and until forever!


<verse eid="PSA 131:3"/><verse eid="PSA 131:3"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 131"/>
  <chapter number="132" style="c" sid="PSA 132"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 132:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of ascents.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Remember, Yahweh, for David,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of his afflictions,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 132:2"/>who swore to
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh; vowed to the Mighty One of Jacob,

<verse eid="PSA 132:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 132:3"/>“If I go into the tent of my house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">if I go up on the bed of my couch,

<verse eid="PSA 132:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 132:4"/>if I give sleep to my eyes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">slumber to my eyelids,

<verse eid="PSA 132:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 132:5"/>until I find a place for Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">dwellings for the Mighty One of Jacob.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 132:6"/>Behold, we heard of it in Ephrathah;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we found it in the fields of Jaar.

<verse eid="PSA 132:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 132:7"/>“Let us go to his dwellings;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let us bow down at the footstool of his feet.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 132:8"/>Arise, Yahweh, to your resting place,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you and the box of your strength.

<verse eid="PSA 132:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 132:9"/>Let your priests wear righteousness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let your faithful shout for joy.

<verse eid="PSA 132:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 132:10"/>For the sake of David your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not turn back the face of your anointed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 132:11"/>Yahweh swore to David,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{in} truth, he will not turn back from it:
</para>
  <para style="q1">“From the fruit of your body
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will set {one} on the throne for you.

<verse eid="PSA 132:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 132:12"/>If your sons keep my covenant
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my testimonies that I will teach them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then also their sons, unto perpetuity,
</para>
  <para style="q2">will sit on the throne for you.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 132:13"/>For Yahweh has chosen Zion;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he desired {it} for a dwelling for himself.

<verse eid="PSA 132:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 132:14"/>“This {is} my resting place unto perpetuity;
</para>
  <para style="q2">here I will dwell, for I have desired it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 132:15"/>Blessing I will bless her provisions;
</para>
  <para style="q2">her needy I will satisfy {with} bread.

<verse eid="PSA 132:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 132:16"/>And her priests I will clothe {with} salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and her faithful, shouting they will shout for joy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 132:17"/>There I will make a horn sprout for David;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have arranged a lamp for my anointed one.

<verse eid="PSA 132:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 132:18"/>His enemies I will clothe {with} shame,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but upon him his crown will flourish.”


<verse eid="PSA 132:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 132"/>
  <chapter number="133" style="c" sid="PSA 133"/>
  <para style="q1">Behold, how good and how pleasant
</para>
  <para style="q2">{is} the dwelling of brothers, yes, together!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 133:2"/>Like the good oil on the head,
</para>
  <para style="q2">coming down on the beard, the beard of Aaron,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is coming down on the mouth of his garments,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 133:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 133:3"/>like the dew of Hermon
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is coming down on the mountains of Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for there Yahweh commanded the blessing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">life to forever.


<verse eid="PSA 133:3"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 133"/>
  <chapter number="134" style="c" sid="PSA 134"/>
  <para style="q1">Behold, bless Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all servants of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones standing in the house of Yahweh in the nights.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 133:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 134:2"/>Lift up your hands {to the} holiness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and bless Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 134:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 134:3"/>May Yahweh bless you from Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the maker of heaven and earth.


<verse eid="PSA 134:3"/><verse eid="PSA 134:3"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 134"/>
  <chapter number="135" style="c" sid="PSA 135"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 135:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise the name of Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise {him}, servants of Yahweh,
<verse eid="PSA 135:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 135:2"/>who are standing in the house of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the courts of the house of our God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 135:3"/>Hallelu Yah, for Yahweh {is} good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">make music to his name, for {it is} pleasant.
<verse eid="PSA 135:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 135:4"/>For Yah chose Jacob for himself;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Israel for his special possession.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 135:5"/>For I, I know that Yahweh {is} great,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and our Lord than all gods.
<verse eid="PSA 135:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 135:6"/>Everything that Yahweh desires, he does,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the heavens and on the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the seas and all deeps—
<verse eid="PSA 135:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 135:7"/>bringing up clouds from the end of the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he makes lightning bolts for the rain—
</para>
  <para style="q2">bringing out wind from his storehouses,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 135:8"/>who struck the firstborn of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from man to beast.
<verse eid="PSA 135:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 135:9"/>He sent signs and wonders
</para>
  <para style="q2">into your midst, Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">against Pharaoh and against all of his servants,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 135:10"/>who struck many nations
</para>
  <para style="q2">and slew mighty kings:
<verse eid="PSA 135:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 135:11"/>Sihon, king of the Amorite,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Og, king of the Bashan,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all the kingdoms of Canaan.
<verse eid="PSA 135:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 135:12"/>And he gave their land {as} an inheritance,
</para>
  <para style="q2">an inheritance for Israel, his people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 135:13"/>Yahweh, your name {is} to forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, your remembrance {is} to generation and generation.
<verse eid="PSA 135:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 135:14"/>For Yahweh vindicates his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he has compassion on his servants.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 135:15"/>The idols of the nations {are} silver and gold,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the work of the hands of man.
<verse eid="PSA 135:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 135:16"/>A mouth {is} to them, but they do not speak;
</para>
  <para style="q2">eyes {are} to them, but they do not see.
<verse eid="PSA 135:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 135:17"/>Ears {are} to them, but they do not listen;
</para>
  <para style="q2">indeed there is no breath in their mouths.
<verse eid="PSA 135:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 135:18"/>Their makers are like them—
</para>
  <para style="q2">everyone who is trusting in them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 135:19"/>House of Israel, bless Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">house of Aaron, bless Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 135:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 135:20"/>House of the Levite, bless Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">fearers of Yahweh, bless Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 135:21"/>Blessed {be} Yahweh from Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one dwelling {in} Jerusalem.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!


<verse eid="PSA 135:21"/><verse eid="PSA 135:21"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 135"/>
  <chapter number="136" style="c" sid="PSA 136"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 136:1"/>Give thanks to Yahweh, for {he} is good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 136:2"/>Give thanks to the God of the gods,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 136:3"/>Give thanks to the Lord of the lords,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 136:4"/>To the doer of great wonders, him alone,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 136:5"/>To the maker of the heavens by understanding,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 136:6"/>To the one spreading out the earth over the waters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 136:7"/>To the maker of great lights,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
<verse eid="PSA 136:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 136:8"/>the sun for dominion in the day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
<verse eid="PSA 136:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 136:9"/>the moon and stars for dominion in the night,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 136:10"/>To the striker of Egypt in their firstborn,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 136:11"/>And he brought out Israel from their midst,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 136:12"/>By a strong hand and by an outstretched arm,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 136:13"/>To the parter of the Sea of Reeds into parts,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 136:14"/>And he made Israel pass through the midst of it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 136:15"/>And he tossed Pharaoh and his army into the Sea of Reeds,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 136:16"/>To the one leading his people in the wilderness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 136:17"/>To the one striking great kings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 136:18"/>And he killed mighty kings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
<verse eid="PSA 136:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 136:19"/>Sihon, king of the Amorite,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
<verse eid="PSA 136:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 136:20"/>and Og, king of the Bashan,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 136:21"/>And he gave their land as an inheritance,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
<verse eid="PSA 136:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 136:22"/>an inheritance to Israel his servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 136:23"/>who, in our humiliation, remembered us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 136:24"/>And he tore us away from our adversaries,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
<verse eid="PSA 136:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 136:25"/>giving bread to all of flesh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
<verse eid="PSA 136:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 136:26"/>Give thanks to the God of the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever!


<verse eid="PSA 136:26"/><verse eid="PSA 136:26"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 136"/>
  <chapter number="137" style="c" sid="PSA 137"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 137:1"/>By the rivers of Babylon,
</para>
  <para style="q2">there we sat down, also we wept,
</para>
  <para style="q2">when we remembered Zion.

<verse eid="PSA 137:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 137:2"/>On the willows in her midst
</para>
  <para style="q2">we hung our harps.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 137:3"/>For there our captors requested of us
</para>
  <para style="q2">words of a song,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and our tormentors, joy: “Sing for us from a song of Zion.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 137:4"/>How shall we sing the song of Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">on the land of foreignness?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 137:5"/>If I forget you, Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">let my right hand forget.

<verse eid="PSA 137:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 137:6"/>Let my tongue cling to my palate
</para>
  <para style="q2">if I do not remember you, if I do not cause Jerusalem to go up
</para>
  <para style="q2">above the head of my joy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 137:7"/>Remember, Yahweh, for the sons of Edom,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the day of Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones saying, “Lay bare, lay bare,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the foundation in her!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 137:8"/>Daughter Babylon, the devastated one,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the happinesses of the one who makes complete to you
</para>
  <para style="q2">your repayment that you paid to us!

<verse eid="PSA 137:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 137:9"/>The happinesses of the one who seizes
</para>
  <para style="q2">and dashes your infants
</para>
  <para style="q2">against the rock!


<verse eid="PSA 137:9"/><verse eid="PSA 137:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 137"/>
  <chapter number="138" style="c" sid="PSA 138"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 138:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will thank you with my whole heart;
</para>
  <para style="q2">before the gods I will make music to you.
<verse eid="PSA 138:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 138:2"/>I will bow down toward the temple of your holiness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will praise your name for your covenant faithfulness and for your trustworthiness,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you have exalted above all of your name your word.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 138:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 138:3"/>On the day that I called and you answered me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you emboldened my soul {with} power.

<verse eid="PSA 138:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 138:4"/>May all the kings of the earth thank you, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because they heard the words from your mouth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 138:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 138:5"/>May they sing of the ways of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for great is the glory of Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 138:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 138:6"/>Though Yahweh is high, yet he sees the lowly,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the proud he knows from far off.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 138:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 138:7"/>Though I walk in the middle of trouble, you will keep me alive;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you will stretch out your hand against the nose of my enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your right hand will save me.
<verse eid="PSA 138:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 138:8"/>Yahweh will accomplish for my benefit;
</para>
  <para style="q1">your covenant faithfulness, Yahweh, {is} forever.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not forsake the works of your hands.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 138:8"/><verse eid="PSA 138:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 138"/>
  <chapter number="139" style="c" sid="PSA 139"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 139:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; of David; a psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, you have searched me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you know {me}.

<verse eid="PSA 139:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 139:2"/>You, you know my sitting down and my rising up;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you understand my thought from far away.

<verse eid="PSA 139:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 139:3"/>My path and my lying down you have winnowed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you are familiar with all of my ways.

<verse eid="PSA 139:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 139:4"/>For there is not a word on my tongue;
</para>
  <para style="q2">behold, Yahweh, you know all of it.

<verse eid="PSA 139:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 139:5"/>Behind and before you have enclosed me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have set your palm upon me.

<verse eid="PSA 139:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 139:6"/>{Such} knowledge {is} too wonderful for me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is high; I am not capable of it.

<verse eid="PSA 139:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 139:7"/>Where shall I go from your spirit?
</para>
  <para style="q2">And where shall I flee from your face?

<verse eid="PSA 139:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 139:8"/>If I ascend {to} the heavens, you {are} there,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I spread out {in} Sheol, behold, you!

<verse eid="PSA 139:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 139:9"/>{If} I lift up the wings of the dawn,
</para>
  <para style="q2">dwell in the farthest part of the sea,

<verse eid="PSA 139:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 139:10"/>even there your hand will lead me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your right hand will hold me.

<verse eid="PSA 139:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 139:11"/>And I said, “Surely darkness will crush me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and night, the light around me.”

<verse eid="PSA 139:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 139:12"/>Even darkness does not make it dark to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the night shines like the day;
</para>
  <para style="q2">like darkness, like light.

<verse eid="PSA 139:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 139:13"/>For you, you created my kidneys;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you knit me together in the womb of my mother.

<verse eid="PSA 139:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 139:14"/>I will thank you because fearsomely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am wonderfully made.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Wonderful {are} your works,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my soul knows {it} very well.

<verse eid="PSA 139:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 139:15"/>My frame was not hidden from you
</para>
  <para style="q2">when I was made in the secret place, {when} I was woven in the depths of the earth,

<verse eid="PSA 139:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 139:16"/>your eyes saw my unformed substance.
</para>
  <para style="q2">And in your book all of them were written:
</para>
  <para style="q1">the days were formed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {yet} not one of them {was}.

<verse eid="PSA 139:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 139:17"/>And to me, how precious are your thoughts, God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">How numerous are their heads!

<verse eid="PSA 139:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 139:18"/>{If} I should count them, they are more than the sand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I awake, and I {am} still with you.

<verse eid="PSA 139:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 139:19"/>If only you would kill the wicked, God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">And men of bloodshed, depart from me,

<verse eid="PSA 139:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 139:20"/>who speak of you for an evil purpose;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they lift up {your name} to emptiness—your enemies.

<verse eid="PSA 139:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 139:21"/>Do I not hate the ones hating you, Yahweh?
</para>
  <para style="q2">And do I not loathe the ones rising up against you?

<verse eid="PSA 139:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 139:22"/>{With} a completeness of hatred I hate them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have become enemies to me.

<verse eid="PSA 139:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 139:23"/>Search me, God, and know my heart;
</para>
  <para style="q2">examine me and know my cares.

<verse eid="PSA 139:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 139:24"/>And see if a way of hurtfulness {is} in me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and lead me in the way of eternity.


<verse eid="PSA 139:24"/><verse eid="PSA 139:24"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 139"/>
  <chapter number="140" style="c" sid="PSA 140"/>
  <para style="d">For the chief musician; a psalm of David.

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 140:1"/>Rescue me, Yahweh, from an evil man;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from a man of violence preserve me,

<verse eid="PSA 140:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 140:2"/>who plot evil things in the heart;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all the day they travel around {to} battles.
<verse eid="PSA 140:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 140:3"/>They have sharpened their tongue like a serpent;
</para>
  <para style="q2">venom of a viper {is} under their lips.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 140:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 140:4"/>Guard me, Yahweh, from the hands of the wicked;
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the man of violence preserve me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">who have planned to push down my steps.

<verse eid="PSA 140:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 140:5"/>The proud have hidden a snare for me, and cords;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have spread out a net to the hand of the path;
</para>
  <para style="q2">traps they have set for me.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 140:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 140:6"/>I have said to Yahweh, “You {are} my God.”
</para>
  <para style="q2">Give ear, Yahweh, to the voice of my supplications.

<verse eid="PSA 140:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 140:7"/>Yahweh, Lord, the strength of my salvation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have covered my head in the day of weaponry.

<verse eid="PSA 140:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 140:8"/>Do not grant, Yahweh, the desires of the wicked;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not bring forth his plot, {lest} they rise up.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 140:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 140:9"/>The head of the ones surrounding me—
</para>
  <para style="q2">let the mischief of their lips cover them.

<verse eid="PSA 140:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 140:10"/>Let burning coals fall on them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let him cast them into the fire,
</para>
  <para style="q2">into pits, let them not rise up.

<verse eid="PSA 140:10"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 140:11"/>Let not a man of tongue be established in the land;
</para>
  <para style="q2">a man of violence—let evil hunt him with blows.

<verse eid="PSA 140:11"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 140:12"/>I know that Yahweh will do the cause of the poor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the justice of the needy.

<verse eid="PSA 140:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 140:13"/>Surely the righteous will praise your name;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the upright will dwell before your face.


<verse eid="PSA 140:13"/><verse eid="PSA 140:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 140"/>
  <chapter number="141" style="c" sid="PSA 141"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 141:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I cry out to you, “Hurry to me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Give ear to my voice when I cry out to you.”
<verse eid="PSA 141:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 141:2"/>May my prayer be established {like} incense to your face,
</para>
  <para style="q1">a raising of my palms {like} the evening sacrifice.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 141:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 141:3"/>Yahweh, place a guard over my mouth;
</para>
  <para style="q1">guard the door of my lips.
<verse eid="PSA 141:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 141:4"/>Do not turn my heart toward an evil thing
</para>
  <para style="q1">to wantonly act in activities in wickedness
</para>
  <para style="q1">with men, doers of evil.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And may I not dine on their delicacies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 141:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 141:5"/>Let the righteous hit me—covenant faithfulness, and he is correcting me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Oil for the head may my head not refuse.
</para>
  <para style="q1">For my prayer {is} continually against their wickedness.
<verse eid="PSA 141:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 141:6"/>Their judges are thrown down beside a cliff;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they hear my words, that they are pleasant.
<verse eid="PSA 141:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 141:7"/>“Just as splitting and breaking up in the ground,
</para>
  <para style="q1">our bones are scattered at the mouth of Sheol.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 141:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 141:8"/>Yet my eyes are on you, Yahweh, Lord;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in you I take refuge; do not uncover my soul.
<verse eid="PSA 141:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 141:9"/>Keep me from the hands of the snare they have laid for me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the traps of the workers of evil.
<verse eid="PSA 141:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 141:10"/>Let the wicked fall into his nets together,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I, while I cross over.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 141:10"/><verse eid="PSA 141:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 141"/>
  <chapter number="142" style="c" sid="PSA 142"/>
  <para style="d">A maskil of David; when he was in the cave; a prayer.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 142:1"/>My voice to Yahweh—I cry out;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my voice to Yahweh—I plead for favor.
<verse eid="PSA 142:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 142:2"/>I pour out my lament to his face;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my distress to his face I declare.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 142:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 142:3"/>When my spirit faints within me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">then you, you know my path.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Along this path I walk
</para>
  <para style="q1">they have hidden a trap for me.
<verse eid="PSA 142:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 142:4"/>Look right and see
</para>
  <para style="q1">and there is no one who recognizes me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">A refuge has become lost from me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">there is no one caring for my soul.
<verse eid="PSA 142:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 142:5"/>I cried out to you, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I said, “You {are} my shelter,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my portion in the land of the living.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 142:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 142:6"/>Listen to my cry,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I am very low;
</para>
  <para style="q1">rescue me from my pursuers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for they are stronger than I.
<verse eid="PSA 142:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 142:7"/>Bring out my soul from prison
</para>
  <para style="q1">to praise your name.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The righteous will gather around me
</para>
  <para style="q1">because you will fulfill for me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 142:7"/><verse eid="PSA 142:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 142"/>
  <chapter number="143" style="c" sid="PSA 143"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 143:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hear my prayer, Yahweh; listen to my pleas!
</para>
  <para style="q2">On account of your faithfulness answer me in your righteousness!
<verse eid="PSA 143:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 143:2"/>And do not enter into judgment with your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for everyone living is not righteous to your face.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 143:3"/>For the enemy has pursued my soul;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he has crushed my life to the ground;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he has made me to live in dark places
</para>
  <para style="q1">like the dead of ages.
<verse eid="PSA 143:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 143:4"/>So my spirit faints within me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my heart despairs inside me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 143:5"/>I remember days from before;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I meditate on all your works;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I reflect on the works of your hands.
<verse eid="PSA 143:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 143:6"/>I spread out my hands to you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my soul, as a thirsty land, to you.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 143:7"/>Hurry! Answer me, Yahweh; my spirit is expiring!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not hide your face from me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">or I will become equal with those going down to the pit.
<verse eid="PSA 143:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 143:8"/>Let me hear your covenant faithfulness in the morning,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I trust in you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Make known to me this way I should walk,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I lift up my soul to you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 143:9"/>Rescue me from my enemies, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I hide in you.
<verse eid="PSA 143:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 143:10"/>Teach me to do your will,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you {are} my God.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May your good Spirit
</para>
  <para style="q1">lead me in a level land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 143:11"/>Yahweh, for the sake of your name, may you preserve my life;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in your righteousness may you bring my soul out of distress.
<verse eid="PSA 143:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 143:12"/>And in your covenant faithfulness may you destroy my enemies
</para>
  <para style="q1">and exterminate all the adversaries of my soul,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for I am your servant.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 143:12"/><verse eid="PSA 143:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 143"/>
  <chapter number="144" style="c" sid="PSA 144"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 144:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Blessed {be} Yahweh, my rock,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one teaching my hands for war,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my fingers for battle,
<verse eid="PSA 144:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 144:2"/>my covenant faithfulness and my fortress,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my stronghold and the one rescuing me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my shield, and in whom I take refuge,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one subduing my people under me.
<verse eid="PSA 144:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 144:3"/>Yahweh, what {is} man, that you know him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the son of man, that you consider him?
<verse eid="PSA 144:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 144:4"/>Man compares to vapor;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his days {are} like a passing shadow.
<verse eid="PSA 144:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 144:5"/>Yahweh, bow your heavens and come down;
</para>
  <para style="q2">touch the mountains, that they may smoke.
<verse eid="PSA 144:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 144:6"/>Light lightning and scatter them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">send your arrows and rout them.
<verse eid="PSA 144:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 144:7"/>Send your hands from above;
</para>
  <para style="q2">break me free and deliver me from many waters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the hand of sons of a foreigner,
<verse eid="PSA 144:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 144:8"/>who, their mouth speaks worthlessness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their right hand {is} a right hand of falsehood.
<verse eid="PSA 144:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 144:9"/>God, I will sing a new song to you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">with a lyre of ten {strings} I will make music to you,
<verse eid="PSA 144:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 144:10"/>the one giving salvation to kings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one breaking free David his servant
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the evil sword.
<verse eid="PSA 144:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 144:11"/>Break me free and deliver me
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the hand of the sons of a foreigner,
</para>
  <para style="q1">who, their mouth speaks worthlessness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their right hand {is} a right hand of falsehood,
<verse eid="PSA 144:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 144:12"/>that our sons {may be} like plants
</para>
  <para style="q2">having been enlarged in their youth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">our daughters, like corner pillars
</para>
  <para style="q2">carved {in} the pattern of a palace.
<verse eid="PSA 144:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 144:13"/>{May} our granaries {be} full,
</para>
  <para style="q2">furnishing from kind to kind;
</para>
  <para style="q1">may our flocks be thousanding,
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they be myriading in our fields.
<verse eid="PSA 144:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 144:14"/>{May} our oxen {be} burdened;
</para>
  <para style="q2">no breach and no going out
</para>
  <para style="q2">and no cry in our squares.
<verse eid="PSA 144:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 144:15"/>The happinesses of the people for whom {it is} thus to it!
</para>
  <para style="q2">The happinesses of the people for whom Yahweh {is} its God!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 144:15"/><verse eid="PSA 144:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 144"/>
  <chapter number="145" style="c" sid="PSA 145"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 145:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will exalt you, my God, the King,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will bless your name forever and ever.
<verse eid="PSA 145:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 145:2"/>I will bless you every day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will praise your name forever and ever.
<verse eid="PSA 145:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 145:3"/>Yahweh {is} great and being much praised,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is no searching of his greatness.
<verse eid="PSA 145:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 145:4"/>Generation to generation will proclaim your works,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will declare your mighty acts.
<verse eid="PSA 145:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 145:5"/>{On} the splendor of the glory of your majesty
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {on} the deeds of your making wonderful, let me meditate.
<verse eid="PSA 145:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 145:6"/>And they will tell the strength of your making fearful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let me recount it, your greatness.
<verse eid="PSA 145:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 145:7"/>They will pour forth the remembrance of the abundance of your goodness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will sing joyfully {about} your righteousness.
<verse eid="PSA 145:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 145:8"/>Yahweh {is} gracious and compassionate,
</para>
  <para style="q2">long of nostrils and great of covenant faithfulness.
<verse eid="PSA 145:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 145:9"/>Yahweh {is} good to all,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his compassions {are} over all of his works.
<verse eid="PSA 145:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 145:10"/>All your works will thank you, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your faithful will bless you.
<verse eid="PSA 145:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 145:11"/>They will tell the glory of your kingdom,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will speak {of} your power,
<verse eid="PSA 145:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 145:12"/>to make known to the sons of man his mighty acts
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the glory of the splendor of his kingdom.
<verse eid="PSA 145:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 145:13"/>Your kingdom {is} a kingdom of all of eternities,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your dominion {is} in every generation and generation.
<verse eid="PSA 145:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 145:14"/>Yahweh is supporting all of the ones falling
</para>
  <para style="q2">and raising up all of the ones being bowed down.
<verse eid="PSA 145:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 145:15"/>The eyes of all wait for you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you, you are giving their food to them in its time,
<verse eid="PSA 145:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 145:16"/>opening your hand
</para>
  <para style="q2">and satisfying every living {thing} {with respect to} desire.
<verse eid="PSA 145:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 145:17"/>Yahweh {is} righteous in all of his ways
</para>
  <para style="q2">and faithful in all of his works.
<verse eid="PSA 145:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 145:18"/>Yahweh {is} near to all of the ones calling on him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to all who call on him in truth.
<verse eid="PSA 145:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 145:19"/>He does the desire of the ones fearing him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he hears their cry, and he saves them.
<verse eid="PSA 145:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 145:20"/>Yahweh is keeping all of the ones loving him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he destroys all of the wicked.
<verse eid="PSA 145:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 145:21"/>My mouth will speak the praise of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all flesh will bless the name of his holiness forever and ever.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 145:21"/><verse eid="PSA 145:21"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 145"/>
  <chapter number="146" style="c" sid="PSA 146"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 146:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise Yahweh, my soul!
<verse eid="PSA 146:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 146:2"/>Let me praise Yahweh in my life;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let me make music to my God while I yet {am}.
<verse eid="PSA 146:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 146:3"/>Do not trust in nobles,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the son of man, in whom there is no salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 146:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 146:4"/>His breath goes out, he returns to his ground;
</para>
  <para style="q2">on that day, his thoughts perish.
<verse eid="PSA 146:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 146:5"/>The happinesses of {the one} who {has} the God of Jacob for his help;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his hope {is} in Yahweh his God,
<verse eid="PSA 146:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 146:6"/>the one having made the heavens and the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the sea and all that {is} in them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one keeping faithfulness forever,
<verse eid="PSA 146:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 146:7"/>doing justice for the oppressed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">giving bread to the hungry.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh is releasing the bound ones.
<verse eid="PSA 146:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 146:8"/>Yahweh is opening the blind;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh is raising up the one bowed down;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh is loving the righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 146:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 146:9"/>Yahweh is guarding the sojourners;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he upholds the orphan and the widow,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the way of the wicked, he overturns.
<verse eid="PSA 146:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 146:10"/>Yahweh reigns forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your God, Zion, to generation and generation.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 146:10"/><verse eid="PSA 146:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 146"/>
  <chapter number="147" style="c" sid="PSA 147"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 147:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">For {it is} good to make music {to} our God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for praise {is} pleasant and suitable.
<verse eid="PSA 147:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 147:2"/>Yahweh builds up Jerusalem;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he gathers the scattered of Israel,
<verse eid="PSA 147:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 147:3"/>healing the broken of heart
</para>
  <para style="q2">and binding up their wounds;
<verse eid="PSA 147:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 147:4"/>counting the number of the stars,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he calls names to all of them.
<verse eid="PSA 147:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 147:5"/>Great is our Lord, and abundant of power,
</para>
  <para style="q2">his understanding {is} without number.
<verse eid="PSA 147:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 147:6"/>Yahweh is lifting up the poor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">bringing down the wicked to the ground.
<verse eid="PSA 147:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 147:7"/>Sing to Yahweh with thanksgiving;
</para>
  <para style="q2">make music to our God with the harp,
<verse eid="PSA 147:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 147:8"/>the one covering the heavens with clouds;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one preparing rain for the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one making the mountains sprout with grass.
<verse eid="PSA 147:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 147:9"/>He gives its food to the beast,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the sons of the raven when they call.
<verse eid="PSA 147:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 147:10"/>He does not delight in the strength of a horse;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does not take pleasure {in} the legs of a man.
<verse eid="PSA 147:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 147:11"/>Yahweh takes pleasure {in} the ones fearing him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones hoping for his covenant faithfulness.
<verse eid="PSA 147:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 147:12"/>Extol Yahweh, Jerusalem;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise your God, Zion.
<verse eid="PSA 147:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 147:13"/>For he strengthens the bars of your gates;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he blesses your sons in your midst.
<verse eid="PSA 147:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 147:14"/>The one putting peace {at} your borders,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he satisfies you {with} the fat of wheat.
<verse eid="PSA 147:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 147:15"/>The one sending his command {to} the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">his word runs to swiftness.
<verse eid="PSA 147:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 147:16"/>The one making snow like wool,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he scatters frost like ashes.
<verse eid="PSA 147:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 147:17"/>The one sending his hail like crumbs,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who can stand to the face of his cold?
<verse eid="PSA 147:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 147:18"/>He sends his word, and he makes them melt;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he makes his wind blow, and the waters flow.
<verse eid="PSA 147:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 147:19"/>He declared his word to Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">his statutes and his judgments to Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 147:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 147:20"/>He has not done this for any {other} nation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his judgments, they do not know them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 147:20"/><verse eid="PSA 147:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 147"/>
  <chapter number="148" style="c" sid="PSA 148"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 148:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh from the heavens;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him in the heights.
<verse eid="PSA 148:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 148:2"/>Praise him, all of his angels;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him, all of his armies.
<verse eid="PSA 148:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 148:3"/>Praise him, sun and moon;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him, all of the stars of light.
<verse eid="PSA 148:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 148:4"/>Praise him, heavens of the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the waters that {are} above the heavens.
<verse eid="PSA 148:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 148:5"/>Let them praise the name of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for he, he commanded, and they were created.
<verse eid="PSA 148:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 148:6"/>And he established them forever and ever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he gave a decree, and it will not pass away.
<verse eid="PSA 148:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 148:7"/>Praise Yahweh from the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">sea creatures and all depths,
<verse eid="PSA 148:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 148:8"/>fire and hail, snow and vapor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">wind of tempest, doing his word,
<verse eid="PSA 148:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 148:9"/>mountains and all hills,
</para>
  <para style="q2">tree of fruit and all cedars,
<verse eid="PSA 148:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 148:10"/>the living {creature} and every beast,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the creeper and the bird of wing,
<verse eid="PSA 148:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 148:11"/>kings of the earth and all peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q2">princes and all judges of the earth,
<verse eid="PSA 148:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 148:12"/>young men and also young women,
</para>
  <para style="q2">old men with youths.
<verse eid="PSA 148:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 148:13"/>Let them praise the name of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his name alone is exalted;
</para>
  <para style="q2">his splendor {is} over the earth and the heavens.
<verse eid="PSA 148:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 148:14"/>And he has raised up a horn for his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise for all of his faithful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the sons of Israel, a people near to him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 148:14"/><verse eid="PSA 148:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 148"/>
  <chapter number="149" style="c" sid="PSA 149"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 149:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Sing to Yahweh a new song,
</para>
  <para style="q2">his praise in the assembly of the faithful.
<verse eid="PSA 149:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 149:2"/>Let Israel rejoice in his Maker;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let the sons of Zion be glad in their king.
<verse eid="PSA 149:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 149:3"/>Let them praise his name in the dance;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let them make music to him with the tambourine and the harp.
<verse eid="PSA 149:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 149:4"/>For Yahweh is taking pleasure in his people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he beautifies the humble with salvation.
<verse eid="PSA 149:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 149:5"/>Let the faithful exult in glory;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let them sing joyfully on their beds.
<verse eid="PSA 149:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 149:6"/>{Let} the exaltations of God {be} in their throat,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a sword of mouths in their hand,
<verse eid="PSA 149:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 149:7"/>to execute vengeance on the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">punishments on the peoples,
<verse eid="PSA 149:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 149:8"/>to bind their kings with chains
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their nobles with shackles of iron,
<verse eid="PSA 149:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 149:9"/>to execute on them the judgment written.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It {is} honor to all of his faithful.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 149:9"/><verse eid="PSA 149:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 149"/>
  <chapter number="150" style="c" sid="PSA 150"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 150:1"/>Hallelu Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise God in his sanctuary;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him in the expanse of his strength.
<verse eid="PSA 150:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 150:2"/>Praise him for his mighty deeds;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him according to the abundance of his greatness.
<verse eid="PSA 150:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 150:3"/>Praise him with the blast of a shofar;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him with the lyre and the harp.
<verse eid="PSA 150:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 150:4"/>Praise him with the tambourine and the dance;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him with stringed instruments and the flute.
<verse eid="PSA 150:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 150:5"/>Praise him with cymbals of hearing;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him with cymbals of a shout.
<verse eid="PSA 150:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 150:6"/>Let all of the breath praise Yah!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Hallelu Yah!
<verse eid="PSA 150:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 150"/>
</usx>
